k 1]\n685-- P55A–P55D are accepted concrete-alpha prerequisites. P56 proves finite-word/algebraic identities only: its C*-extension depends on introduced `ProductStateBound` and lacks positivity, so it is not a formal C*-state. [Task 2]\n686:- `bound_beating/formalize_itp/Formalization/InfiniteTensorProductHilbert.lean` contributes an auditable finite-support kernel, finite-mode tensor realization, positivity, sesquilinearity, and `PreInnerProductSpace.Core`; exclude `VacuumRestrictedITPInnerProductAxioms` and completion wrappers from accepted evidence. P56R targets finite-density-matrix-derived boundedness/positivity, P57A a local audited ITP-core port, and P57 waits on both. [Task 2]\n687-- `P48` constructs the decreasing projection tower and strong-limit `q`, retaining `q ∈ M` under explicit lattice/support/representation hypotheses via commutant closedness and `M=(M')'`; it does not prove the analytic double-commutant theorem. Pinned Mathlib has WOT primitives and generic strong convergence, but defines concrete `VonNeumannAlgebra` by double commutant and lacks the analytic SOT/WOT equivalence and Kaplansky density package. [Task 3]\n688-- Preserve the dependency `P49` finite-stage/C*-corner trace → bicommutant/Kaplansky bounded approximation → `P50` faithful normal trace on `qMq` → `P51` finiteness/fullness. The finiteness calculation needs `τ_q(q-vv*)=0`; `q-v*v` is identically zero when `v*v=q`. Initial ready packets were `P47, P48, P52, P54`; recheck live state before relying on that snapshot. [Task 3]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
