{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"printf '%s\\\\n' '--- formalization audit decision ---'; nl -ba work/FORMALIZATION-AUDIT-DECISION.md | sed -n '1,360p'; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- semantic audit ---'; nl -ba work/FORMALIZATION-SEMANTIC-AUDIT.md | sed -n '1,420p'; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- recent handoff/state candidates ---'; rg --files | rg '(\"'^|/)(STATE|PROGRESS|HANDOFF|STATUS)('\"\\\\.|\"'$)|aristotle_autopilot|queue|CLOSEOUT'\"' | sort\"","aggregated_output":"--- formalization audit decision ---\n     1\t# Formalization semantic-audit decision\n     2\t\n     3\tDate: 2026-08-07\n     4\t\n     5\tThe approved deliverable is a semantic audit/tutorial of the Lean\n     6\tformalization, rather than another proof package or a compilation report.\n     7\t\n     8\tThe audit will provide:\n     9\t\n    10\t1. a status summary separating proved mathematics, conditional interfaces,\n    11\t   supplied data, and unformalized claims;\n    12\t2. a dependency map from the manuscript's finite-coordinate argument through\n    13\t   the algebraic limit, concrete C-star model, GNS transport, bicommutant\n    14\t   transport, and product-factor boundary;\n    15\t3. a theorem ledger mapping each important natural-language proof sentence to\n    16\t   exact Lean declarations, hypotheses, intermediate lemmas, and semantic\n    17\t   verdicts; and\n    18\t4. a step-by-step Lean reading sequence with code excerpts and direct build or\n    19\t   `#check` commands.\n    20\t\n    21\tThe audit must keep compilation separate from mathematical validity and must\n    22\tidentify exact manuscript locators from `SOURCE-CONTRACT.md`. In particular,\n    23\tit must not call the regional hyperfinite-factor theorem proved merely because\n    24\tconditional Lean interfaces compile.\n    25\t\n    26\tThe first pass will inventory the current modules and completed-package\n    27\treviews. Later passes will inspect the principal declarations and their proof\n    28\tchains in dependency order.\n--- semantic audit ---\n     1\t# Formalization semantic audit\n     2\t\n     3\tStatus: first inventory in progress.\n     4\t\n     5\tThis document is the approved semantic/tutorial audit described in\n     6\t`FORMALIZATION-AUDIT-DECISION.md`. It is not itself a proof and does not\n     7\tchange the manuscript theorem status.\n     8\t\n     9\t## Audit verdict convention\n    10\t\n    11\t- **proved**: the stated Lean theorem follows from its explicit hypotheses and\n    12\t  compiles without placeholders;\n    13\t- **conditional**: the Lean implication is proved, but one or more hypotheses\n    14\t  are supplied structures or external analytic assumptions;\n    15\t- **infrastructure**: reusable Lean mathematics with no manuscript claim;\n    16\t- **unformalized**: a manuscript step for which no corresponding theorem is\n    17\t  currently present;\n    18\t- **not aligned**: the Lean conclusion is stronger, weaker, or materially\n    19\t  different from the natural-language sentence.\n    20\t\n    21\tCompilation, axiom reports, and mathematical alignment will be recorded\n    22\tseparately.\n    23\t\n    24\t## Source clauses\n    25\t\n    26\tThe manuscript-facing audit uses only the locators recorded in\n    27\t`SOURCE-CONTRACT.md`:\n    28\t\n    29\t- `main.tex:1671-1679`: local symplectic basis and finite-support condition;\n    30\t- `main.tex:1740-1752`: regional factor theorem statement;\n    31\t- `main.tex:1915-1920`: proposed adapted-basis star-isomorphism;\n    32\t- `main.tex:1927-1931`: pure/mixed product density state;\n    33\t- `main.tex:1945-1967`: GNS, tensor, and factor claims;\n    34\t- `main.tex:1970-2004`: quasi-equivalence and normal-folium claims.\n    35\t\n    36\t## Initial module inventory\n    37\t\n    38\tThe detailed theorem ledger and dependency graph are the next sections to be\n    39\tfilled after inspecting the principal declarations. The current theorem\n    40\tcontract itself still says:\n    41\t\n    42\t```lean\n    43\tdef regionalAlgebraTheoremStatus : String :=\n    44\t  \"conditional contract pending analytic model\"\n    45\t```\n    46\t\n    47\tThat status is consistent with the source contract and is not to be upgraded\n    48\twithout discharging the missing finite-coordinate, representation, normality,\n    49\tand product-classification premises.\n    50\t\n    51\t## First-pass verdict\n    52\t\n    53\tThe current formalization is a sequence of conditional bridges, not yet a\n    54\tformal proof of the manuscript's regional factor theorem. The strongest\n    55\tcurrently checked route is:\n    56\t\n    57\t```text\n    58\tfinite adapted-coordinate data\n    59\t  -> finite StarAlgEquiv at each stage\n    60\t  -> coherent algebraic direct-limit StarAlgEquiv alpha\n    61\t  -> compatible algebraic state transport\n    62\t  -> supplied compatible operator representation\n    63\t  -> closed operator-range C*-algebra\n    64\t  -> supplied state-preserving C*-extension\n    65\t  -> GNS unitary and algebraic bicommutant transport\n    66\t  -> conditional product-factor/type classification\n    67\t```\n    68\t\n    69\tThe arrows are not all existence theorems. In particular, the source-specific\n    70\tfinite coordinate realization, a faithful representation of the algebraic\n    71\tlimit, the regional C*-extension, the analytic normality/WOT statements, and\n    72\tthe product-factor classification remain explicit premises or missing\n    73\tmathematics.\n    74\t\n    75\t## Status table for the reviewed overnight packages\n    76\t\n    77\t| Package | Principal Lean object | Semantic verdict | Main external premise |\n    78\t|---|---|---|---|\n    79\t| P37 | `algebraicLimitOperatorRep` | conditional theorem proved | compatible finite-stage operator representations |\n    80\t| P38 | `quasilocalCStarAlgebra` | conditional theorem proved | supplied compatible representation; stage injectivity for faithfulness |\n    81\t| P39 | `StatePreservingData`, `gnsUnitary` | conditional theorem proved | C*-completion, alpha extension, state identity and continuity |\n    82\t| P40 | `bicommutantStarEquiv`, folium transport | algebraic part proved; analytic part conditional | WOT/double-commutant and normal-functional characterizations |\n    83\t| P41 | `ProductGNSFactorization` | partial boundary only | supplied factorization/classification; infinite weight interface is incomplete |\n    84\t| P42--P46 | no reviewed candidate currently present | not yet audited | candidate/archive status must be established before use |\n    85\t\n    86\tAll five reviewed packages compile in the local project. Their closeout\n    87\treviews explicitly separate compilation from mathematical scope. P41 is\n    88\taccepted only as partial: its infinite-pure `TracialWeightCore` does not yet\n    89\tassert positivity, normality, faithfulness, or semifiniteness.\n    90\t\n    91\t## Dependency spine and one-to-one theorem anchors\n    92\t\n    93\t### 1. Finite coordinate map\n    94\t\n    95\tNatural-language sentence:\n    96\t\n    97\t> Given finite adapted source and target word bases, send each source word to a\n    98\t> phase-corrected target word.\n    99\t\n   100\tLean anchor:\n   101\t\n   102\t```lean\n   103\tFiniteAdaptedCoordinateStarData.starEquiv\n   104\tFiniteAdaptedCoordinateStarData.starEquiv_word\n   105\tFiniteAdaptedCoordinateStarData.starEquiv_correctedWord\n   106\t```\n   107\t\n   108\tSemantic status: the construction is proved from the fields of\n   109\t`FiniteAdaptedCoordinateStarData`, but the actual manuscript-specific finite\n   110\tdata are not constructed from `main.tex:1671-1679` or `main.tex:1915-1920`.\n   111\t\n   112\t### 2. Coherence of finite maps\n   113\t\n   114\tNatural-language sentence:\n   115\t\n   116\t> The finite coordinate maps commute with the inclusions of stages.\n   117\t\n   118\tLean anchor:\n   119\t\n   120\t```lean\n   121\tstarEquiv_connecting_of_pauliBasis\n   122\tDirectedFiniteCoordinateFamily.stageEquiv_connecting\n   123\t```\n   124\t\n   125\tSemantic status: proved when word, label, phase, and connecting-map\n   126\tcompatibility are supplied.\n   127\t\n   128\t### 3. Algebraic infinite map\n   129\t\n   130\tNatural-language sentence:\n   131\t\n   132\t> Compatible finite maps descend to a unique star-isomorphism of algebraic\n   133\t> direct limits.\n   134\t\n   135\tLean anchor:\n   136\t\n   137\t```lean\n   138\tDirectedFiniteCoordinateFamily.alpha\n   139\tDirectedFiniteCoordinateFamily.alpha_of\n   140\tDirectedFiniteCoordinateFamily.existsUnique_alpha\n   141\t```\n   142\t\n   143\tSemantic status: this is a genuine algebraic direct-limit theorem, conditional\n   144\ton the finite coherent family. It is not yet a C*-completion theorem.\n   145\t\n   146\t### 4. State transport\n   147\t\n   148\tNatural-language sentence:\n   149\t\n   150\t> Pull the target product state back along the algebraic alpha.\n   151\t\n   152\tLean anchor:\n   153\t\n   154\t```lean\n   155\tTargetStageStates.targetLimitState\n   156\tTargetStageStates.pulledBackState\n   157\tTargetStageStates.pulledBackState_eq_targetLimitState_alpha\n   158\tTargetStageStates.pulledBackState_isAlgebraicState\n   159\t```\n   160\t\n   161\tSemantic status: the state-level implication is proved from compatible target\n   162\tstage states. The infinite product density operator itself is not constructed\n   163\tas a von Neumann-algebraic state in this module.\n   164\t\n   165\t### 5. Algebraic operator representation\n   166\t\n   167\tNatural-language sentence:\n   168\t\n   169\t> Compatible finite-stage operator representations define a representation of\n   170\t> the quasi-local algebra.\n   171\t\n   172\tLean anchor:\n   173\t\n   174\t```lean\n   175\talgebraicLimitOperatorRep\n   176\talgebraicLimitOperatorRep_of\n   177\talgebraicLimitOperatorRep_stage_congr\n   178\talgebraicLimitOperatorRep_injective\n   179\t```\n   180\t\n   181\tSemantic status: proved conditionally. Injectivity requires stagewise\n   182\tinjectivity; no infinite tensor-product Hilbert space is constructed.\n   183\t\n   184\t### 6. Concrete C*-model\n   185\t\n   186\tNatural-language sentence:\n   187\t\n   188\t> Complete the quasi-local algebra in the operator norm.\n   189\t\n   190\tLean anchor:\n   191\t\n   192\t```lean\n   193\tOperatorRepresentation.rangeClosure\n   194\tOperatorRepresentation.embedding\n   195\tOperatorRepresentation.denseRange_embedding\n   196\t```\n   197\t\n   198\tand, for the direct-limit range,\n   199\t\n   200\t```lean\n   201\tquasilocalCStarAlgebra\n   202\tquasilocalEmbedding\n   203\tdenseRange_quasilocalEmbedding\n   204\t```\n   205\t\n   206\tSemantic status: the closure is genuinely constructed inside bounded\n   207\toperators, but only after an isometric operator representation is supplied.\n   208\tThis does not prove that the manuscript's algebra has such a representation.\n   209\t\n   210\t### 7. State-preserving GNS transport\n   211\t\n   212\tNatural-language sentence:\n   213\t\n   214\t> A state-preserving C*-isomorphism induces a canonical GNS unitary.\n   215\t\n   216\tLean anchor:\n   217\t\n   218\t```lean\n   219\tStatePreservingData.sourceState_eq_pullback\n   220\tStatePreservingData.gnsUnitary\n   221\tStatePreservingData.gnsUnitary_intertwines\n   222\tStatePreservingData.gnsConjStarAlgEquiv\n   223\t```\n   224\t\n   225\tSemantic status: proved from supplied C*-completions, state positivity/order\n   226\tdata, continuity, and an exact state identity. It is not a proof of the\n   227\tmanuscript's state identity.\n   228\t\n   229\t### 8. Bicommutant transport\n   230\t\n   231\tNatural-language sentence:\n   232\t\n   233\t> The GNS unitary identifies the represented von Neumann algebras.\n   234\t\n   235\tLean anchors:\n   236\t\n   237\t```lean\n   238\tStarSubalgebra.vonNeumannGenerated\n   239\tStarSubalgebra.le_vonNeumannGenerated\n   240\tStarSubalgebra.vonNeumannGenerated_le\n   241\tbicommutantStarEquiv_sourceRepVN\n   242\t```\n   243\t\n   244\tSemantic status: the algebraic bicommutant/conjugation statement is proved.\n   245\tThe identification with strong/weak operator closure and the normal-folium\n   246\tstep are conditional interfaces, not proved analytic theorems.\n   247\t\n   248\t### 9. Product-factor and trace conclusion\n   249\t\n   250\tNatural-language sentence:\n   251\t\n   252\t> The product GNS algebra is a type-I pure factor tensor a finite type-I or\n   253\t> hyperfinite type-II1 mixed factor, with the appropriate trace conclusion.\n   254\t\n   255\tLean anchors:\n   256\t\n   257\t```lean cddddddddssssssssssssssssssssssssssw1\n   258\tProductGNSFactorization.pureFactor_typeI_of_finite\n   259\tProductGNSFactorization.pureFactor_typeIInfinity_of_infinite\n   260\tProductGNSFactorization.mixedFactor_typeI_of_finite\n   261\tProductGNSFactorization.mixedFactor_hyperfiniteII1_of_infinite\n   262\tfinitePureSector_product_classification\n   263\tinfinitePureSector_product_classification\n   264\t```\n   265\t\n   266\tSemantic status: the type labels and tensor identification are supplied data.\n   267\tThe finite algebraic trace transport is proved. The infinite-pure package does\n   268\tnot yet provide a faithful normal semifinite weight, so the corrected\n   269\tinfinite-sector trace conclusion is not formalized.\n--- recent handoff/state candidates ---\nPROGRESS.md\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"printf '%s\\\\n' '--- P57 closeout ---'; nl -ba reviews/P57-product-gns-tensor-factorization-closeout.md | sed -n '1,360p'; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- P58 closeout ---'; nl -ba reviews/P58-mixed-uhf-hyperfinite-factor-closeout.md | sed -n '1,400p'; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- P56R closeout ---'; nl -ba reviews/P56R-regional-cstar-product-state-closeout.md | sed -n '1,320p'; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- P57A closeout ---'; nl -ba reviews/P57A-vacuum-restricted-itp-core-closeout.md | sed -n '1,320p'\"","aggregated_output":"--- P57 closeout ---\n     1\t# P57 closeout review — product GNS tensor factorization\n     2\t\n     3\t## Decision\n     4\t\n     5\t**Status: proved at the packet's stated conditional Lane-H scope; queue may\n     6\tadvance.**\n     7\t\n     8\tRelative to the complete manuscript theorem, this is intentionally **partial**:\n     9\tthe module does not prove the pure or mixed factor classifications, factorhood,\n    10\tnormal/spatial tensor-product theory beyond its concrete bicommutant definition,\n    11\tor the final trace/weight conclusions.\n    12\t\n    13\tThe exact supervisor-supplied archive\n    14\t`aristotle_responses/P57-product-gns-tensor-factorization-a7accfb8-36471af9.tar.gz`\n    15\thas SHA-256\n    16\t`27aa2166368ee5ded0dc2f5ea2573811bb4b6be623c54f53da69b71a14ecdeed`.  It was\n    17\textracted only into\n    18\t`aristotle_responses/P57-product-gns-tensor-factorization-a7accfb8-36471af9-quarantine/`.\n    19\tNo build, dependency update, or dependency fetch was run in that quarantine\n    20\tsnapshot.  Only the packet-authorized candidate\n    21\t`AristotleCandidates/ProductGNSTensorFactorization.lean` was integrated into\n    22\tthe live project.  Its live SHA-256 matches the quarantined candidate exactly:\n    23\t\n    24\t```text\n    25\t6e4549050881ec26557bbf243095ae549de03ce6a8628ad4bf4724e2d3478b07\n    26\t```\n    27\t\n    28\tThe archive, quarantine extraction, and this review are retained as raw\n    29\tresponse records.  No manuscript file was changed.\n    30\t\n    31\t## Source and exact scope\n    32\t\n    33\tThe packet's manuscript source basis is `main.tex:1945-1985`.  Lines\n    34\t`1945-1953` state the product-state GNS splitting target\n    35\t`\\mathcal H_{\\widetilde\\omega}=\\mathcal K\\otimes\\mathcal K'`; lines\n    36\t`1954-1967` contain the later factor/type classification, which is outside P57;\n    37\tand lines `1968-1981` describe the separate identification with the regional\n    38\tGNS representation and its quasi-equivalence problem.  The candidate therefore\n    39\tformalizes the P57 GNS/spatial-identification gate only, not the later\n    40\tclassification or source-specific quasi-equivalence theorem.\n    41\t\n    42\t## Exact assumptions and declarations\n    43\t\n    44\tThe central declaration is\n    45\t`AristotleCandidates.ProductGNSTensor.ProductGNSData`.  Its explicit fields\n    46\tare:\n    47\t\n    48\t- C-star structures and order structures for `Pure`, `Mixed`, and `Total`;\n    49\t- unital star-algebra embeddings `pureEmb : Pure →⋆ₐ[ℂ] Total` and\n    50\t  `mixedEmb : Mixed →⋆ₐ[ℂ] Total`;\n    51\t- positive linear functionals `pureState`, `mixedState`, and `totalState`;\n    52\t- elementwise commutation of the two embeddings;\n    53\t- the product identity\n    54\t  `totalState (pureEmb a * mixedEmb b) = pureState a * mixedState b`;\n    55\t- the contractivity premise `state_norm_le`; and\n    56\t- norm-density of the complex linear span of elementary products,\n    57\t  `span_dense`.\n    58\t\n    59\tThe GNS construction uses positive functionals, so normalized-state fields are\n    60\tnot needed for these declarations.  Reading the data specifically as states\n    61\trequires the usual supplied normalization; no normalization is silently used\n    62\tto prove a later trace or factor statement.  The algebraic tensor product and\n    63\tits completion are constructed in the module.  No completed infinite tensor\n    64\tproduct, spatial von Neumann tensor-product API, normal extension, or closure\n    65\tpremise is supplied as an axiom or interface.\n    66\t\n    67\tThe load-bearing declarations are:\n    68\t\n    69\t- `prodElt`, `prodElt_mul`, `prodElt_star_mul`, and\n    70\t  `preInner_prodElt`, giving the elementary product algebra and its GNS inner\n    71\t  product factorization;\n    72\t- `prodCLM`, `inner_prodCLM`, `TensorPre`, `TensorGNS`,\n    73\t  `tensorLiftₗ`, `inner_tensorLiftₗ`, and `norm_tensorLiftₗ`, constructing the\n    74\t  algebraic tensor map and its isometry;\n    75\t- `tensorUnitaryCLM`, `denseRange_tensorUnitaryCLM`,\n    76\t  `surjective_tensorUnitaryCLM`, and\n    77\t  `productGNSUnitary`, constructing the canonical GNS unitary;\n    78\t- `prodCLM_intertwine` and `tensorUnitaryCLM_tensorOpC`, proving the dense\n    79\t  finite-word intertwining and its continuous extension;\n    80\t- `unitaryConj_tensorOpC`, transporting elementary tensor operators to the\n    81\t  total GNS representation;\n    82\t- `commute_totalRep_of_commute_prodElt` and\n    83\t  `centralizer_representedProductSet`, proving that elementary products and\n    84\t  the full represented total algebra have the same commutant;\n    85\t- `unitaryConj_image_bicommutant_elementaryTensorSet`, transporting the\n    86\t  generated bicommutant through the GNS unitary;\n    87\t- `pureFactorSet`, `mixedFactorSet`, `spatialTensorAlgebra`,\n    88\t  `tensorOpC_split`, `tensorOpC_commute`, and\n    89\t  `bicommutant_elementary_eq_spatial`; and\n    90\t- `unitaryConj_image_spatialTensorAlgebra`, the final concrete equality with\n    91\t  `(Set.range totalRep).centralizer.centralizer`.\n    92\t\n    93\t`spatialTensorAlgebra` is explicitly defined as the bicommutant of the two\n    94\tcommuting represented factor families.  This is a project-local concrete set\n    95\tdefinition, not an imported standard spatial von Neumann tensor-product\n    96\tconstruction.  The candidate documents that pinned Mathlib still lacks the\n    97\tstandard tensor-product algebra, commutation, slice-map, and normal-product\n    98\textension API.  The included `trivialProductGNSData` witness only proves that\n    99\tthe data structure is non-vacuous; it is not a classification or regional\n   100\tapplication theorem.\n   101\t\n   102\t## Acceptance classification\n   103\t\n   104\t| Classification | Result |\n   105\t| --- | --- |\n   106\t| proved | The conditional product-data theorem constructs the GNS tensor-product unitary, proves the finite-word and continuous intertwining identities, and identifies the represented total bicommutant with the concrete bicommutant-defined spatial algebra. |\n   107\t| partial | The result remains generic over `ProductGNSData`; it does not itself instantiate that bundle from the manuscript's regional algebra and P55D/P56R data. Standard spatial von Neumann tensor-product theory and all later factor/type/trace conclusions remain open. |\n   108\t| blocked | Nothing blocks the packet's permitted strongest-local-form gate. The stronger standard spatial-von-Neumann API is unavailable in pinned Mathlib and is explicitly recorded rather than assumed. |\n   109\t| failed | None. No compilation, placeholder, archive-integrity, or scope failure was found. |\n   110\t\n   111\tThe packet's mathematical target is therefore met at its stated conditional\n   112\tscope.  It is not a proof of the complete manuscript claim\n   113\t`\\pi_{\\widetilde\\omega}(\\mathcal P_I)''=\\mathcal B(\\mathcal K)\\bar\\otimes\\mathcal R`:\n   114\tthe classification of the two factors and the source-specific regional\n   115\tidentification are downstream work.\n   116\t\n   117\t## Changed proof route\n   118\t\n   119\tThe candidate takes a constructive route through the algebraic tensor product\n   120\t`PureGNS ⊗[ℂ] MixedGNS`, then completes the norm-preserving tensor lift.  It\n   121\tderives boundedness of elementary tensor operators from the proved\n   122\tintertwining identity and the isometry, rather than assuming a general\n   123\toperator-tensor norm inequality unavailable in the pinned API.  It defines the\n   124\tstrongest available concrete spatial object as a bicommutant of the two\n   125\tcommuting factor families.  These are alternative proof choices within the\n   126\tpacket's scope, not silent weakenings; every added premise is a named field of\n   127\t`ProductGNSData` above.\n   128\t\n   129\t## Plan alignment\n   130\t\n   131\t- **Package and lane:** `P57`; Lane `H`, correct.\n   132\t- **Integrated predecessors:** `P54`, `P56R`, and `P57A`, each locally\n   133\t  integrated, compiled, and accepted in its closeout review.  The preserved\n   134\t  partial `P56` artifact is not used as a predecessor.  The additional GNS and\n   135\t  bicommutant imports are already-built local infrastructure.\n   136\t- **Permitted gate:** construct the pure/mixed product GNS Hilbert-space split,\n   137\t  prove the dense/continuous intertwining identity, and identify the generated\n   138\t  represented algebra with the strongest concrete spatial tensor object\n   139\t  supported by pinned Mathlib.  This gate is discharged conditionally on the\n   140\t  explicitly declared `ProductGNSData` fields.\n   141\t- **Forbidden downstream claims:** respected.  The candidate does not claim\n   142\t  mixed-factor classification, factorhood of either factor, regional\n   143\t  factorhood, `\\mathcal B(\\mathcal K)` identification, hyperfiniteness, or any\n   144\t  trace/weight dichotomy.\n   145\t\n   146\t## Verification\n   147\t\n   148\t- `lake build AristotleCandidates.ProductGNSTensorFactorization` — passed\n   149\t  (`8072/8072` jobs).\n   150\t- `lake build AristotleCandidates.UHFReferenceRepresentation AristotleCandidates.RegionalProductStateIdentity AristotleCandidates.VacuumRestrictedInfiniteTensorProduct AristotleCandidates.GNSCommutantConjugation AristotleCandidates.BicommutantVonNeumannCore AristotleCandidates.VonNeumannBicommutantTheorem AristotleCandidates.ProductGNSTensorFactorization Formalization` — passed (`8100` jobs).\n   151\t- `lake build` — passed (`0` jobs; live project already up to date).\n   152\t- `#print axioms` for `productGNSUnitary`, `prodCLM_intertwine`,\n   153\t  `unitaryConj_image_bicommutant_elementaryTensorSet`,\n   154\t  `bicommutant_elementary_eq_spatial`, and\n   155\t  `unitaryConj_image_spatialTensorAlgebra` — each reports only\n   156\t  `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`.\n   157\t- A declaration-level scan of the candidate and direct imports found no\n   158\t  `axiom`, `sorry`, `admit`, `opaque`, `unsafe`, `implemented_by`, or\n   159\t  `native_decide` declarations.  Textual mentions in explanatory comments\n   160\t  were not treated as declarations.\n   161\t- `git diff --check` and live/quarantine SHA-256 comparison — passed.\n   162\t\n   163\t## Adversarial review\n   164\t\n   165\tArtifact types touched: Lean code, mathematical formalization, and workflow\n   166\tcloseout metadata.  No acceptance-blocking finding was found.  The review\n   167\tchecked that the candidate is the packet-authorized file, that its explicit\n   168\tfields account for density and product-state assumptions, that completion and\n   169\tspatial objects are constructed at the available scope, that no downstream\n   170\tfactor/trace claim is smuggled in, and that no unrelated dirty work was\n   171\toverwritten.  Compilation and axiom checks validate the Lean declarations only;\n   172\tthey do not validate the manuscript's missing regional coordinate construction,\n   173\tnormal/quasi-equivalence argument, or factor classification.\n   174\t\n   175\t## Cleanup and worktree state\n   176\t\n   177\tThe pre-existing modified plan, packet, decision, and queue files, together\n   178\twith all earlier candidates and reviews, were preserved.  The new integrated\n   179\tcandidate, exact archive, quarantine extraction, and this closeout review are\n   180\tkept intentionally.  The live `.lake/build` cache produced/used by the Lean\n   181\tchecks is also retained under the existing project build tree.  No commit,\n   182\tpush, dependency update, manuscript edit, or archive build was performed.\n--- P58 closeout ---\n     1\t# P58 closeout review — mixed UHF factor classification\n     2\t\n     3\t## Decision\n     4\t\n     5\t**Status: proved at the stated mixed-sector, conditional Lane-H scope; queue may\n     6\tadvance.**\n     7\t\n     8\tAristotle task `ed55ef94-0313-4123-9cc0-b00ffdb465aa` was downloaded as\n     9\t`aristotle_responses/P58-mixed-uhf-hyperfinite-factor.tar.gz` (SHA-256\n    10\t`6a9c6e453986cbacfed106b03db592f946fd61c13acb976a9b9da8f4c3c7c7b5`) and\n    11\textracted without building, updating, or fetching dependencies at\n    12\t`aristotle_responses/P58-quarantine/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p58-3px4hkyb_aristotle/`.\n    13\tOnly the packet-authorized module\n    14\t`AristotleCandidates/MixedUHFHyperfiniteFactor.lean` was integrated into the\n    15\tlive project. Its quarantine and live SHA-256 values agree:\n    16\t`5dbf9ff8c35035c94b37804435793102cb0c59f88c7a39e2746c32274fc67d20`.\n    17\tThe archive and extraction remain raw response records. No manuscript file was\n    18\tchanged.\n    19\t\n    20\t## Source and exact declarations\n    21\t\n    22\tThe source basis is the narrow claim in `main.tex:1945-1967`, specifically the\n    23\tfinite maximally-mixed matrix alternative and the infinite maximally-mixed\n    24\thyperfinite-II1 assertion at lines 1964-1966. This packet formalizes only the\n    25\tproject-local dyadic mixed sector; it neither establishes the preceding GNS\n    26\ttensor splitting nor transports its result to the manuscript's regional algebra.\n    27\t\n    28\tThe new module's load-bearing declarations are:\n    29\t\n    30\t- `qubitMatrixStarEquiv` (line 197) and\n    31\t  `qubitTensorTrace_eq_normalizedTrace` (line 213), identifying the `n`-qubit\n    32\t  algebra with `M_(2^n)(C)` and its trace with normalized matrix trace;\n    33\t- `qubitTensorPower_isMixedMatrixFactor` (line 291), whose explicit fields are\n    34\t  the star equivalence, positivity of `2^n`, normalized-trace identity,\n    35\t  traciality, faithfulness, and algebraic scalar centre;\n    36\t- `qubitUHF_hasScalarCenter` (line 314) and\n    37\t  `qubitUHF_not_matrixAlgebra` (line 331), the algebraic infinite-limit\n    38\t  statements;\n    39\t- `uhfConcreteCStar_isMatricialChain` (line 410), an increasing dense chain of\n    40\t  finite matrix subalgebras in the P54 concrete C-star model;\n    41\t- `matrixRange_vonNeumannGenerated_trivialCenter` (line 683) and\n    42\t  `mixedStage_vonNeumannGenerated_trivialCenter` (line 725), direct\n    43\t  matrix-unit proofs of trivial centre for each finite-stage generated concrete\n    44\t  von Neumann algebra;\n    45\t- `mixedVonNeumann` (line 739), defined as the von Neumann algebra generated\n    46\t  by `UHFConcreteCStar`; and\n    47\t- the conditional `mixedVonNeumann_isHyperfiniteFiniteFactor` (line 840).\n    48\t\n    49\tThe last theorem uses exactly the three fields of\n    50\t`MixedWeakClosurePremises` (lines 798-811): traciality of `uhfVectorState` on\n    51\tthe weak closure, faithfulness there, and `HasTrivialOperatorCenter` of that\n    52\tweak closure. `IsHyperfiniteFiniteFactorModel` (line 814) is explicitly a\n    53\tproject-local feature predicate: factorhood, a vector-normal faithful tracial\n    54\tstate, a matricial chain, and unbounded matrix sizes. It is **not** a proof of\n    55\tthe Murray-von Neumann/Connes uniqueness/classification theorem for the\n    56\thyperfinite II1 factor.\n    57\t\n    58\t## Acceptance review\n    59\t\n    60\t| Classification | Result |\n    61\t| --- | --- |\n    62\t| proved | The finite mixed stage is star-isomorphic to `M_(2^n)(C)` with normalized faithful tracial functional and scalar centre. The algebraic UHF limit has scalar centre and is not a finite matrix algebra. In the P54 representation, finite matrix stages form a monotone dense C-star-level chain; each individual stage's generated von Neumann algebra has trivial centre by the local matrix-unit proof. The conditional theorem assembles the stated project-local finite-factor model. |\n    63\t| partial | Infinite weak-closure traciality, faithfulness, and factorhood are not proved; they are the three named fields above. The module's `IsVectorNormal` is a project-local single-vector-functional predicate, not a formalized Mathlib sigma-weak continuity theory. No canonical hyperfinite-II1 classification/isomorphism is formalized. |\n    64\t| blocked | Nothing blocks P58's stated gate, because the packet expressly permits an analytic factoriality/classification bridge only as an explicit conditional interface. Those analytic premises remain open for any later use. |\n    65\t| failed | None. |\n    66\t\n    67\tThe packet's mathematical target is met at its stated scope. The alternate\n    68\troute is a direct finite-matrix/matrix-unit construction plus a C-star-level\n    69\tmatricial approximation, rather than an unproved weak-closure transfer. It\n    70\tadds exactly the three `MixedWeakClosurePremises`; it does not silently weaken\n    71\tthe finite result or promote the conditional infinite result to a theorem of\n    72\tthe manuscript.\n    73\t\n    74\t## Plan alignment\n    75\t\n    76\t- **Package and lane:** P58, Lane H — correct.\n    77\t- **Predecessors:** P54 is integrated, compiled, and audited in\n    78\t  `reviews/P54-uhf-reference-representation-closeout.md`. The imports\n    79\t  `Formalization.DyadicTensorTower`, P54's\n    80\t  `UHFReferenceRepresentation`, and the pre-existing local bicommutant core\n    81\t  are byte-identical between the quarantine snapshot and live checkout. The\n    82\t  bicommutant core is supporting infrastructure, not an undeclared later Lane-H\n    83\t  package dependency.\n    84\t- **Permitted gate:** discharged: the finite mixed matrix alternative is\n    85\t  proved, and the infinite alternative supplies a checked matrix approximation\n    86\t  with all weak-closure/factor/classification gaps isolated as named premises.\n    87\t- **Forbidden downstream claims:** respected. The candidate contains no\n    88\t  regional alpha transport, pure-sector classification, spatial product\n    89\t  factorhood, regional factor claim, or final trace/weight theorem. Its\n    90\t  finite-stage factor statements and conditional mixed weak-closure model are\n    91\t  confined to the P54 dyadic reference representation.\n    92\t\n    93\t## Verification\n    94\t\n    95\t- `lake build AristotleCandidates.MixedUHFHyperfiniteFactor` — passed (8038\n    96\t  jobs) in the live project.\n    97\t- `lake build AristotleCandidates.UHFReferenceRepresentation AristotleCandidates.BicommutantVonNeumannCore AristotleCandidates.MixedUHFHyperfiniteFactor Formalization` — passed (8089 jobs) in the live project.\n    98\t- `lake build` — passed in the live project; no work was required after the\n    99\t  focused build.\n   100\t- `lake env lean -o .lake/build/lib/lean/AristotleCandidates/MixedUHFHyperfiniteFactor.olean AristotleCandidates/MixedUHFHyperfiniteFactor.lean` — passed in the live project, producing the importable cache used by the axiom check.\n   101\t- `#print axioms` for `qubitTensorPower_isMixedMatrixFactor`,\n   102\t  `qubitUHF_hasScalarCenter`, `qubitUHF_not_matrixAlgebra`,\n   103\t  `uhfConcreteCStar_isMatricialChain`,\n   104\t  `matrixRange_vonNeumannGenerated_trivialCenter`,\n   105\t  `mixedStage_vonNeumannGenerated_trivialCenter`,\n   106\t  `uhfVectorState_isVectorNormal`, and\n   107\t  `mixedVonNeumann_isHyperfiniteFiniteFactor` — each reports only\n   108\t  `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`.\n   109\t- Forbidden-declaration scan of the candidate and its three direct imports —\n   110\t  no `sorry`, `admit`, user `axiom`, `opaque`, `unsafe`,\n   111\t  `implemented_by`, or `native_decide` occurrence.\n   112\t- Direct-import SHA-256 comparisons, candidate quarantine/live SHA-256\n   113\t  comparison, and `git diff --check` — passed.\n   114\t\n   115\t## Adversarial review\n   116\t\n   117\tNo acceptance-blocking finding. The review checked the finite normalization\n   118\tagainst the actual recursive matrix equivalence; that the algebraic scalar-\n   119\tcentre proof first reduces an arbitrary limit element to a finite stage; that\n   120\tthe non-matrix result uses a finite-rank obstruction rather than a mere label;\n   121\tand that the matrix-unit proof establishes only trivial centre for each finite\n   122\tgenerated algebra. It also checked that `mixedVonNeumann` factorhood,\n   123\tfaithfulness, and traciality remain three separate explicit premises, and that\n   124\tthe project-local `IsHyperfiniteFiniteFactorModel` is not reported as a\n   125\thyperfinite-II1 uniqueness theorem. Lean builds and axiom reports validate the\n   126\tformal statements, not the manuscript's unformalized GNS tensor splitting or\n   127\tthe open analytic closure bridge.\n   128\t\n   129\t## Cleanup and worktree state\n   130\t\n   131\tKept intentionally: the P58 candidate, this closeout review, its raw archive,\n   132\tquarantine extraction, and the generated `.olean` under the existing\n   133\t`.lake/build/` cache. All previously untracked P49/P49A/P49B/P53 candidates\n   134\tand reviews remain untouched. No commit, push, dependency update, archive\n   135\tbuild, fetch, or manuscript modification was performed.\n--- P56R closeout ---\n     1\t# P56R closeout review — recovered regional C-star product state\n     2\t\n     3\t## Decision\n     4\t\n     5\t**Status: proved at the stated conditional Lane-H scope; queue may advance.**\n     6\t\n     7\tAristotle project `026bfc92-1158-49a3-9049-ca7588e54dbb`, task\n     8\t`91db2acf-a167-41cd-bebd-ef882f843c64`, is terminal `COMPLETE` in\n     9\t`history/logs/20260810T080459Z-026bfc92-tasks.log`.\n    10\tThe supervisor-supplied archive\n    11\t`aristotle_responses/P56R-regional-cstar-product-state-026bfc92-91db2acf.tar.gz`\n    12\thas SHA-256\n    13\t`09c401cad7ea05da5257575b5a4a019bed4fdb802833e3a95e2e70f14f75ba1a`.\n    14\tIt was extracted only into\n    15\t`aristotle_responses/P56R-regional-cstar-product-state-026bfc92-91db2acf-quarantine/`;\n    16\tno Lean build, dependency update, or dependency fetch ran there.  The only\n    17\tpacket-owned source integrated into the live project was\n    18\t`AristotleCandidates/RegionalProductStateIdentity.lean`.  Its live SHA-256\n    19\tmatches the quarantined candidate exactly:\n    20\t\n    21\t```text\n    22\ta2a4cbcc0aabdf90da9de9b75d15a60bc6c8dff7c5f12a5d7f5a56f2a76b5f00\n    23\t```\n    24\t\n    25\tNo manuscript, P55D predecessor, unrelated candidate, or unrelated dirty file\n    26\twas modified.  The older P56 material remains in the same candidate as a\n    27\tpreserved partial artifact; it is not evidence for the P56R acceptance.\n    28\t\n    29\t## Exact P56R declarations and assumptions\n    30\t\n    31\tThe recovery section adds the following proved declarations:\n    32\t\n    33\t- `AlphaData.norm_stageProductState_le`: the finite-stage product functional\n    34\t  is norm-decreasing for the finite matrix C-star norm.\n    35\t- `AlphaData.stageProductState_positive`: every finite-stage value on\n    36\t  `star x * x` is a nonnegative real.\n    37\t- `AlphaData.sourceProductState_positive` and\n    38\t  `AlphaData.sourceProductState_isAlgebraicState`: positivity and unitality\n    39\t  on the algebraic direct limit.\n    40\t- `AlphaData.norm_sourceEmbedding_sourceOf` and\n    41\t  `SourceConcreteRep.norm_sourceProductState_le`: the stage and direct-limit\n    42\t  estimates transported through the faithful isometric P55C embedding.\n    43\t- `SourceConcreteRep.cstarProductStateRecovered`, together with\n    44\t  `cstarProductStateRecovered_sourceEmbedding`,\n    45\t  `cstarProductStateRecovered_one`,\n    46\t  `cstarProductStateRecovered_positive`,\n    47\t  `cstarProductStateRecovered_isAlgebraicState`, and\n    48\t  `norm_cstarProductStateRecovered_le_one`: the continuous source C-star\n    49\t  functional, its dense formula, unitality, positivity on every square, local\n    50\t  state predicate, and norm bound.\n    51\t- `SourceConcreteRep.cstarRegionalStateRecovered`, together with\n    52\t  `cstarRegionalStateRecovered_targetEmbedding`,\n    53\t  `cstarRegionalStateRecovered_one`,\n    54\t  `cstarRegionalStateRecovered_positive`, and\n    55\t  `cstarRegionalStateRecovered_isAlgebraicState`: the transported regional\n    56\t  functional and its corresponding properties.\n    57\t- `SourceConcreteRep.cstarRegionalStateRecovered_cstarAlpha` and\n    58\t  `cstarRegionalStateRecovered_comp_cstarAlpha`: the required exact\n    59\t  alpha-transport identity.\n    60\t\n    61\tP56R adds no auxiliary premise.  It takes an `A : AlphaData L I` and an\n    62\t`R : A.SourceConcreteRep`, hence inherits only the already explicit P53/P55D\n    63\tconditional infrastructure: the P52 local-hyperbolic family and lattice\n    64\texhaustion, `[LinearOrder I]`, and the named `AlphaData.symplectic` and\n    65\t`AlphaData.stage_surjective` assumptions, together with the constructed\n    66\tP55C finite/infinite concrete representation branch and the checked finite\n    67\tpure/mixed one-qubit data.  No `ProductStateBound`, supplied positivity,\n    68\tsupplied state, supplied completion, or new axiom is used by any recovery\n    69\tdeclaration.\n    70\t\n    71\tThe local predicate is the existing project predicate\n    72\t`StabilizerHyperfinite.IsAlgebraicState`: unitality plus positivity on\n    73\t`star x * x`.  All fields are proved; no standard von Neumann normality claim\n    74\tis being smuggled into this predicate.\n    75\t\n    76\t## Changed proof route\n    77\t\n    78\tP56R replaces the old conditional `ProductStateBound` route with a proved\n    79\tfinite-dimensional density-matrix route.  It constructs the allowed-stage\n    80\tdensity matrix\n    81\t`D = ∑ v ∈ allowedStage, pauliMat v`, proves `D† = D`, `D² = |G| D`, and\n    82\tcomputes its trace.  A column decomposition of `tr (D x D)` proves both the\n    83\tfinite-stage norm estimate and positivity.  The estimate transports through\n    84\tthe injective star homomorphism into the P55C concrete C-star model, after\n    85\twhich a proved dense continuous extension supplies the source functional and\n    86\ttransport through `cstarAlpha.symm` supplies the regional functional.\n    87\t\n    88\tThis is an alternative proof route, not a weakened target: it adds no premise\n    89\tand does not reuse the preserved §8 `ProductStateBound` declarations in the\n    90\tP56R recovery results.\n    91\t\n    92\t## Acceptance classification\n    93\t\n    94\t| Classification | Result |\n    95\t| --- | --- |\n    96\t| proved | The complete P56R gate is proved: finite-stage norm/positivity, algebraic state, continuous source C-star state, transported regional state, and exact alpha identity. |\n    97\t| partial | Relative to the manuscript theorem, the result remains conditional on P55D’s explicit coordinate and concrete-model data. The manuscript source does not itself construct those hypotheses. |\n    98\t| blocked | None at the P56R gate. GNS tensor splitting, spatial von Neumann tensor products, factorhood, and trace/weight classification remain later packages and were not attempted. |\n    99\t| failed | None. No compilation, placeholder, archive-integrity, or scope failure was found. |\n   100\t\n   101\tThe packet’s mathematical target is therefore met at its stated scope.  It is\n   102\tnot a claim that the full manuscript theorem is established.\n   103\t\n   104\t## Plan alignment\n   105\t\n   106\t- **Package and lane:** `P56R`, Lane `H`; correct.\n   107\t- **Predecessors:** `P55D` is integrated, live-compiled, and semantically\n   108\t  audited in `reviews/P55D-regional-concrete-cstar-alpha-closeout.md`.  The\n   109\t  original `P56` is explicitly retained as a partial artifact and was not\n   110\t  treated as a predecessor.\n   111\t- **Permitted gate:** discharged exactly: construct the pure/mixed product\n   112\t  C-star state and prove its equality with the regional state transported by\n   113\t  the exact P55D C-star `alpha`.\n   114\t- **Forbidden claims:** respected.  No GNS tensor splitting, von Neumann\n   115\t  spatial tensor product, factorhood, center/trivial-center theorem, or\n   116\t  trace/weight classification occurs in the recovery section.\n   117\t\n   118\tThe source basis in the packet is `main.tex:1921-1946`, matching the\n   119\tmanuscript’s proposed state construction and finite-word identity.  The\n   120\tmanuscript-facing geometric coordinate/model hypotheses remain external\n   121\tconditional infrastructure, as required by `AGENTS.md` and\n   122\t`SOURCE-CONTRACT.md`.\n   123\t\n   124\t## Verification\n   125\t\n   126\t- `lake build AristotleCandidates.RegionalProductStateIdentity` — passed\n   127\t  (`8096/8096` jobs).\n   128\t- `lake build AristotleCandidates.RegionalProductStateIdentity Formalization`\n   129\t  — passed (`8096/8096` jobs).\n   130\t- `lake build` — passed; the full live project was up to date.\n   131\t- `#print axioms` for all load-bearing recovery declarations listed above —\n   132\t  each reports only `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`.\n   133\t- Placeholder scan of the candidate and direct P55D/finite-pure-mixed imports\n   134\t  — no `sorry`, `admit`, user `axiom`, `opaque`, `unsafe`,\n   135\t  `implemented_by`, or `native_decide` occurrence.\n   136\t- Recovery-section scan — no forbidden downstream terms or declarations.\n   137\t- Live/quarantine candidate hash comparison and `git diff --check` — passed.\n   138\t- The exact archive was inspected and extracted without building inside the\n   139\t  dependency-free quarantine snapshot.\n   140\t\n   141\t## Adversarial review\n   142\t\n   143\tNo acceptance-blocking finding.  The review checked that the finite estimate\n   144\tdoes not divide by zero (`allowedStage` contains zero and the source label\n   145\ttype is nonempty), that positivity is proved first on finite matrix squares\n   146\tand then extended by closedness from the dense algebraic image, and that the\n   147\tregional positivity proof uses only the already constructed C-star\n   148\tequivalence.  It also checked that the old `ProductStateBound` occurs only in\n   149\tthe preserved partial §8 material and explanatory text, not as an argument of\n   150\tthe recovery declarations.  Compilation and axiom reports validate the Lean\n   151\tproof artifacts; they do not prove the inherited P53/P55D geometric premises\n   152\tor any later operator-algebraic classification.\n   153\t\n   154\t## Cleanup and worktree state\n   155\t\n   156\tKept intentionally: the exact archive, its quarantine extraction, the\n   157\tintegrated P56R candidate, and this closeout review.  Existing modified\n   158\t`PLAN.md`, packet/decision files, earlier candidates, and earlier reviews were\n   159\tpreserved.  No commit, push, manuscript edit, archive build, dependency update,\n   160\tor dependency fetch was performed.\n--- P57A closeout ---\n     1\t# P57A closeout review — vacuum-restricted infinite-tensor pre-Hilbert core\n     2\t\n     3\t## Decision\n     4\t\n     5\t**Status: proved at the stated shared-infrastructure scope; queue may advance.**\n     6\t\n     7\tAristotle task `563e769a-0e9b-4395-9895-e03c81c26851` was downloaded as\n     8\t`aristotle_responses/P57A-vacuum-restricted-itp-core-205100d0-563e769a.tar.gz`\n     9\tand extracted, without a build, dependency update, or fetch, only under\n    10\t`aristotle_responses/P57A-vacuum-restricted-itp-core-205100d0-563e769a-quarantine/`.\n    11\tOnly the packet-authorized module\n    12\t`AristotleCandidates/VacuumRestrictedInfiniteTensorProduct.lean` was\n    13\tintegrated into the live project.  The raw archive and quarantine extraction\n    14\tremain intact response records.  No manuscript file was changed.\n    15\t\n    16\tThe quarantined response incorrectly said that the nominated local source\n    17\t`<original-home>/Projects/current/bound_beating/formalize_itp/Formalization/InfiniteTensorProductHilbert.lean`\n    18\twas absent.  It is present.  Local comparison confirms that the integrated\n    19\tmodule independently re-expresses the source's proved finite-support core,\n    20\tbut with a finite-Gram-coordinate proof route rather than importing the other\n    21\tproject.  I corrected that provenance comment in the live integrated module;\n    22\tthis changes documentation only.  The candidate and quarantine SHA-256 values\n    23\ttherefore differ:\n    24\t\n    25\t- live: `c4936227e370cd0d04c32f4d62807003ed688afba9ca661a330c696a5c75feca`;\n    26\t- quarantined response: `ee8862347e606cc8ac629e3baa8909354ad288da9a4f5502c8639fa595633c52`.\n    27\t\n    28\t## Source, assumptions, and exact declarations\n    29\t\n    30\tThis is **infrastructure only**, not a manuscript-facing assertion.  The\n    31\tcandidate imports only `Mathlib`; it does not import the `bound_beating`\n    32\tproject or any other package result.\n    33\t\n    34\tAll generic results use only the packet-authorized assumptions\n    35\t`[DecidableEq ι]`, `[∀ i, NormedAddCommGroup (E i)]`, and\n    36\t`[∀ i, InnerProductSpace ℂ (E i)]`.  The normalization premise\n    37\t\n    38\t```lean\n    39\thΩ : ∀ i, ⟪Ω i, Ω i⟫_ℂ = 1\n    40\t```\n    41\t\n    42\tis used exactly where padding a product outside active support, positivity,\n    43\tfinite-mode kernel realization, finite-mode evaluation, and the exported\n    44\tpre-inner-product core require it.  No completion, density, positivity, or\n    45\texternal analytical premise was added.\n    46\t\n    47\tThe load-bearing live declarations are:\n    48\t\n    49\t- `exists_gram_coords` (lines 64--77), finite coordinates for every finite\n    50\t  Gram matrix;\n    51\t- `exists_finiteMode_realization` (88--104) and\n    52\t  `sum_prod_inner_nonneg` (109--122), realizing the product kernel as a\n    53\t  norm square in a finite coordinate tensor model;\n    54\t- `VacuumTensor` (128--134), `kern` (153--154), and\n    55\t  `kern_eq_prod_of_subset` (158--164), defining the finite-support\n    56\t  elementary tensors and support-independent kernel;\n    57\t- `itpInner` (183--184), `conj_itpInner_symm` (220--231),\n    58\t  `itpInner_add_left` (234--247), and `itpInner_smul_left` (250--262),\n    59\t  the algebraic sesquilinear extension;\n    60\t- `itpInner_nonneg` (266--285), positivity for an arbitrary finite linear\n    61\t  combination, and `re_itpInner_nonneg` (288--291);\n    62\t- `itpCore` (295--301), the exported\n    63\t  `PreInnerProductSpace.Core ℂ (ITPSpan Ω)`;\n    64\t- `vacuumVector` and `itpInner_vacuumVector` (309--322), whose\n    65\t  norm-square is one; and\n    66\t- `exists_finiteMode_realization_kern` (329--341) and\n    67\t  `itpInner_eq_finiteMode` (344--352), the finite-mode statements for the\n    68\t  actual vacuum-restricted kernel and algebraic span.\n    69\t\n    70\t## Acceptance review\n    71\t\n    72\t| Classification | Result |\n    73\t| --- | --- |\n    74\t| proved | The finite-support elementary tensors, their finite-product kernel, the free finite span, sesquilinearity, finite-mode realization, positivity on arbitrary finite sums, the pre-inner-product core, and the algebraic vacuum norm-square-one theorem are all explicit proved declarations. |\n    75\t| p