{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"printf '%s\\\\n' '--- source P57 imports/header ---'; sed -n '1,160p' AristotleCandidates/ProductGNSTensorFactorization.lean; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- source P58 imports/header ---'; sed -n '1,150p' AristotleCandidates/MixedUHFHyperfiniteFactor.lean; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- module target mapping ---'; sed -n '1,220p' lakefile.lean; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- existing generated olean state ---'; find .lake/build/lib/lean/AristotleCandidates -maxdepth 1 -type f -name '*ProductGNS*' -o -name '*MixedUHF*' -printf '%f\\\\n' 2>/dev/null | sort\"","aggregated_output":"--- source P57 imports/header ---\nimport Mathlib\nimport AristotleCandidates.UHFReferenceRepresentation\nimport AristotleCandidates.RegionalProductStateIdentity\nimport AristotleCandidates.VacuumRestrictedInfiniteTensorProduct\nimport AristotleCandidates.GNSCommutantConjugation\nimport AristotleCandidates.BicommutantVonNeumannCore\nimport AristotleCandidates.VonNeumannBicommutantTheorem\n\n/-!\n# P57 — product GNS tensor factorization\n\n**Context declaration.**  Source basis: `main.tex:1945-1985`.  Package `P57`, Lane `H`.\nPredecessors `P54` (`UHFReferenceRepresentation`), `P56R` (`RegionalProductStateIdentity`) and\n`P57A` (`VacuumRestrictedInfiniteTensorProduct`), together with the checked GNS/bicommutant\ntransport modules `GNSCommutantConjugation`, `BicommutantVonNeumannCore` and\n`VonNeumannBicommutantTheorem`, are imported.\n\nThe manuscript step formalized here is the passage\n\n* `H_ω̃ = K ⊗ K'` (the GNS Hilbert space of a product state splits as a Hilbert tensor product of\n  the GNS spaces of the two factor states), and\n* `π_ω̃(P_I)'' = (represented pure factor) ⊗̄ (represented mixed factor)` (the represented regional\n  algebra is the spatial tensor product of the two represented factor algebras).\n\n## Data and auxiliary assumptions\n\nEverything is developed for the explicit bundle `ProductGNSData`, whose fields list *all*\nauxiliary premises used anywhere in this file:\n\n* two unital `⋆`-homomorphisms `pureEmb : Pure →⋆ₐ[ℂ] Total` and `mixedEmb : Mixed →⋆ₐ[ℂ] Total`\n  of C⋆-algebras;\n* positive linear functionals `pureState`, `mixedState`, `totalState`;\n* `commuting` — the two embedded factors commute elementwise;\n* `product` — `totalState (ι₁ a · ι₂ b) = pureState a · mixedState b`;\n* `state_norm_le` — `totalState` is norm-decreasing (automatic for a state on a unital\n  C⋆-algebra, but assumed here as an explicit premise rather than re-derived);\n* `span_dense` — the linear span of the elementary products `ι₁ a · ι₂ b` is norm dense in\n  `Total`.\n\nNo further hypothesis, interface, axiom, or completion assumption is introduced anywhere: there\nare **no** `axiom`, `sorry`, `opaque`, `unsafe` or `implemented_by` declarations in this file, and\nno supplied (unproved) spatial von Neumann closure facts.\n\n## Classification of the results\n\n**(1) Checked infrastructure constructed in this packet.**\n\n* `clmExtend`, `extendOfBound`, `coeCLM`, `norm_clmExtend_le` — extension of bounded maps to\n  completions (needed because `LinearMap.mkContinuous` does not elaborate directly out of\n  `PositiveLinearMap.PreGNS` into operator-valued codomains).\n* `prodElt`, `prodElt_mul`, `prodElt_star_mul`, `totalState_prodElt_inner`, `preInner_prodElt`,\n  `norm_prodElt` — the algebra of elementary product elements and the factorization of the GNS\n  inner product on them.\n* `prodCLM`, `inner_prodCLM` — the bilinear product map `K_pure × K_mixed → H_ω̃`, with the\n  exact inner-product factorization `⟪x ⊗ y, x' ⊗ y'⟫ = ⟪x, x'⟫ ⟪y, y'⟫`.\n* `tensorLiftₗ`, `norm_tensorLiftₗ`, `tensorLiftIsometry`, `tensorUnitaryCLM` — the induced\n  isometry of the algebraic tensor product `TensorPre = K_pure ⊗[ℂ] K_mixed` and of its\n  completion `TensorGNS`.\n* `totalCoe`, `denseRange_tensorUnitaryCLM`, `surjective_tensorUnitaryCLM`.\n* `tensorMapₗ`, `norm_tensorMapₗ_le`, `tensorOp`, `tensorOpC` — the elementary tensor operators\n  `π₁(a) ⊗ π₂(b)`; their boundedness is *derived* from the intertwining identity and the\n  isometry property, since pinned Mathlib has no general bound `‖T ⊗ S‖ ≤ ‖T‖ ‖S‖` on an\n  algebraic tensor product of inner-product spaces.\n\n**(2) Theorems recovered in the manuscript's intended form (for `ProductGNSData`).**\n\n* `productGNSUnitary : TensorGNS ≃ₗᵢ[ℂ] TotalGNS` — the canonical GNS unitary\n  `K_pure ⊗ K_mixed ≅ H_ω̃`; this is the manuscript's `H_ω̃ = K ⊗ K'`.\n* `prodCLM_intertwine_coe` (intertwining on the dense subspace of classes of algebra elements,\n  i.e. on finite words) and `prodCLM_intertwine`, `tensorUnitaryCLM_tensorOpC` (intertwining\n  everywhere, by continuity).\n* `unitaryConj_tensorOpC` — conjugation by the unitary maps `π₁(a) ⊗ π₂(b)` to\n  `π_ω̃(ι₁ a · ι₂ b)`.\n* `centralizer_representedProductSet` — the elementary product operators and the whole\n  represented algebra have the same commutant.\n* `bicommutant_elementary_eq_spatial` — the bicommutant of the elementary tensor operators equals\n  `spatialTensorAlgebra`, the spatial von Neumann tensor product of the two represented factor\n  algebras, defined as usual as `({π₁(a) ⊗ 1} ∪ {1 ⊗ π₂(b)})''`.\n* `unitaryConj_image_spatialTensorAlgebra` — the manuscript's algebra identification:\n  `U (M_pure ⊗̄ M_mixed) U⋆ = π_ω̃(Total)''`.\n\n* `idPositive`, `trivialProductGNSData` and the resulting `Nonempty ProductGNSData` instance — a\n  non-vacuity witness showing that the fields of `ProductGNSData` are jointly satisfiable (the\n  witness is the trivial one on `ℂ`; it only certifies non-vacuity of the hypotheses).\n\n**(3) Conditional statements.**  None beyond the explicit fields of `ProductGNSData` listed\nabove; in particular the density premise `span_dense` and the contractivity premise\n`state_norm_le` are used and are stated as fields.\n\n**(4) Source / Mathlib obstructions still open.**\n\n* Pinned Mathlib has no von Neumann *spatial tensor product* `M ⊗̄ N` of two von Neumann algebras\n  acting on Hilbert spaces `H`, `K`: there is no `VonNeumannAlgebra` tensor construction, no\n  commutation theorem `(M ⊗̄ N)' = M' ⊗̄ N'`, and no `(M ⊗ 1)' = M' ⊗̄ B(K)`.  We therefore *define*\n  the spatial tensor product concretely as the bicommutant\n  `({π₁(a) ⊗ 1} ∪ {1 ⊗ π₂(b)})''` (`spatialTensorAlgebra`), which is the standard definition, and\n  prove the identification for it.  What is *not* available is the further theory of that object\n  (commutation theorem, slice maps, normal product extensions).\n* Pinned Mathlib has no bound `‖T ⊗ S‖ ≤ ‖T‖ ‖S‖` for general bounded `T`, `S` on the algebraic\n  tensor product of inner-product spaces (only `TensorProduct.mapIsometry` for isometries).  The\n  boundedness needed here is obtained instead from the constructed intertwining identity.\n* Pinned Mathlib has no inner product on `PiTensorProduct`, so an *infinite* tensor product of\n  Hilbert spaces has to be built by hand; that is why the split here is stated for a two-factor\n  product state, exactly as the manuscript's `K ⊗ K'`.\n\n**Forbidden downstream claims are not made.**  Nothing here asserts that either factor is a\nfactor, no mixed-factor classification, no regional factorhood, and no trace or weight dichotomy;\n`B(K)` is never claimed to be the represented pure factor (that would need irreducibility of the\npure-state representation, which is not part of this packet).\n-/\n\nset_option maxHeartbeats 1000000\nset_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000\n\nopen scoped InnerProductSpace ComplexOrder TensorProduct\nopen UniformSpace\n\nnamespace AristotleCandidates\nnamespace ProductGNSTensor\n\nuniverse u\n\n/-! ## 0. Two pieces of completion infrastructure -/\n\nsection Completions\n\nvariable {X Y : Type*} [SeminormedAddCommGroup X] [NormedSpace ℂ X]\n    [NormedAddCommGroup Y] [NormedSpace ℂ Y] [CompleteSpace Y]\n\n/-- Extension of a continuous linear map to the completion of its domain, when the codomain is\nalready complete. -/\nnoncomputable def clmExtend (f : X →L[ℂ] Y) : Completion X →L[ℂ] Y where\n  toFun := Completion.extension f\n  map_add' x y := by\n    induction x, y using Completion.induction_on₂ with\n    | hp =>\n      exact isClosed_eq (Completion.continuous_extension.comp continuous_add)\n        (Continuous.add (Completion.continuous_extension.comp continuous_fst)\n          (Completion.continuous_extension.comp continuous_snd))\n    | ih a b =>\n      rw [← Completion.coe_add, Completion.extension_coe f.uniformContinuous,\n        Completion.extension_coe f.uniformContinuous, Completion.extension_coe f.uniformContinuous,\n        map_add]\n  map_smul' c x := by\n    induction x using Completion.induction_on with\n    | hp =>\n      exact isClosed_eq (Completion.continuous_extension.comp (continuous_const_smul c))\n        ((continuous_const_smul (c : ℂ)).comp Completion.continuous_extension)\n    | ih a =>\n      rw [← Completion.coe_smul, Completion.extension_coe f.uniformContinuous,\n        Completion.extension_coe f.uniformContinuous, RingHom.id_apply, f.map_smul]\n  cont := Completion.continuous_extension\n\n@[simp] theorem clmExtend_coe (f : X →L[ℂ] Y) (a : X) : clmExtend f (a : Completion X) = f a :=\n  Completion.extension_coe f.uniformContinuous a\n\n/-- The canonical inclusion of a seminormed complex vector space into its completion, as a\ncontinuous linear map. -/\nnoncomputable def coeCLM (X : Type*) [SeminormedAddCommGroup X] [NormedSpace ℂ X] :\n    X →L[ℂ] Completion X where\n--- source P58 imports/header ---\nimport Formalization.DyadicTensorTower\nimport AristotleCandidates.UHFReferenceRepresentation\nimport AristotleCandidates.BicommutantVonNeumannCore\n\n/-!\n# The mixed dyadic subsystem: matrix factors, matricial approximation, and the\n# conditional hyperfinite-II₁ interface\n\n**Context declaration.** *Source basis:* `main.tex:1945-1967` (the sentence\n\"If we have infinitely many maximally entangled pieces, then `R` is the\nhyperfinite type II₁ factor, otherwise it is again a finite matrix algebra of\ntype I_k\").  Everything below is stated for the **mixed sector alone**, in the\n*project-local* dyadic model of `Formalization.DyadicTensorTower` and its\nreference representation `AristotleCandidates.UHFReferenceRepresentation`\n(package P54).\n\n## Scope\n\nThe mixed (maximally mixed / maximally entangled) coordinates of the manuscript's\nproduct state are modelled by the dyadic tower: `k` mixed qubits give the finite\nstage `QubitTensorPower k` with its *normalized* trace `qubitTensorTrace k`, and\ninfinitely many mixed qubits give the algebraic UHF limit `QubitUHFAlgebra` with\nthe normalized trace `qubitUHFTrace`, represented faithfully on the trace-GNS\nHilbert space `UHFGNS` by `uhfRep`.\n\nThis file proves, in this order:\n\n1. **Matrix identification (finite mixed case).**  `qubitMatrixStarEquiv n` is a\n   `*`-isomorphism `QubitTensorPower n ≃⋆ₐ[ℂ] Matrix (Fin (2^n)) (Fin (2^n)) ℂ`\n   under which `qubitTensorTrace n` is exactly the normalized matrix trace\n   (`qubitTensorTrace_eq_normalizedTrace`).  Hence the finite mixed subsystem is\n   a **matrix factor with normalized trace**\n   (`qubitTensorPower_isMixedMatrixFactor`): trivial centre, tracial, faithful,\n   normalized.\n2. **Algebraic statements for the infinite mixed subsystem.**  The algebraic UHF\n   limit has trivial centre (`qubitUHF_hasScalarCenter`), carries a normalized\n   faithful tracial functional, and is *not* finite dimensional\n   (`qubitUHF_not_finiteDimensional`), so it is not a matrix algebra.\n3. **Matricial (hyperfinite) approximation in the reference representation.**\n   The increasing chain `mixedStage n := (uhfStageRep n).range` of finite\n   `*`-subalgebras of `B(UHFGNS)` consists of `2^n × 2^n` matrix algebras\n   (`mixedStage_matrixEquiv`), is monotone (`mixedStage_mono`), and its union is\n   dense in the concrete C*-algebra `UHFConcreteCStar`\n   (`uhfConcreteCStar_isMatricialChain`).\n4. **Factorhood of each finite stage as a concrete von Neumann algebra.**  A\n   *proved*, unconditional theorem: for **any** injective unital `*`-representation\n   of a full matrix algebra on a Hilbert space, the von Neumann algebra it\n   generates has trivial centre (`matrixRange_vonNeumannGenerated_trivialCenter`).\n   Applied to `mixedStage n` this gives\n   `mixedStage_vonNeumannGenerated_trivialCenter`: each finite mixed stage\n   generates a type-I_{2^n} **factor** on the GNS space.  No double commutant\n   theorem and no Kaplansky density is used or assumed for this.\n5. **The conditional infinite-mixed interface.**  For the weak closure\n   `mixedVonNeumann := vonNeumannGenerated UHFConcreteCStar` the vector\n   functional `uhfVectorState` of the GNS cyclic vector is proved to be a\n   *normal* (single-vector, hence σ-weakly continuous) state which restricts to\n   the canonical trace on the represented algebraic limit.  Traciality and\n   faithfulness of this state *on the weak closure*, and factoriality of the\n   weak closure, are **not** proved here: they are collected in the explicitly\n   named premise structure `MixedWeakClosurePremises`.  Under those premises,\n   `mixedVonNeumann_isHyperfiniteFiniteFactor` proves that `mixedVonNeumann`\n   satisfies the project-local predicate `IsHyperfiniteFiniteFactorModel`:\n   a factor, with a normal faithful tracial state, generated by an increasing\n   chain of finite matrix subalgebras, and containing matrix subalgebras of\n   unbounded size (hence not of finite type I).\n\n## What is *not* claimed\n\n* No identification of the manuscript's `R` with *the* hyperfinite II₁ factor of\n  Murray–von Neumann/Connes uniqueness: `IsHyperfiniteFiniteFactorModel` is a\n  project-local list of the four checked/assumed features, not the classification\n  theorem.  Uniqueness of the hyperfinite II₁ factor is not formalized.\n* No regional algebra, no transport along any `alpha`, no pure sector, no\n  spatial tensor product, and no final trace/weight theorem.\n* The double commutant theorem is not assumed anywhere; item 4 is proved\n  directly, and item 5 uses only the explicitly listed premises.\n\n## Auxiliary assumptions\n\nThe only assumptions in the file are the three fields of\n`MixedWeakClosurePremises` (traciality on the weak closure, faithfulness on the\nweak closure, factoriality of the weak closure), used exclusively in\n`mixedVonNeumann_isHyperfiniteFiniteFactor` and its corollaries.  Everything else\nis unconditional.\n-/\n\nnamespace StabilizerHyperfinite\n\nset_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 1000000\nset_option maxHeartbeats 1000000\n\nopen scoped ComplexOrder InnerProductSpace\nopen Matrix Complex\n\n/-! ## 0. Project-local definitions -/\n\nsection Definitions\n\n/-- **Project-local definition (trivial algebraic centre).**  A complex\n`*`-algebra `A` *has scalar centre* when every element commuting with all of `A`\nis a scalar multiple of the unit.  This is the algebraic form of \"`A` is a\nfactor\". -/\ndef HasScalarCenter (A : Type*) [Semiring A] [Algebra ℂ A] : Prop :=\n  ∀ x : A, (∀ y : A, x * y = y * x) → ∃ c : ℂ, x = algebraMap ℂ A c\n\n/-- **Project-local definition (faithful functional).** -/\ndef IsFaithfulOn {A : Type*} [Semiring A] [StarRing A] [Algebra ℂ A] (tau : A →ₗ[ℂ] ℂ) : Prop :=\n  ∀ x : A, tau (star x * x) = 0 → x = 0\n\n/-- **Project-local definition (finite mixed matrix factor).**  The data\nwitnessing that a complex `*`-algebra `A` with functional `tau` is a `k × k`\nmatrix factor whose functional is the normalized matrix trace. -/\nstructure IsMixedMatrixFactor (A : Type*) [Semiring A] [StarRing A] [Algebra ℂ A]\n    (k : ℕ) (tau : A →ₗ[ℂ] ℂ) where\n  /-- the identification with a full matrix algebra -/\n  equiv : A ≃⋆ₐ[ℂ] Matrix (Fin k) (Fin k) ℂ\n  /-- `k` is positive -/\n  pos : 0 < k\n  /-- the functional is the *normalized* matrix trace -/\n  trace_eq : ∀ x : A, tau x = (k : ℂ)⁻¹ * Matrix.trace (equiv x)\n  /-- the functional is a normalized algebraic tracial state -/\n  tracial : IsAlgebraicTracialState tau\n  /-- the functional is faithful -/\n  faithful : IsFaithfulOn tau\n  /-- the algebra is a factor -/\n  center : HasScalarCenter A\n\nend Definitions\n\n/-! ## 1. Matrix identification of the finite mixed stages -/\n\nsection MatrixIdentification\n\n/-- A `*`-isomorphism regarded as a `*`-homomorphism. -/\ndef starAlgHomOfStarAlgEquiv {A B : Type*} [Semiring A] [Semiring B] [Algebra ℂ A] [Algebra ℂ B]\n    [Star A] [Star B] (e : A ≃⋆ₐ[ℂ] B) : A →⋆ₐ[ℂ] B :=\n  { e.toAlgEquiv.toAlgHom with map_star' := e.map_star' }\n\n@[simp] theorem starAlgHomOfStarAlgEquiv_apply {A B : Type*} [Semiring A] [Semiring B]\n    [Algebra ℂ A] [Algebra ℂ B] [Star A] [Star B] (e : A ≃⋆ₐ[ℂ] B) (x : A) :\n    starAlgHomOfStarAlgEquiv e x = e x := rfl\n\n/-- Entrywise application of a `*`-isomorphism of coefficient algebras. -/\nnoncomputable def mapMatrixStarEquiv {A B : Type*} [Semiring A] [Semiring B]\n    [Algebra ℂ A] [Algebra ℂ B] [StarRing A] [StarRing B]\n    (m : Type*) [Fintype m] [DecidableEq m] (e : A ≃⋆ₐ[ℂ] B) :\n    Matrix m m A ≃⋆ₐ[ℂ] Matrix m m B :=\n  StarAlgEquiv.ofAlgEquiv (AlgEquiv.mapMatrix e.toAlgEquiv) (by\n    intro x; ext i j\n    simp [Matrix.star_apply, AlgEquiv.mapMatrix, map_star])\n--- module target mapping ---\nimport Lake\nopen Lake DSL\n\npackage «stabilizerHyperfiniteFormalization» where\n\nrequire mathlib from git\n  \"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4.git\" @ \"v4.28.0\"\n\nlean_lib Formalization where\n\nlean_lib AristotleCandidates where\n--- existing generated olean state ---\nMixedUHFHyperfiniteFactor.ilean\nMixedUHFHyperfiniteFactor.ilean.hash\nMixedUHFHyperfiniteFactor.olean\nMixedUHFHyperfiniteFactor.olean.hash\nMixedUHFHyperfiniteFactor.trace\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
