{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"printf '%s\\\\n' '--- source contract relevant locators ---'; nl -ba SOURCE-CONTRACT.md | sed -n '1,260p'; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- context ledger ---'; nl -ba CONTEXT-LEDGER.md | sed -n '1,340p'\"","aggregated_output":"--- source contract relevant locators ---\n     1\t# Manuscript source contract\n     2\t\n     3\t## Authoritative source\n     4\t\n     5\t- Manuscript: `sources/manuscript/main.tex`\n     6\t- Title in source: *Infinite Magic and the Continuum* (`main.tex:117`)\n     7\t- Formalization policy: `AGENTS.md`\n     8\t\n     9\tThis project does not treat its own Lean files, prior agent prompts, or the\n    10\tsurrounding repository as mathematical source authority.\n    11\t\n    12\t## Source clauses in scope\n    13\t\n    14\t| Source locator | What the manuscript says | Formalization status |\n    15\t| --- | --- | --- |\n    16\t| `main.tex:1671-1679` | Defines short-range order through a local symplectic basis, with `W_Gamma = span{z_i : i in P}` and finite support. | Requires a precise Lean model of the infinite Pauli/symplectic data. |\n    17\t| `main.tex:1740-1752` | States the short-range regional-algebra theorem, with an asserted factorization `A_Gamma` into a pure-sector type-I factor and a core factor that is finite type I or hyperfinite `II_1`. | Target statement; not established by current Lean artifacts. |\n    18\t| `main.tex:1915-1920` | Proposes an adapted symplectic basis and a star-isomorphism from an infinite Pauli algebra to `A_Gamma`. | External assumption/gap until the source construction is formalized. |\n    19\t| `main.tex:1927-1931` | Writes a pure/mixed product density state. | Finite density-matrix fragments are formalized; the infinite model is not. |\n    20\t| `main.tex:1945-1967` | Proposes the GNS/tensor-factor and type conclusions. | Conditional GNS transport is formalized; analytic product and type conclusions are not. |\n    21\t| `main.tex:1970-2004` | Proposes quasi-equivalence and normal-folium transport. | Not formalized. |\n    22\t\n    23\tThe wording above is a locator-oriented paraphrase, not a replacement for the\n    24\tmanuscript.\n    25\t\n    26\t## Permitted auxiliary assumptions\n    27\t\n    28\tAny manuscript-facing Lean theorem that needs one of the following must expose\n    29\tit in the theorem statement or task packet:\n    30\t\n    31\t1. a completed C-star or von Neumann algebra model for the infinite Pauli\n    32\t   system and its regional algebra;\n    33\t2. the asserted star-isomorphism from that model to the regional algebra;\n    34\t3. the product-state formula and hypotheses making the GNS representation a\n    35\t   spatial tensor product;\n    36\t4. the von Neumann closure, normality, and quasi-equivalence assumptions needed\n    37\t   to transport the claimed factor type; and\n    38\t5. any hyperfiniteness or trace theorem used for the core factor.\n    39\t\n    40\tNone of these assumptions is supplied merely by the phrase “short-range\n    41\torder” in the current manuscript source.\n    42\t\n    43\t## Trace correction\n    44\t\n    45\tThe manuscript-facing target must distinguish two cases:\n    46\t\n    47\t- if the pure-sector Hilbert space is finite-dimensional, a normalized tracial\n    48\t  state can be obtained from the finite matrix trace together with the core\n    49\t  trace;\n    50\t- if the pure-sector Hilbert space is infinite-dimensional, the appropriate\n    51\t  conclusion is a faithful normal semifinite trace/weight on the `II_infinity`\n    52\t  target, not a tracial state.\n    53\t\n    54\tThis is a correction to the intended theorem contract, not a claim that the\n    55\tcurrent manuscript already states or proves the corrected dichotomy.\n    56\t\n    57\t## Legacy firewall\n    58\t\n    59\tEarlier gLU/refinement/layer-coherence material is listed in\n    60\t`CONTEXT-LEDGER.md`. It is retained, but it is neither a source clause nor an\n    61\timplicit assumption of this formalization.\n--- context ledger ---\n     1\t# Context ledger\n     2\t\n     3\t## Legacy exploratory material: not manuscript authority\n     4\t\n     5\tThe following artifacts contain gLU, refinement, or layer-coherence language\n     6\timported from broader repository history rather than from the manuscript named\n     7\tin `SOURCE-CONTRACT.md`:\n     8\t\n     9\t- `blueprints/002-aristotle-parallel-formalization.tex`;\n    10\t- `aristotle_tasks/P6-layered-direct-limit.md`;\n    11\t- `AristotleCandidates/LayeredDirectLimit.lean`;\n    12\t- `AristotleCandidates/RegionalWitness.lean`; and\n    13\t- `Formalization/CoherentPhaseQubitState.lean`.\n    14\t\n    15\tThey are preserved unchanged as useful exploratory or infrastructure work.\n    16\tThey may be cited only by a future task explicitly marked `Infrastructure\n    17\tonly`; they cannot establish a manuscript-derived hypothesis or conclusion.\n    18\t\n    19\t## Interpretation rule\n    20\t\n    21\tWhen an older document conflicts with `AGENTS.md` or `SOURCE-CONTRACT.md`, the\n    22\tnew manuscript-only policy governs all future task packets and reports. No\n    23\thistorical label retroactively changes the source basis of a checked Lean\n    24\ttheorem.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
