{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"snapshot_root='aristotle_responses/P59-local-hyperbolic-factor-trace-theorem-a12190c2-9efd5c22-quarantine/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p59-80nvzu02_aristotle'\ncandidate=\\\"\"'$snapshot_root/AristotleCandidates/LocalHyperbolicFactorTraceTheorem.lean\"\nnl -ba \"$candidate\" | sed -n '\"'1,460p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"snapshot_root='aristotle_responses/P59-local-hyperbolic-factor-trace-theorem-a12190c2-9efd5c22-quarantine/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p59-80nvzu02_aristotle'\ncandidate=\\\"\"'$snapshot_root/AristotleCandidates/LocalHyperbolicFactorTraceTheorem.lean\"\nnl -ba \"$candidate\" | sed -n '\"'1,460p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\timport AristotleCandidates.ProductGNSTensorFactorization\n     2\timport AristotleCandidates.MixedUHFHyperfiniteFactor\n     3\t\n     4\t/-!\n     5\t# P59 — local-hyperbolic factor and trace theorem\n     6\t\n     7\t**Context declaration.** Source basis: `main.tex:1671-1679, 1970-2004`.\n     8\tPackage `P59`, Lane `H`.  Predecessors `P57` (`ProductGNSTensorFactorization`)\n     9\tand `P58` (`MixedUHFHyperfiniteFactor`) are imported.\n    10\t\n    11\tThis module transports the P57 spatial product model to the regional\n    12\trepresented algebra, proves the factor (trivial-centre) conclusion from\n    13\texplicitly named commutation premises, and separates the finite-pure tracial\n    14\t**state** from the infinite-pure faithful normal semifinite **weight**.\n    15\t\n    16\t## Results, by status\n    17\t\n    18\t**(a) Checked infrastructure (no premise).**\n    19\t\n    20\t* Sections 1–2: the two commuting amplification `⋆`-homomorphisms\n    21\t  `lampHom : B(K₁) →⋆ₐ[ℂ] B(K₁ ⊗̂ K₂)` and `rampHom : B(K₂) →⋆ₐ[ℂ] B(K₁ ⊗̂ K₂)`, including the\n    22\t  operator norm bounds `norm_lmapₗ_le`, `norm_rmapₗ_le` (pinned Mathlib has no Hilbert-space\n    23\t  operator tensor product), injectivity, and the centre/transport lemmas\n    24\t  `hasTrivialCenterSet_bicommutant`, `HasTrivialCenterSet.image`, `restrictStarAlgEquiv`.\n    25\t* Section 3: `tensorOpC_eq_amp`, `pureFactorSet_eq`, `mixedFactorSet_eq`.\n    26\t* Section 4: the finite-pure functional `finitePureTrace` with `finitePureTrace_one`,\n    27\t  `finitePureTrace_positive`, `finitePureTrace_isFiniteVectorNormal`, the elementary-product\n    28\t  formula `finitePureTrace_lamp_ramp`, traciality on elementary products\n    29\t  `finitePureTrace_tracial_lamp_ramp`, and faithfulness from a separating family.\n    30\t* Sections 5, 7, 8: transport of functionals and of `ℝ≥0∞`-valued weights along a unitary, plus\n    31\t  the unconditional weight calculus (`vectorWeight_add`, `vectorWeight_smul`,\n    32\t  `vectorWeight_star_mul_self`, `vectorWeight_one_eq_top`).\n    33\t* Section 10: the **bundled spatial `⋆`-isomorphism** `spatialRegionalStarEquiv`.\n    34\t\n    35\t**(b) Theorems in the manuscript's intended form (unconditional).**\n    36\t\n    37\t* `spatialRegionalStarEquiv : spatialSubalgebra D ≃⋆ₐ[ℂ] regionalSubalgebra D`, together with\n    38\t  `unitaryConj_image_spatial`: the regional represented algebra is *spatially* `⋆`-isomorphic to\n    39\t  `B(K_pure) ⊗̄ R_mixed`.\n    40\t* `regionalAlgebra_weight_one_eq_top`: in the infinite-pure case the transported weight takes\n    41\t  the value `∞` on `1`, so it is provably **not** a state.\n    42\t\n    43\t**(c) Conditional theorems, with their exact extra premises.**\n    44\t\n    45\t* `spatialTensorAlgebra_hasTrivialCenter`, `regionalAlgebra_hasTrivialCenter`\n    46\t  (premise `SpatialFactorPremises`: `pure_nontrivial`, `pure_commutant`, `mixed_factor`).\n    47\t* `spatialTensorAlgebra_isNormalizedTracialState`,\n    48\t  `regionalAlgebra_isNormalizedTracialState`\n    49\t  (premise `FinitePureTracePremises`: `mixed_unit`, `tracial`, `separating`).\n    50\t* `spatialTensorAlgebra_isFaithfulNormalSemifiniteWeight`,\n    51\t  `regionalAlgebra_isFaithfulNormalSemifiniteWeight`\n    52\t  (premise `InfinitePureWeightPremises`: `mixed_unit`, `separating`, `semifinite`, `tracial`).\n    53\t\n    54\t**(d) Auxiliary assumptions used (all explicit Lean structure fields, never axioms).**\n    55\t\n    56\t1. `SpatialFactorPremises.pure_commutant` — the commutation theorem for the pure type I factor,\n    57\t   `(π₁(A₁) ⊗ 1)' = 1 ⊗ B(K_mixed)`; it packages irreducibility of the pure GNS representation\n    58\t   together with the elementary commutation theorem.\n    59\t2. `SpatialFactorPremises.mixed_factor` — factoriality of the mixed weak closure (supplied in the\n    60\t   local-hyperbolic model by P58's `MixedWeakClosurePremises.factor`).\n    61\t3. `SpatialFactorPremises.pure_nontrivial` — the pure GNS space is nonzero.\n    62\t4. `FinitePureTracePremises.tracial` / `InfinitePureWeightPremises.tracial` — persistence of\n    63\t   traciality from the elementary products (proved here) to the whole bicommutant; this needs\n    64\t   σ-weak normality plus Kaplansky density, absent from pinned Mathlib.\n    65\t5. `FinitePureTracePremises.separating` / `InfinitePureWeightPremises.separating` — the product\n    66\t   vectors `eᵢ ⊗ Ω` are separating for the algebra.\n    67\t6. `FinitePureTracePremises.mixed_unit` / `InfinitePureWeightPremises.mixed_unit` — `Ω` is a unit\n    68\t   vector.\n    69\t7. `InfinitePureWeightPremises.semifinite` — semifiniteness of the canonical trace-weight.\n    70\t\n    71\t**(e) Source/Mathlib obstructions still open.**  Pinned Mathlib has no von Neumann spatial tensor\n    72\tproduct, no commutation theorem `(M ⊗̄ N)' = M' ⊗̄ N'`, no Kaplansky density theorem, no σ-weak\n    73\ttopology API for normality, and no canonical semifinite trace on `B(H)`.  Items 1, 4 and 7 above\n    74\tare exactly the places where those missing theories enter.\n    75\t\n    76\t**Forbidden downstream claims are not made here**: no general-lattice central decomposition, no\n    77\tclaim that Lane H proves Lane G, and no global tracial *state* in the infinite-pure case (the\n    78\tinfinite-pure functional is `ℝ≥0∞`-valued and satisfies `W 1 = ∞`).\n    79\t-/\n    80\t\n    81\tset_option maxHeartbeats 1000000\n    82\tset_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000\n    83\t\n    84\topen scoped InnerProductSpace TensorProduct ComplexOrder\n    85\topen UniformSpace\n    86\t\n    87\tnamespace AristotleCandidates\n    88\tnamespace LocalHyperbolicFactorTrace\n    89\t\n    90\tuniverse u\n    91\t\n    92\t/-! ## 1. Amplifications on a Hilbert tensor product\n    93\t\n    94\tGiven two complex Hilbert spaces `K₁`, `K₂`, we construct the two commuting\n    95\tamplification `⋆`-homomorphisms\n    96\t\n    97\t* `lampHom : B(K₁) →⋆ₐ[ℂ] B(K₁ ⊗̂ K₂)`, `A ↦ A ⊗ 1`;\n    98\t* `rampHom : B(K₂) →⋆ₐ[ℂ] B(K₁ ⊗̂ K₂)`, `B ↦ 1 ⊗ B`,\n    99\t\n   100\twhere `K₁ ⊗̂ K₂ = Completion (K₁ ⊗[ℂ] K₂)` is the Hilbert tensor product used\n   101\tby P57.  Pinned Mathlib has no operator tensor product, so the required norm\n   102\tbound `‖(A ⊗ 1) t‖ ≤ ‖A‖ ‖t‖` is proved here from scratch, using positivity of\n   103\t`‖A‖² - A* A` and the fact that a nonnegative operator is a sum of elements\n   104\t`star s * s`.\n   105\t\n   106\tEverything in this section is **checked infrastructure**: no premise is\n   107\tassumed. -/\n   108\t\n   109\tsection Amplification\n   110\t\n   111\tvariable {K₁ K₂ : Type u}\n   112\t  [NormedAddCommGroup K₁] [InnerProductSpace ℂ K₁] [CompleteSpace K₁]\n   113\t  [NormedAddCommGroup K₂] [InnerProductSpace ℂ K₂] [CompleteSpace K₂]\n   114\t\n   115\t/-- The algebraic operator `A ⊗ 1` on the algebraic tensor product. -/\n   116\tnoncomputable def lmapₗ (A : K₁ →L[ℂ] K₁) : (K₁ ⊗[ℂ] K₂) →ₗ[ℂ] (K₁ ⊗[ℂ] K₂) :=\n   117\t  TensorProduct.map A.toLinearMap LinearMap.id\n   118\t\n   119\t/-- The algebraic operator `1 ⊗ B` on the algebraic tensor product. -/\n   120\tnoncomputable def rmapₗ (B : K₂ →L[ℂ] K₂) : (K₁ ⊗[ℂ] K₂) →ₗ[ℂ] (K₁ ⊗[ℂ] K₂) :=\n   121\t  TensorProduct.map LinearMap.id B.toLinearMap\n   122\t\n   123\tomit [CompleteSpace K₁] [CompleteSpace K₂] in\n   124\t@[simp] theorem lmapₗ_tmul (A : K₁ →L[ℂ] K₁) (x : K₁) (y : K₂) :\n   125\t    lmapₗ A (x ⊗ₜ[ℂ] y) = (A x) ⊗ₜ[ℂ] y := rfl\n   126\t\n   127\tomit [CompleteSpace K₁] [CompleteSpace K₂] in\n   128\t@[simp] theorem rmapₗ_tmul (B : K₂ →L[ℂ] K₂) (x : K₁) (y : K₂) :\n   129\t    rmapₗ (K₁ := K₁) B (x ⊗ₜ[ℂ] y) = x ⊗ₜ[ℂ] (B y) := rfl\n   130\t\n   131\tomit [CompleteSpace K₁] [CompleteSpace K₂] in\n   132\ttheorem lmapₗ_one : lmapₗ (K₂ := K₂) (1 : K₁ →L[ℂ] K₁) = LinearMap.id := by\n   133\t  refine TensorProduct.ext' fun x y => ?_\n   134\t  simp\n   135\t\n   136\tomit [CompleteSpace K₁] [CompleteSpace K₂] in\n   137\ttheorem rmapₗ_one : rmapₗ (K₁ := K₁) (1 : K₂ →L[ℂ] K₂) = LinearMap.id := by\n   138\t  refine TensorProduct.ext' fun x y => ?_\n   139\t  simp\n   140\t\n   141\tomit [CompleteSpace K₁] [CompleteSpace K₂] in\n   142\ttheorem lmapₗ_comp (A A' : K₁ →L[ℂ] K₁) (t : K₁ ⊗[ℂ] K₂) :\n   143\t    lmapₗ (A ∘L A') t = lmapₗ A (lmapₗ A' t) := by\n   144\t  induction t using TensorProduct.induction_on with\n   145\t  | zero => simp\n   146\t  | tmul x y => simp\n   147\t  | add t s ht hs => simp only [map_add, ht, hs]\n   148\t\n   149\tomit [CompleteSpace K₁] [CompleteSpace K₂] in\n   150\ttheorem rmapₗ_comp (B B' : K₂ →L[ℂ] K₂) (t : K₁ ⊗[ℂ] K₂) :\n   151\t    rmapₗ (B ∘L B') t = rmapₗ B (rmapₗ B' t) := by\n   152\t  induction t using TensorProduct.induction_on with\n   153\t  | zero => simp\n   154\t  | tmul x y => simp\n   155\t  | add t s ht hs => simp only [map_add, ht, hs]\n   156\t\n   157\tomit [CompleteSpace K₁] [CompleteSpace K₂] in\n   158\ttheorem lmapₗ_rmapₗ_comm (A : K₁ →L[ℂ] K₁) (B : K₂ →L[ℂ] K₂) (t : K₁ ⊗[ℂ] K₂) :\n   159\t    lmapₗ A (rmapₗ B t) = rmapₗ B (lmapₗ A t) := by\n   160\t  induction t using TensorProduct.induction_on with\n   161\t  | zero => simp\n   162\t  | tmul x y => simp\n   163\t  | add t s ht hs => simp only [map_add, ht, hs]\n   164\t\n   165\tomit [CompleteSpace K₁] [CompleteSpace K₂] in\n   166\ttheorem lmapₗ_add (A A' : K₁ →L[ℂ] K₁) (t : K₁ ⊗[ℂ] K₂) :\n   167\t    lmapₗ (A + A') t = lmapₗ A t + lmapₗ A' t := by\n   168\t  induction t using TensorProduct.induction_on with\n   169\t  | zero => simp\n   170\t  | tmul x y => simp [TensorProduct.add_tmul]\n   171\t  | add t s ht hs =>\n   172\t    simp only [map_add, ht, hs]\n   173\t    abel\n   174\t\n   175\tomit [CompleteSpace K₁] [CompleteSpace K₂] in\n   176\ttheorem rmapₗ_add (B B' : K₂ →L[ℂ] K₂) (t : K₁ ⊗[ℂ] K₂) :\n   177\t    rmapₗ (K₁ := K₁) (B + B') t = rmapₗ B t + rmapₗ B' t := by\n   178\t  induction t using TensorProduct.induction_on with\n   179\t  | zero => simp\n   180\t  | tmul x y => simp [TensorProduct.tmul_add]\n   181\t  | add t s ht hs =>\n   182\t    simp only [map_add, ht, hs]\n   183\t    abel\n   184\t\n   185\tomit [CompleteSpace K₁] [CompleteSpace K₂] in\n   186\ttheorem lmapₗ_smul (c : ℂ) (A : K₁ →L[ℂ] K₁) (t : K₁ ⊗[ℂ] K₂) :\n   187\t    lmapₗ (c • A) t = c • lmapₗ A t := by\n   188\t  induction t using TensorProduct.induction_on with\n   189\t  | zero => simp\n   190\t  | tmul x y => simp [TensorProduct.smul_tmul']\n   191\t  | add t s ht hs => simp only [map_add, ht, hs, smul_add]\n   192\t\n   193\tomit [CompleteSpace K₁] [CompleteSpace K₂] in\n   194\ttheorem rmapₗ_smul (c : ℂ) (B : K₂ →L[ℂ] K₂) (t : K₁ ⊗[ℂ] K₂) :\n   195\t    rmapₗ (K₁ := K₁) (c • B) t = c • rmapₗ B t := by\n   196\t  induction t using TensorProduct.induction_on with\n   197\t  | zero => simp\n   198\t  | tmul x y => simp [TensorProduct.tmul_smul]\n   199\t  | add t s ht hs => simp only [map_add, ht, hs, smul_add]\n   200\t\n   201\tomit [CompleteSpace K₁] [CompleteSpace K₂] in\n   202\ttheorem lmapₗ_rsmul (c : ℝ) (A : K₁ →L[ℂ] K₁) (t : K₁ ⊗[ℂ] K₂) :\n   203\t    lmapₗ (c • A) t = (c : ℂ) • lmapₗ A t := by\n   204\t  have : (c • A) = ((c : ℂ) • A) := by\n   205\t    ext x; simp [Complex.coe_smul]\n   206\t  rw [this, lmapₗ_smul]\n   207\t\n   208\tomit [CompleteSpace K₁] [CompleteSpace K₂] in\n   209\ttheorem rmapₗ_rsmul (c : ℝ) (B : K₂ →L[ℂ] K₂) (t : K₁ ⊗[ℂ] K₂) :\n   210\t    rmapₗ (K₁ := K₁) (c • B) t = (c : ℂ) • rmapₗ B t := by\n   211\t  have : (c • B) = ((c : ℂ) • B) := by\n   212\t    ext x; simp [Complex.coe_smul]\n   213\t  rw [this, rmapₗ_smul]\n   214\t\n   215\tomit [CompleteSpace K₁] [CompleteSpace K₂] in\n   216\ttheorem lmapₗ_sub (A A' : K₁ →L[ℂ] K₁) (t : K₁ ⊗[ℂ] K₂) :\n   217\t    lmapₗ (A - A') t = lmapₗ A t - lmapₗ A' t := by\n   218\t  have h : lmapₗ (K₂ := K₂) (A - A' + A') t = lmapₗ (A - A') t + lmapₗ A' t := lmapₗ_add _ _ t\n   219\t  rw [sub_add_cancel] at h\n   220\t  rw [h]\n   221\t  abel\n   222\t\n   223\tomit [CompleteSpace K₁] [CompleteSpace K₂] in\n   224\ttheorem rmapₗ_sub (B B' : K₂ →L[ℂ] K₂) (t : K₁ ⊗[ℂ] K₂) :\n   225\t    rmapₗ (K₁ := K₁) (B - B') t = rmapₗ B t - rmapₗ B' t := by\n   226\t  have h : rmapₗ (K₁ := K₁) (B - B' + B') t = rmapₗ (B - B') t + rmapₗ B' t := rmapₗ_add _ _ t\n   227\t  rw [sub_add_cancel] at h\n   228\t  rw [h]\n   229\t  abel\n   230\t\n   231\tomit [CompleteSpace K₂] in\n   232\t/-- The adjoint identity for `A ⊗ 1` on the algebraic tensor product. -/\n   233\ttheorem inner_lmapₗ (A : K₁ →L[ℂ] K₁) (t s : K₁ ⊗[ℂ] K₂) :\n   234\t    ⟪lmapₗ A t, s⟫_ℂ = ⟪t, lmapₗ (ContinuousLinearMap.adjoint A) s⟫_ℂ := by\n   235\t  induction t using TensorProduct.induction_on with\n   236\t  | zero => simp\n   237\t  | tmul x y =>\n   238\t    induction s using TensorProduct.induction_on with\n   239\t    | zero => simp\n   240\t    | tmul x' y' =>\n   241\t      show ⟪(A x) ⊗ₜ[ℂ] y, x' ⊗ₜ[ℂ] y'⟫_ℂ\n   242\t        = ⟪x ⊗ₜ[ℂ] y, (ContinuousLinearMap.adjoint A x') ⊗ₜ[ℂ] y'⟫_ℂ\n   243\t      rw [TensorProduct.inner_tmul, TensorProduct.inner_tmul,\n   244\t        ContinuousLinearMap.adjoint_inner_right]\n   245\t    | add s₁ s₂ h1 h2 => rw [inner_add_right, h1, h2, map_add, inner_add_right]\n   246\t  | add t₁ t₂ h1 h2 => rw [inner_add_left, ← h1, ← h2, map_add, inner_add_left]\n   247\t\n   248\tomit [CompleteSpace K₁] in\n   249\t/-- The adjoint identity for `1 ⊗ B` on the algebraic tensor product. -/\n   250\ttheorem inner_rmapₗ (B : K₂ →L[ℂ] K₂) (t s : K₁ ⊗[ℂ] K₂) :\n   251\t    ⟪rmapₗ B t, s⟫_ℂ = ⟪t, rmapₗ (ContinuousLinearMap.adjoint B) s⟫_ℂ := by\n   252\t  induction t using TensorProduct.induction_on with\n   253\t  | zero => simp\n   254\t  | tmul x y =>\n   255\t    induction s using TensorProduct.induction_on with\n   256\t    | zero => simp\n   257\t    | tmul x' y' =>\n   258\t      show ⟪x ⊗ₜ[ℂ] (B y), x' ⊗ₜ[ℂ] y'⟫_ℂ\n   259\t        = ⟪x ⊗ₜ[ℂ] y, x' ⊗ₜ[ℂ] (ContinuousLinearMap.adjoint B y')⟫_ℂ\n   260\t      rw [TensorProduct.inner_tmul, TensorProduct.inner_tmul,\n   261\t        ContinuousLinearMap.adjoint_inner_right]\n   262\t    | add s₁ s₂ h1 h2 => rw [inner_add_right, h1, h2, map_add, inner_add_right]\n   263\t  | add t₁ t₂ h1 h2 => rw [inner_add_left, ← h1, ← h2, map_add, inner_add_left]\n   264\t\n   265\tomit [CompleteSpace K₁] [CompleteSpace K₂] in\n   266\t@[simp] theorem lmapₗ_zero (t : K₁ ⊗[ℂ] K₂) : lmapₗ (0 : K₁ →L[ℂ] K₁) t = 0 := by\n   267\t  induction t using TensorProduct.induction_on with\n   268\t  | zero => simp\n   269\t  | tmul x y => simp\n   270\t  | add a b ha hb => simp [map_add, ha, hb]\n   271\t\n   272\tomit [CompleteSpace K₁] [CompleteSpace K₂] in\n   273\t@[simp] theorem rmapₗ_zero (t : K₁ ⊗[ℂ] K₂) : rmapₗ (K₁ := K₁) (0 : K₂ →L[ℂ] K₂) t = 0 := by\n   274\t  induction t using TensorProduct.induction_on with\n   275\t  | zero => simp\n   276\t  | tmul x y => simp\n   277\t  | add a b ha hb => simp [map_add, ha, hb]\n   278\t\n   279\tomit [CompleteSpace K₁] [CompleteSpace K₂] in\n   280\t/-- The real part of `⟪x, x⟫` is `‖x‖²`. -/\n   281\ttheorem re_inner_self (x : K₁ ⊗[ℂ] K₂) : (⟪x, x⟫_ℂ).re = ‖x‖ ^ 2 := by\n   282\t  have h : ⟪x, x⟫_ℂ = ((‖x‖ : ℂ) ^ 2) := inner_self_eq_norm_sq_to_K x\n   283\t  rw [h]; simp [← Complex.ofReal_pow]\n   284\t\n   285\tomit [CompleteSpace K₁] [CompleteSpace K₂] in\n   286\t/-- The real part of `c * ⟪x, x⟫` for a real scalar `c`. -/\n   287\ttheorem re_inner_self_mul (c : ℝ) (x : K₁ ⊗[ℂ] K₂) :\n   288\t    ((c : ℂ) * ⟪x, x⟫_ℂ).re = c * ‖x‖ ^ 2 := by\n   289\t  have h : ⟪x, x⟫_ℂ = ((‖x‖ : ℂ) ^ 2) := inner_self_eq_norm_sq_to_K x\n   290\t  rw [h]; simp [← Complex.ofReal_pow, ← Complex.ofReal_mul]\n   291\t\n   292\tomit [CompleteSpace K₁] [CompleteSpace K₂] in\n   293\t/-- Inner products against the scaled identity in the first slot. -/\n   294\ttheorem inner_lmapₗ_rsmul_one (c : ℝ) (s t : K₁ ⊗[ℂ] K₂) :\n   295\t    ⟪s, lmapₗ ((c : ℝ) • (1 : K₁ →L[ℂ] K₁)) t⟫_ℂ = (c : ℂ) * ⟪s, t⟫_ℂ := by\n   296\t  induction t using TensorProduct.induction_on with\n   297\t  | zero => simp\n   298\t  | tmul x y =>\n   299\t    induction s using TensorProduct.induction_on with\n   300\t    | zero => simp\n   301\t    | tmul x' y' =>\n   302\t      show ⟪x' ⊗ₜ[ℂ] y', (((c : ℝ) • (1 : K₁ →L[ℂ] K₁)) x) ⊗ₜ[ℂ] y⟫_ℂ\n   303\t        = (c : ℂ) * ⟪x' ⊗ₜ[ℂ] y', x ⊗ₜ[ℂ] y⟫_ℂ\n   304\t      rw [TensorProduct.inner_tmul, TensorProduct.inner_tmul]\n   305\t      have hx : (((c : ℝ) • (1 : K₁ →L[ℂ] K₁)) x) = (c : ℂ) • x := by\n   306\t        simp [Complex.coe_smul]\n   307\t      rw [hx, inner_smul_right]\n   308\t      ring\n   309\t    | add s₁ s₂ h1 h2 => rw [inner_add_left, h1, h2, inner_add_left, mul_add]\n   310\t  | add t₁ t₂ h1 h2 => rw [map_add, inner_add_right, h1, h2, inner_add_right, mul_add]\n   311\t\n   312\tomit [CompleteSpace K₁] [CompleteSpace K₂] in\n   313\t/-- Inner products against the scaled identity in the second slot. -/\n   314\ttheorem inner_rmapₗ_rsmul_one (c : ℝ) (s t : K₁ ⊗[ℂ] K₂) :\n   315\t    ⟪s, rmapₗ (K₁ := K₁) ((c : ℝ) • (1 : K₂ →L[ℂ] K₂)) t⟫_ℂ = (c : ℂ) * ⟪s, t⟫_ℂ := by\n   316\t  induction t using TensorProduct.induction_on with\n   317\t  | zero => simp\n   318\t  | tmul x y =>\n   319\t    induction s using TensorProduct.induction_on with\n   320\t    | zero => simp\n   321\t    | tmul x' y' =>\n   322\t      show ⟪x' ⊗ₜ[ℂ] y', x ⊗ₜ[ℂ] (((c : ℝ) • (1 : K₂ →L[ℂ] K₂)) y)⟫_ℂ\n   323\t        = (c : ℂ) * ⟪x' ⊗ₜ[ℂ] y', x ⊗ₜ[ℂ] y⟫_ℂ\n   324\t      rw [TensorProduct.inner_tmul, TensorProduct.inner_tmul]\n   325\t      have hy : (((c : ℝ) • (1 : K₂ →L[ℂ] K₂)) y) = (c : ℂ) • y := by\n   326\t        simp [Complex.coe_smul]\n   327\t      rw [hy, inner_smul_right]\n   328\t      ring\n   329\t    | add s₁ s₂ h1 h2 => rw [inner_add_left, h1, h2, inner_add_left, mul_add]\n   330\t  | add t₁ t₂ h1 h2 => rw [map_add, inner_add_right, h1, h2, inner_add_right, mul_add]\n   331\t\n   332\tomit [CompleteSpace K₂] in\n   333\t/-- Nonnegativity of `⟪t, (P ⊗ 1) t⟫` for a nonnegative operator `P`. -/\n   334\ttheorem re_inner_lmapₗ_nonneg {P : K₁ →L[ℂ] K₁} (hP : 0 ≤ P) (t : K₁ ⊗[ℂ] K₂) :\n   335\t    0 ≤ (⟪t, lmapₗ P t⟫_ℂ).re := by\n   336\t  rw [StarOrderedRing.nonneg_iff] at hP\n   337\t  induction hP using AddSubmonoid.closure_induction with\n   338\t  | mem P hP =>\n   339\t    obtain ⟨s, rfl⟩ := hP\n   340\t    have h : ⟪t, lmapₗ (K₂ := K₂) (star s * s) t⟫_ℂ = ⟪lmapₗ s t, lmapₗ s t⟫_ℂ := by\n   341\t      rw [inner_lmapₗ]\n   342\t      congr 1\n   343\t      have : (star s * s) = (ContinuousLinearMap.adjoint s) ∘L s := by\n   344\t        rw [ContinuousLinearMap.star_eq_adjoint]; rfl\n   345\t      rw [this, lmapₗ_comp]\n   346\t    rw [h, re_inner_self]\n   347\t    positivity\n   348\t  | zero => simp\n   349\t  | add P Q _ _ hP hQ =>\n   350\t    have hadd : ⟪t, lmapₗ (K₂ := K₂) (P + Q) t⟫_ℂ = ⟪t, lmapₗ P t⟫_ℂ + ⟪t, lmapₗ Q t⟫_ℂ := by\n   351\t      rw [lmapₗ_add, inner_add_right]\n   352\t    rw [hadd, Complex.add_re]\n   353\t    exact add_nonneg hP hQ\n   354\t\n   355\tomit [CompleteSpace K₁] in\n   356\t/-- Nonnegativity of `⟪t, (1 ⊗ Q) t⟫` for a nonnegative operator `Q`. -/\n   357\ttheorem re_inner_rmapₗ_nonneg {Q : K₂ →L[ℂ] K₂} (hQ : 0 ≤ Q) (t : K₁ ⊗[ℂ] K₂) :\n   358\t    0 ≤ (⟪t, rmapₗ Q t⟫_ℂ).re := by\n   359\t  rw [StarOrderedRing.nonneg_iff] at hQ\n   360\t  induction hQ using AddSubmonoid.closure_induction with\n   361\t  | mem Q hQ =>\n   362\t    obtain ⟨s, rfl⟩ := hQ\n   363\t    have h : ⟪t, rmapₗ (K₁ := K₁) (star s * s) t⟫_ℂ = ⟪rmapₗ s t, rmapₗ s t⟫_ℂ := by\n   364\t      rw [inner_rmapₗ]\n   365\t      congr 1\n   366\t      have : (star s * s) = (ContinuousLinearMap.adjoint s) ∘L s := by\n   367\t        rw [ContinuousLinearMap.star_eq_adjoint]; rfl\n   368\t      rw [this, rmapₗ_comp]\n   369\t    rw [h, re_inner_self]\n   370\t    positivity\n   371\t  | zero => simp\n   372\t  | add P Q _ _ hP hQ =>\n   373\t    have hadd : ⟪t, rmapₗ (K₁ := K₁) (P + Q) t⟫_ℂ = ⟪t, rmapₗ P t⟫_ℂ + ⟪t, rmapₗ Q t⟫_ℂ := by\n   374\t      rw [rmapₗ_add, inner_add_right]\n   375\t    rw [hadd, Complex.add_re]\n   376\t    exact add_nonneg hP hQ\n   377\t\n   378\t/-- `‖A‖² - A*A` is a nonnegative operator. -/\n   379\ttheorem norm_sq_sub_adjoint_mul_self_nonneg (A : K₁ →L[ℂ] K₁) :\n   380\t    (0 : K₁ →L[ℂ] K₁) ≤ (‖A‖ ^ 2 : ℝ) • (1 : K₁ →L[ℂ] K₁) - ContinuousLinearMap.adjoint A ∘L A := by\n   381\t  rw [ContinuousLinearMap.nonneg_iff_isPositive, ContinuousLinearMap.isPositive_iff']\n   382\t  refine ⟨?_, ?_⟩\n   383\t  · refine IsSelfAdjoint.sub (IsSelfAdjoint.smul (IsSelfAdjoint.all _) (IsSelfAdjoint.one _)) ?_\n   384\t    show star (ContinuousLinearMap.adjoint A ∘L A) = _\n   385\t    rw [ContinuousLinearMap.star_eq_adjoint, ContinuousLinearMap.adjoint_comp,\n   386\t      ContinuousLinearMap.adjoint_adjoint]\n   387\t  · intro x\n   388\t    have h1 : ⟪((‖A‖ ^ 2 : ℝ) • (1 : K₁ →L[ℂ] K₁) - ContinuousLinearMap.adjoint A ∘L A) x, x⟫_ℂ\n   389\t        = ((‖A‖ ^ 2 * ‖x‖ ^ 2 - ‖A x‖ ^ 2 : ℝ) : ℂ) := by\n   390\t      simp [ContinuousLinearMap.adjoint_inner_left, inner_self_eq_norm_sq_to_K]\n   391\t    rw [h1, Complex.zero_le_real]\n   392\t    nlinarith [A.le_opNorm x, norm_nonneg (A x), norm_nonneg x, norm_nonneg A]\n   393\t\n   394\tomit [CompleteSpace K₂] in\n   395\t/-- **The tensor norm bound for `A ⊗ 1`.** -/\n   396\ttheorem norm_lmapₗ_le (A : K₁ →L[ℂ] K₁) (t : K₁ ⊗[ℂ] K₂) : ‖lmapₗ A t‖ ≤ ‖A‖ * ‖t‖ := by\n   397\t  set P : K₁ →L[ℂ] K₁ :=\n   398\t    (‖A‖ ^ 2 : ℝ) • (1 : K₁ →L[ℂ] K₁) - ContinuousLinearMap.adjoint A ∘L A with hPdef\n   399\t  have hP : (0 : K₁ →L[ℂ] K₁) ≤ P := norm_sq_sub_adjoint_mul_self_nonneg A\n   400\t  have hsplit : ContinuousLinearMap.adjoint A ∘L A = (‖A‖ ^ 2 : ℝ) • (1 : K₁ →L[ℂ] K₁) - P := by\n   401\t    rw [hPdef]; abel\n   402\t  have key : ‖lmapₗ (K₂ := K₂) A t‖ ^ 2 = (‖A‖ ^ 2) * ‖t‖ ^ 2 - (⟪t, lmapₗ P t⟫_ℂ).re := by\n   403\t    have h0 := inner_lmapₗ (K₂ := K₂) A t (lmapₗ A t)\n   404\t    rw [← lmapₗ_comp] at h0\n   405\t    have h1 : (‖lmapₗ (K₂ := K₂) A t‖ ^ 2 : ℝ)\n   406\t        = (⟪t, lmapₗ (ContinuousLinearMap.adjoint A ∘L A) t⟫_ℂ).re := by\n   407\t      rw [← h0, re_inner_self]\n   408\t    rw [h1, hsplit, lmapₗ_sub, inner_sub_right, Complex.sub_re]\n   409\t    congr 1\n   410\t    rw [inner_lmapₗ_rsmul_one, re_inner_self_mul]\n   411\t  have hnn : 0 ≤ (⟪t, lmapₗ (K₂ := K₂) P t⟫_ℂ).re := re_inner_lmapₗ_nonneg hP t\n   412\t  have hle : ‖lmapₗ (K₂ := K₂) A t‖ ^ 2 ≤ (‖A‖ * ‖t‖) ^ 2 := by\n   413\t    rw [key, mul_pow]; linarith\n   414\t  exact (sq_le_sq₀ (norm_nonneg _) (by positivity)).mp hle\n   415\t\n   416\tomit [CompleteSpace K₁] in\n   417\t/-- **The tensor norm bound for `1 ⊗ B`.** -/\n   418\ttheorem norm_rmapₗ_le (B : K₂ →L[ℂ] K₂) (t : K₁ ⊗[ℂ] K₂) : ‖rmapₗ B t‖ ≤ ‖B‖ * ‖t‖ := by\n   419\t  set Q : K₂ →L[ℂ] K₂ :=\n   420\t    (‖B‖ ^ 2 : ℝ) • (1 : K₂ →L[ℂ] K₂) - ContinuousLinearMap.adjoint B ∘L B with hQdef\n   421\t  have hQ : (0 : K₂ →L[ℂ] K₂) ≤ Q := norm_sq_sub_adjoint_mul_self_nonneg B\n   422\t  have hsplit : ContinuousLinearMap.adjoint B ∘L B = (‖B‖ ^ 2 : ℝ) • (1 : K₂ →L[ℂ] K₂) - Q := by\n   423\t    rw [hQdef]; abel\n   424\t  have key : ‖rmapₗ (K₁ := K₁) B t‖ ^ 2 = (‖B‖ ^ 2) * ‖t‖ ^ 2 - (⟪t, rmapₗ Q t⟫_ℂ).re := by\n   425\t    have h0 := inner_rmapₗ (K₁ := K₁) B t (rmapₗ B t)\n   426\t    rw [← rmapₗ_comp] at h0\n   427\t    have h1 : (‖rmapₗ (K₁ := K₁) B t‖ ^ 2 : ℝ)\n   428\t        = (⟪t, rmapₗ (ContinuousLinearMap.adjoint B ∘L B) t⟫_ℂ).re := by\n   429\t      rw [← h0, re_inner_self]\n   430\t    rw [h1, hsplit, rmapₗ_sub, inner_sub_right, Complex.sub_re]\n   431\t    congr 1\n   432\t    rw [inner_rmapₗ_rsmul_one, re_inner_self_mul]\n   433\t  have hnn : 0 ≤ (⟪t, rmapₗ (K₁ := K₁) Q t⟫_ℂ).re := re_inner_rmapₗ_nonneg hQ t\n   434\t  have hle : ‖rmapₗ (K₁ := K₁) B t‖ ^ 2 ≤ (‖B‖ * ‖t‖) ^ 2 := by\n   435\t    rw [key, mul_pow]; linarith\n   436\t  exact (sq_le_sq₀ (norm_nonneg _) (by positivity)).mp hle\n   437\t\n   438\t/-! ### 1.2 The amplification `⋆`-homomorphisms on the Hilbert tensor product -/\n   439\t\n   440\tomit [CompleteSpace K₁] [CompleteSpace K₂] in\n   441\t/-- Extensionality on the completion: two continuous linear maps out of a completion agree as\n   442\tsoon as they agree on the image of the dense subspace. -/\n   443\ttheorem completion_clm_ext {Y : Type u} [NormedAddCommGroup Y] [NormedSpace ℂ Y]\n   444\t    (S T : Completion (K₁ ⊗[ℂ] K₂) →L[ℂ] Y)\n   445\t    (h : ∀ t : K₁ ⊗[ℂ] K₂, S (t : Completion (K₁ ⊗[ℂ] K₂)) = T t) : S = T := by\n   446\t  ext z\n   447\t  induction z using Completion.induction_on with\n   448\t  | hp => exact isClosed_eq S.continuous T.continuous\n   449\t  | ih t => exact h t\n   450\t\n   451\t/-- The bounded operator `A ⊗ 1` on the algebraic tensor product. -/\n   452\tnoncomputable def lampPre (A : K₁ →L[ℂ] K₁) : (K₁ ⊗[ℂ] K₂) →L[ℂ] (K₁ ⊗[ℂ] K₂) :=\n   453\t  (lmapₗ A).mkContinuous ‖A‖ (norm_lmapₗ_le A)\n   454\t\n   455\t/-- The bounded operator `1 ⊗ B` on the algebraic tensor product. -/\n   456\tnoncomputable def rampPre (B : K₂ →L[ℂ] K₂) : (K₁ ⊗[ℂ] K₂) →L[ℂ] (K₁ ⊗[ℂ] K₂) :=\n   457\t  (rmapₗ B).mkContinuous ‖B‖ (norm_rmapₗ_le B)\n   458\t\n   459\t/-- **The left amplification** `A ↦ A ⊗ 1` on the Hilbert tensor product. -/\n   460\tnoncomputable def lamp (A : K₁ →L[ℂ] K₁) :\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"candidate='aristotle_responses/P59-local-hyperbolic-factor-trace-theorem-a12190c2-9efd5c22-quarantine/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p59-80nvzu02_aristotle/AristotleCandidates/LocalHyperbolicFactorTraceTheorem.lean'\nprintf '%s\\\\n' '--- infinite weight / terminal sections ---'\nnl -ba \\\"\"'$candidate\" | sed -n '\"'1230,1660p'\nprintf '%s\\\\n' '--- P58 terms actually used ---'\nrg -n 'MixedUHF|MixedWeak|mixedVonNeumann|Hyperfinite|qubit|IsHyperfinite|isMixed|Factor|FiniteFactor|HasTrivialOperatorCenter|uhf' \\\"\"'$candidate\" | sed -n '\"'1,420p'\nprintf '%s\\\\n' '--- P57 terms actually used ---'\nrg -n 'ProductGNS|ProductGNSData|spatialTensor|unitaryConj|pureFactorSet|mixedFactorSet|TensorGNS|TotalGNS|totalRep' \\\"\"'$candidate\" | sed -n '\"'1,500p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"candidate='aristotle_responses/P59-local-hyperbolic-factor-trace-theorem-a12190c2-9efd5c22-quarantine/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p59-80nvzu02_aristotle/AristotleCandidates/LocalHyperbolicFactorTraceTheorem.lean'\nnl -ba \\\"\"'$candidate\" | sed -n '\"'1,130p'\nprintf '\\\\n--- center/spatial section ---\\\\n'\nnl -ba \\\"\"'$candidate\" | sed -n '\"'680,920p'\nprintf '\\\\n--- finite trace section ---\\\\n'\nnl -ba \\\"\"'$candidate\" | sed -n '\"'920,1240p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"candidate='aristotle_responses/P59-local-hyperbolic-factor-trace-theorem-a12190c2-9efd5c22-quarantine/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p59-80nvzu02_aristotle/AristotleCandidates/LocalHyperbolicFactorTraceTheorem.lean'\nnl -ba \\\"\"'$candidate\" | sed -n '\"'1,130p'\nprintf '\\\\n--- center/spatial section ---\\\\n'\nnl -ba \\\"\"'$candidate\" | sed -n '\"'680,920p'\nprintf '\\\\n--- finite trace section ---\\\\n'\nnl -ba \\\"\"'$candidate\" | sed -n '\"'920,1240p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\timport AristotleCandidates.ProductGNSTensorFactorization\n     2\timport AristotleCandidates.MixedUHFHyperfiniteFactor\n     3\t\n     4\t/-!\n     5\t# P59 — local-hyperbolic factor and trace theorem\n     6\t\n     7\t**Context declaration.** Source basis: `main.tex:1671-1679, 1970-2004`.\n     8\tPackage `P59`, Lane `H`.  Predecessors `P57` (`ProductGNSTensorFactorization`)\n     9\tand `P58` (`MixedUHFHyperfiniteFactor`) are imported.\n    10\t\n    11\tThis module transports the P57 spatial product model to the regional\n    12\trepresented algebra, proves the factor (trivial-centre) conclusion from\n    13\texplicitly named commutation premises, and separates the finite-pure tracial\n    14\t**state** from the infinite-pure faithful normal semifinite **weight**.\n    15\t\n    16\t## Results, by status\n    17\t\n    18\t**(a) Checked infrastructure (no premise).**\n    19\t\n    20\t* Sections 1–2: the two commuting amplification `⋆`-homomorphisms\n    21\t  `lampHom : B(K₁) →⋆ₐ[ℂ] B(K₁ ⊗̂ K₂)` and `rampHom : B(K₂) →⋆ₐ[ℂ] B(K₁ ⊗̂ K₂)`, including the\n    22\t  operator norm bounds `norm_lmapₗ_le`, `norm_rmapₗ_le` (pinned Mathlib has no Hilbert-space\n    23\t  operator tensor product), injectivity, and the centre/transport lemmas\n    24\t  `hasTrivialCenterSet_bicommutant`, `HasTrivialCenterSet.image`, `restrictStarAlgEquiv`.\n    25\t* Section 3: `tensorOpC_eq_amp`, `pureFactorSet_eq`, `mixedFactorSet_eq`.\n    26\t* Section 4: the finite-pure functional `finitePureTrace` with `finitePureTrace_one`,\n    27\t  `finitePureTrace_positive`, `finitePureTrace_isFiniteVectorNormal`, the elementary-product\n    28\t  formula `finitePureTrace_lamp_ramp`, traciality on elementary products\n    29\t  `finitePureTrace_tracial_lamp_ramp`, and faithfulness from a separating family.\n    30\t* Sections 5, 7, 8: transport of functionals and of `ℝ≥0∞`-valued weights along a unitary, plus\n    31\t  the unconditional weight calculus (`vectorWeight_add`, `vectorWeight_smul`,\n    32\t  `vectorWeight_star_mul_self`, `vectorWeight_one_eq_top`).\n    33\t* Section 10: the **bundled spatial `⋆`-isomorphism** `spatialRegionalStarEquiv`.\n    34\t\n    35\t**(b) Theorems in the manuscript's intended form (unconditional).**\n    36\t\n    37\t* `spatialRegionalStarEquiv : spatialSubalgebra D ≃⋆ₐ[ℂ] regionalSubalgebra D`, together with\n    38\t  `unitaryConj_image_spatial`: the regional represented algebra is *spatially* `⋆`-isomorphic to\n    39\t  `B(K_pure) ⊗̄ R_mixed`.\n    40\t* `regionalAlgebra_weight_one_eq_top`: in the infinite-pure case the transported weight takes\n    41\t  the value `∞` on `1`, so it is provably **not** a state.\n    42\t\n    43\t**(c) Conditional theorems, with their exact extra premises.**\n    44\t\n    45\t* `spatialTensorAlgebra_hasTrivialCenter`, `regionalAlgebra_hasTrivialCenter`\n    46\t  (premise `SpatialFactorPremises`: `pure_nontrivial`, `pure_commutant`, `mixed_factor`).\n    47\t* `spatialTensorAlgebra_isNormalizedTracialState`,\n    48\t  `regionalAlgebra_isNormalizedTracialState`\n    49\t  (premise `FinitePureTracePremises`: `mixed_unit`, `tracial`, `separating`).\n    50\t* `spatialTensorAlgebra_isFaithfulNormalSemifiniteWeight`,\n    51\t  `regionalAlgebra_isFaithfulNormalSemifiniteWeight`\n    52\t  (premise `InfinitePureWeightPremises`: `mixed_unit`, `separating`, `semifinite`, `tracial`).\n    53\t\n    54\t**(d) Auxiliary assumptions used (all explicit Lean structure fields, never axioms).**\n    55\t\n    56\t1. `SpatialFactorPremises.pure_commutant` — the commutation theorem for the pure type I factor,\n    57\t   `(π₁(A₁) ⊗ 1)' = 1 ⊗ B(K_mixed)`; it packages irreducibility of the pure GNS representation\n    58\t   together with the elementary commutation theorem.\n    59\t2. `SpatialFactorPremises.mixed_factor` — factoriality of the mixed weak closure (supplied in the\n    60\t   local-hyperbolic model by P58's `MixedWeakClosurePremises.factor`).\n    61\t3. `SpatialFactorPremises.pure_nontrivial` — the pure GNS space is nonzero.\n    62\t4. `FinitePureTracePremises.tracial` / `InfinitePureWeightPremises.tracial` — persistence of\n    63\t   traciality from the elementary products (proved here) to the whole bicommutant; this needs\n    64\t   σ-weak normality plus Kaplansky density, absent from pinned Mathlib.\n    65\t5. `FinitePureTracePremises.separating` / `InfinitePureWeightPremises.separating` — the product\n    66\t   vectors `eᵢ ⊗ Ω` are separating for the algebra.\n    67\t6. `FinitePureTracePremises.mixed_unit` / `InfinitePureWeightPremises.mixed_unit` — `Ω` is a unit\n    68\t   vector.\n    69\t7. `InfinitePureWeightPremises.semifinite` — semifiniteness of the canonical trace-weight.\n    70\t\n    71\t**(e) Source/Mathlib obstructions still open.**  Pinned Mathlib has no von Neumann spatial tensor\n    72\tproduct, no commutation theorem `(M ⊗̄ N)' = M' ⊗̄ N'`, no Kaplansky density theorem, no σ-weak\n    73\ttopology API for normality, and no canonical semifinite trace on `B(H)`.  Items 1, 4 and 7 above\n    74\tare exactly the places where those missing theories enter.\n    75\t\n    76\t**Forbidden downstream claims are not made here**: no general-lattice central decomposition, no\n    77\tclaim that Lane H proves Lane G, and no global tracial *state* in the infinite-pure case (the\n    78\tinfinite-pure functional is `ℝ≥0∞`-valued and satisfies `W 1 = ∞`).\n    79\t-/\n    80\t\n    81\tset_option maxHeartbeats 1000000\n    82\tset_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000\n    83\t\n    84\topen scoped InnerProductSpace TensorProduct ComplexOrder\n    85\topen UniformSpace\n    86\t\n    87\tnamespace AristotleCandidates\n    88\tnamespace LocalHyperbolicFactorTrace\n    89\t\n    90\tuniverse u\n    91\t\n    92\t/-! ## 1. Amplifications on a Hilbert tensor product\n    93\t\n    94\tGiven two complex Hilbert spaces `K₁`, `K₂`, we construct the two commuting\n    95\tamplification `⋆`-homomorphisms\n    96\t\n    97\t* `lampHom : B(K₁) →⋆ₐ[ℂ] B(K₁ ⊗̂ K₂)`, `A ↦ A ⊗ 1`;\n    98\t* `rampHom : B(K₂) →⋆ₐ[ℂ] B(K₁ ⊗̂ K₂)`, `B ↦ 1 ⊗ B`,\n    99\t\n   100\twhere `K₁ ⊗̂ K₂ = Completion (K₁ ⊗[ℂ] K₂)` is the Hilbert tensor product used\n   101\tby P57.  Pinned Mathlib has no operator tensor product, so the required norm\n   102\tbound `‖(A ⊗ 1) t‖ ≤ ‖A‖ ‖t‖` is proved here from scratch, using positivity of\n   103\t`‖A‖² - A* A` and the fact that a nonnegative operator is a sum of elements\n   104\t`star s * s`.\n   105\t\n   106\tEverything in this section is **checked infrastructure**: no premise is\n   107\tassumed. -/\n   108\t\n   109\tsection Amplification\n   110\t\n   111\tvariable {K₁ K₂ : Type u}\n   112\t  [NormedAddCommGroup K₁] [InnerProductSpace ℂ K₁] [CompleteSpace K₁]\n   113\t  [NormedAddCommGroup K₂] [InnerProductSpace ℂ K₂] [CompleteSpace K₂]\n   114\t\n   115\t/-- The algebraic operator `A ⊗ 1` on the algebraic tensor product. -/\n   116\tnoncomputable def lmapₗ (A : K₁ →L[ℂ] K₁) : (K₁ ⊗[ℂ] K₂) →ₗ[ℂ] (K₁ ⊗[ℂ] K₂) :=\n   117\t  TensorProduct.map A.toLinearMap LinearMap.id\n   118\t\n   119\t/-- The algebraic operator `1 ⊗ B` on the algebraic tensor product. -/\n   120\tnoncomputable def rmapₗ (B : K₂ →L[ℂ] K₂) : (K₁ ⊗[ℂ] K₂) →ₗ[ℂ] (K₁ ⊗[ℂ] K₂) :=\n   121\t  TensorProduct.map LinearMap.id B.toLinearMap\n   122\t\n   123\tomit [CompleteSpace K₁] [CompleteSpace K₂] in\n   124\t@[simp] theorem lmapₗ_tmul (A : K₁ →L[ℂ] K₁) (x : K₁) (y : K₂) :\n   125\t    lmapₗ A (x ⊗ₜ[ℂ] y) = (A x) ⊗ₜ[ℂ] y := rfl\n   126\t\n   127\tomit [CompleteSpace K₁] [CompleteSpace K₂] in\n   128\t@[simp] theorem rmapₗ_tmul (B : K₂ →L[ℂ] K₂) (x : K₁) (y : K₂) :\n   129\t    rmapₗ (K₁ := K₁) B (x ⊗ₜ[ℂ] y) = x ⊗ₜ[ℂ] (B y) := rfl\n   130\t\n\n--- center/spatial section ---\n   680\t    rcases mul_eq_zero.mp h4 with h | h\n   681\t    · exact absurd (norm_eq_zero.mp h) hx\n   682\t    · exact h\n   683\t  exact sub_eq_zero.mp (norm_eq_zero.mp h5)\n   684\t\n   685\tend Amplification\n   686\t\n   687\t/-! ## 2. Centres, factors, and transport along a `⋆`-isomorphism\n   688\t\n   689\tAll results in this section are **checked infrastructure**; nothing is assumed. -/\n   690\t\n   691\tsection Center\n   692\t\n   693\tvariable {H H' : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℂ H] [CompleteSpace H]\n   694\t  [NormedAddCommGroup H'] [InnerProductSpace ℂ H'] [CompleteSpace H']\n   695\t\n   696\t/-- **Project-local definition (trivial centre / factor, set form).**  A set of operators has\n   697\ttrivial centre when each of its elements that commutes with the whole set is a scalar.  For a\n   698\tconcrete von Neumann algebra this is exactly P58's `HasTrivialOperatorCenter`. -/\n   699\tdef HasTrivialCenterSet (S : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)) : Prop :=\n   700\t  ∀ T ∈ S, (∀ y ∈ S, y * T = T * y) → ∃ c : ℂ, T = c • 1\n   701\t\n   702\ttheorem hasTrivialOperatorCenter_iff (M : VonNeumannAlgebra H) :\n   703\t    StabilizerHyperfinite.HasTrivialOperatorCenter M ↔\n   704\t      HasTrivialCenterSet (M : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)) := Iff.rfl\n   705\t\n   706\tomit [CompleteSpace H] in\n   707\t/-- **The centre of `S''` is the centre of `S'`.**  Hence a bicommutant is a factor as soon as\n   708\tthe commutant is one. -/\n   709\ttheorem hasTrivialCenterSet_bicommutant (S : Set (H →L[ℂ] H))\n   710\t    (h : HasTrivialCenterSet S.centralizer) :\n   711\t    HasTrivialCenterSet S.centralizer.centralizer := by\n   712\t  intro T hTmem hTcomm\n   713\t  have ha : T ∈ S.centralizer := fun y hy =>\n   714\t    hTcomm y (Set.subset_centralizer_centralizer hy)\n   715\t  exact h T ha hTmem\n   716\t\n   717\t/-- **Transport of factoriality along a `⋆`-isomorphism of operator algebras.** -/\n   718\ttheorem HasTrivialCenterSet.image (e : (H →L[ℂ] H) ≃⋆ₐ[ℂ] (H' →L[ℂ] H'))\n   719\t    {S : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)} (h : HasTrivialCenterSet S) : HasTrivialCenterSet (e '' S) := by\n   720\t  rintro _ ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩ hcomm\n   721\t  have hxc : ∀ y ∈ S, y * x = x * y := by\n   722\t    intro y hy\n   723\t    have h1 : e y * e x = e x * e y := hcomm (e y) ⟨y, hy, rfl⟩\n   724\t    rw [← map_mul, ← map_mul] at h1\n   725\t    exact e.injective h1\n   726\t  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := h x hx hxc\n   727\t  exact ⟨c, by rw [hc, map_smul, map_one]⟩\n   728\t\n   729\t/-- Restriction of a `⋆`-isomorphism to a pair of matching `⋆`-subalgebras. -/\n   730\tnoncomputable def restrictStarAlgEquiv {A B : Type*}\n   731\t    [Ring A] [StarRing A] [Algebra ℂ A] [StarModule ℂ A]\n   732\t    [Ring B] [StarRing B] [Algebra ℂ B] [StarModule ℂ B]\n   733\t    (e : A ≃⋆ₐ[ℂ] B) (S : StarSubalgebra ℂ A) (T : StarSubalgebra ℂ B)\n   734\t    (h : ∀ x : A, x ∈ S ↔ e x ∈ T) : S ≃⋆ₐ[ℂ] T :=\n   735\t  StarAlgEquiv.ofBijective\n   736\t    ((((e : A →⋆ₐ[ℂ] B)).comp S.subtype).codRestrict T (fun x => (h x).mp x.2))\n   737\t    ⟨by\n   738\t      intro x y hxy\n   739\t      exact Subtype.ext (e.injective (congrArg Subtype.val hxy)),\n   740\t     by\n   741\t      rintro ⟨y, hy⟩\n   742\t      refine ⟨⟨e.symm y, (h (e.symm y)).mpr ?_⟩, ?_⟩\n   743\t      · rw [e.apply_symm_apply]; exact hy\n   744\t      · exact Subtype.ext (by simp)⟩\n   745\t\n   746\t@[simp] theorem restrictStarAlgEquiv_apply {A B : Type*}\n   747\t    [Ring A] [StarRing A] [Algebra ℂ A] [StarModule ℂ A]\n   748\t    [Ring B] [StarRing B] [Algebra ℂ B] [StarModule ℂ B]\n   749\t    (e : A ≃⋆ₐ[ℂ] B) (S : StarSubalgebra ℂ A) (T : StarSubalgebra ℂ B)\n   750\t    (h : ∀ x : A, x ∈ S ↔ e x ∈ T) (x : S) :\n   751\t    (restrictStarAlgEquiv e S T h x : B) = e (x : A) := rfl\n   752\t\n   753\tend Center\n   754\t\n   755\t/-! ## 3. The spatial product model of the regional algebra\n   756\t\n   757\tWe now specialize to the P57 product-GNS datum `D`.  Its Hilbert tensor product\n   758\t`D.TensorGNS = Completion (K_pure ⊗ K_mixed)` carries the two amplifications of Section 1, and\n   759\tP57's elementary tensor operators factor through them. -/\n   760\t\n   761\tsection Regional\n   762\t\n   763\topen AristotleCandidates.ProductGNSTensor\n   764\t\n   765\tvariable (D : ProductGNSData.{u})\n   766\t\n   767\t/-- The represented pure factor operator `π₁(a) ⊗ 1`. -/\n   768\tnoncomputable def pureAmp (a : D.Pure) : D.TensorGNS →L[ℂ] D.TensorGNS := lamp (D.pureRep a)\n   769\t\n   770\t/-- The represented mixed factor operator `1 ⊗ π₂(b)`. -/\n   771\tnoncomputable def mixedAmp (b : D.Mixed) : D.TensorGNS →L[ℂ] D.TensorGNS := ramp (D.mixedRep b)\n   772\t\n   773\ttheorem tensorMapₗ_eq (a : D.Pure) (b : D.Mixed) (t : D.TensorPre) :\n   774\t    D.tensorMapₗ a b t = lmapₗ (D.pureRep a) (rmapₗ (D.mixedRep b) t) := by\n   775\t  induction t using TensorProduct.induction_on with\n   776\t  | zero => simp\n   777\t  | tmul x y => rfl\n   778\t  | add t s ht hs => simp only [map_add, ht, hs]\n   779\t\n   780\t/-- **P57's elementary tensor operator is the product of the two amplifications.** -/\n   781\ttheorem tensorOpC_eq_amp (a : D.Pure) (b : D.Mixed) :\n   782\t    D.tensorOpC a b = pureAmp D a * mixedAmp D b := by\n   783\t  refine completion_clm_ext _ _ fun t => ?_\n   784\t  show D.tensorOpC a b (t : D.TensorGNS) = lamp (D.pureRep a) (ramp (D.mixedRep b) (t : D.TensorGNS))\n   785\t  rw [ProductGNSData.tensorOpC_coe, ramp_coe, lamp_coe, tensorMapₗ_eq]\n   786\t\n   787\ttheorem pureFactorSet_eq : D.pureFactorSet = Set.range (pureAmp D) := by\n   788\t  refine congrArg Set.range (funext fun a => ?_)\n   789\t  rw [tensorOpC_eq_amp, mixedAmp, map_one, ramp_one, mul_one]\n   790\t\n   791\ttheorem mixedFactorSet_eq : D.mixedFactorSet = Set.range (mixedAmp D) := by\n   792\t  refine congrArg Set.range (funext fun b => ?_)\n   793\t  rw [tensorOpC_eq_amp, pureAmp, map_one, lamp_one, one_mul]\n   794\t\n   795\t/-- The regional represented von Neumann algebra `π_ω̃(A_Γ)''` on the GNS space of the product\n   796\tstate. -/\n   797\tdef regionalAlgebra : Set (D.TotalGNS →L[ℂ] D.TotalGNS) :=\n   798\t  (Set.range D.totalRep).centralizer.centralizer\n   799\t\n   800\t/-- **The spatial identification (P57), restated for this packet.**  Conjugation by the product\n   801\tGNS unitary carries the spatial tensor product `B_pure ⊗̄ R_mixed` onto the regional algebra. -/\n   802\ttheorem unitaryConj_image_spatial : D.unitaryConj '' D.spatialTensorAlgebra = regionalAlgebra D :=\n   803\t  D.unitaryConj_image_spatialTensorAlgebra\n   804\t\n   805\t/-! ### 3.1 The auxiliary commutation premises\n   806\t\n   807\tThe two fields below are the analytic inputs that neither P57 nor P58 provides and that pinned\n   808\tMathlib does not contain.  They are stated as explicit premises, never as axioms.\n   809\t\n   810\t* `pure_commutant` is the *commutation theorem for the type I factor*: the commutant of the\n   811\t  represented pure factor `π₁(A₁) ⊗ 1` consists exactly of the operators `1 ⊗ B`.  It contains\n   812\t  both the irreducibility of the pure GNS representation (`π₁(A₁)'' = B(K_pure)`, true for a pure\n   813\t  state) and the elementary commutation theorem `(B(K_pure) ⊗ 1)' = 1 ⊗ B(K_mixed)`.\n   814\t* `mixed_factor` is the mixed-sector factoriality supplied, in the local-hyperbolic model, by\n   815\t  P58's `MixedWeakClosurePremises.factor`.\n   816\t* `pure_nontrivial` says the pure GNS space is nonzero; it holds whenever `pureState` is a state\n   817\t  (i.e. `pureState 1 = 1`). -/\n   818\tstructure SpatialFactorPremises : Prop where\n   819\t  /-- the pure GNS space is nonzero -/\n   820\t  pure_nontrivial : ∃ x : D.PureGNS, x ≠ 0\n   821\t  /-- commutation theorem for the pure type I factor -/\n   822\t  pure_commutant :\n   823\t    D.pureFactorSet.centralizer = Set.range (ramp (K₁ := D.PureGNS) (K₂ := D.MixedGNS))\n   824\t  /-- the mixed represented algebra is a factor -/\n   825\t  mixed_factor : HasTrivialCenterSet (Set.range D.mixedRep).centralizer.centralizer\n   826\t\n   827\t/-- **Factoriality of the spatial tensor product.**  Under the two named commutation premises,\n   828\t`B(K_pure) ⊗̄ R_mixed` has trivial centre. -/\n   829\ttheorem spatialTensorAlgebra_hasTrivialCenter (h : SpatialFactorPremises D) :\n   830\t    HasTrivialCenterSet D.spatialTensorAlgebra := by\n   831\t  classical\n   832\t  set S : Set (D.TensorGNS →L[ℂ] D.TensorGNS) := D.pureFactorSet ∪ D.mixedFactorSet with hS\n   833\t  have hramp_inj : Function.Injective (ramp (K₁ := D.PureGNS) (K₂ := D.MixedGNS)) :=\n   834\t    ramp_injective h.pure_nontrivial\n   835\t  intro T hTmem hTcomm\n   836\t  -- `T` commutes with `S`, hence lies in `S'`\n   837\t  have hTS : T ∈ S.centralizer := fun y hy =>\n   838\t    hTcomm y (Set.subset_centralizer_centralizer hy)\n   839\t  -- hence `T = 1 ⊗ b` for some `b`\n   840\t  have hTpure : T ∈ D.pureFactorSet.centralizer := fun y hy => hTS y (Or.inl hy)\n   841\t  obtain ⟨b, rfl⟩ : ∃ b, ramp b = T := by\n   842\t    have := h.pure_commutant ▸ hTpure\n   843\t    exact this\n   844\t  -- `b` commutes with the represented mixed algebra\n   845\t  have hbN' : b ∈ (Set.range D.mixedRep).centralizer := by\n   846\t    rintro _ ⟨m, rfl⟩\n   847\t    have h1 : mixedAmp D m * ramp b = ramp b * mixedAmp D m :=\n   848\t      hTS _ (Or.inr (by rw [mixedFactorSet_eq]; exact ⟨m, rfl⟩))\n   849\t    rw [mixedAmp, ← ramp_mul, ← ramp_mul] at h1\n   850\t    exact hramp_inj h1\n   851\t  -- every `1 ⊗ c` with `c` in the commutant lies in `S'`\n   852\t  have hrampS : ∀ c ∈ (Set.range D.mixedRep).centralizer, ramp c ∈ S.centralizer := by\n   853\t    intro c hc y hy\n   854\t    rcases hy with hy | hy\n   855\t    · rw [pureFactorSet_eq] at hy\n   856\t      obtain ⟨a, rfl⟩ := hy\n   857\t      exact (lamp_ramp_commute (D.pureRep a) c).symm ▸ rfl\n   858\t    · rw [mixedFactorSet_eq] at hy\n   859\t      obtain ⟨m, rfl⟩ := hy\n   860\t      rw [mixedAmp, ← ramp_mul, ← ramp_mul, hc _ ⟨m, rfl⟩]\n   861\t  -- so `b` also commutes with the whole commutant, i.e. `b ∈ N''`\n   862\t  have hbN'' : b ∈ (Set.range D.mixedRep).centralizer.centralizer := by\n   863\t    intro c hc\n   864\t    have h1 : ramp c * ramp b = ramp b * ramp c := hTmem _ (hrampS c hc)\n   865\t    rw [← ramp_mul, ← ramp_mul] at h1\n   866\t    exact hramp_inj h1\n   867\t  -- `b` is central in `N''`, hence scalar\n   868\t  obtain ⟨c₀, hc₀⟩ := h.mixed_factor b hbN'' (fun y hy => (hy b hbN').symm)\n   869\t  exact ⟨c₀, by rw [hc₀, ramp_smul, ramp_one]⟩\n   870\t\n   871\t/-- **Factoriality of the regional algebra.**  Transporting the previous theorem through the\n   872\tproduct GNS unitary: the regional represented von Neumann algebra is a factor. -/\n   873\ttheorem regionalAlgebra_hasTrivialCenter (h : SpatialFactorPremises D) :\n   874\t    HasTrivialCenterSet (regionalAlgebra D) := by\n   875\t  rw [← unitaryConj_image_spatial]\n   876\t  exact (spatialTensorAlgebra_hasTrivialCenter D h).image D.unitaryConj\n   877\t\n   878\tend Regional\n   879\t\n   880\t/-! ## 4. Product vectors and the finite-pure normalized tracial state\n   881\t\n   882\tFor a *finite-dimensional* pure sector `K_pure` with orthonormal basis `e`, and a unit vector\n   883\t`Ω` in the mixed sector, the functional\n   884\t\n   885\t`φ(T) = (dim K_pure)⁻¹ ∑ᵢ ⟪eᵢ ⊗ Ω, T (eᵢ ⊗ Ω)⟫`\n   886\t\n   887\tis the normalized `tr ⊗ τ`.  Unitality, positivity, normality (as a finite sum of vector\n   888\tfunctionals) and traciality on elementary products are proved unconditionally; only faithfulness\n   889\tuses a named separating-vector premise. -/\n   890\t\n   891\tsection ProductVectors\n   892\t\n   893\tvariable {K₁ K₂ : Type u}\n   894\t  [NormedAddCommGroup K₁] [InnerProductSpace ℂ K₁] [CompleteSpace K₁]\n   895\t  [NormedAddCommGroup K₂] [InnerProductSpace ℂ K₂] [CompleteSpace K₂]\n   896\t\n   897\t/-- The product vectors `vᵢ ⊗ Ω` in the Hilbert tensor product. -/\n   898\tnoncomputable def tvec {ι : Type*} (v : ι → K₁) (Ω : K₂) (i : ι) :\n   899\t    Completion (K₁ ⊗[ℂ] K₂) := ((v i ⊗ₜ[ℂ] Ω : K₁ ⊗[ℂ] K₂) : Completion (K₁ ⊗[ℂ] K₂))\n   900\t\n   901\tomit [CompleteSpace K₁] [CompleteSpace K₂] in\n   902\ttheorem inner_tvec_self {ι : Type*} (v : ι → K₁) (Ω : K₂) (i : ι) :\n   903\t    ⟪tvec v Ω i, tvec v Ω i⟫_ℂ = ⟪v i, v i⟫_ℂ * ⟪Ω, Ω⟫_ℂ := by\n   904\t  rw [tvec, Completion.inner_coe, TensorProduct.inner_tmul]\n   905\t\n   906\ttheorem lamp_ramp_apply_tvec {ι : Type*} (v : ι → K₁) (Ω : K₂)\n   907\t    (A : K₁ →L[ℂ] K₁) (B : K₂ →L[ℂ] K₂) (i : ι) :\n   908\t    (lamp A * ramp B : Completion (K₁ ⊗[ℂ] K₂) →L[ℂ] Completion (K₁ ⊗[ℂ] K₂)) (tvec v Ω i)\n   909\t      = ((A (v i) ⊗ₜ[ℂ] B Ω : K₁ ⊗[ℂ] K₂) : Completion (K₁ ⊗[ℂ] K₂)) := by\n   910\t  show lamp A (ramp B (tvec v Ω i)) = _\n   911\t  rw [tvec, ramp_coe, lamp_coe]\n   912\t  rfl\n   913\t\n   914\ttheorem inner_tvec_lamp_ramp {ι : Type*} (v : ι → K₁) (Ω : K₂)\n   915\t    (A : K₁ →L[ℂ] K₁) (B : K₂ →L[ℂ] K₂) (i : ι) :\n   916\t    ⟪tvec v Ω i, (lamp A * ramp B : Completion (K₁ ⊗[ℂ] K₂) →L[ℂ] Completion (K₁ ⊗[ℂ] K₂))\n   917\t        (tvec v Ω i)⟫_ℂ = ⟪v i, A (v i)⟫_ℂ * ⟪Ω, B Ω⟫_ℂ := by\n   918\t  rw [lamp_ramp_apply_tvec, tvec, Completion.inner_coe, TensorProduct.inner_tmul]\n   919\t\n   920\t/-- **Project-local definition (finitely-vector-normal functional).**  A functional given by a\n\n--- finite trace section ---\n   920\t/-- **Project-local definition (finitely-vector-normal functional).**  A functional given by a\n   921\tfinite sum of vector functionals; this is the concrete form of normality available here. -/\n   922\tdef IsFiniteVectorNormal {H : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℂ H]\n   923\t    [CompleteSpace H] (phi : (H →L[ℂ] H) →ₗ[ℂ] ℂ) : Prop :=\n   924\t  ∃ (n : ℕ) (w : Fin n → H), ∀ T : H →L[ℂ] H, phi T = ∑ i, ⟪w i, T (w i)⟫_ℂ\n   925\t\n   926\t/-- **Project-local definition (normalized tracial state on a set of operators).** -/\n   927\tstructure IsNormalizedTracialStateOn {H : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℂ H]\n   928\t    [CompleteSpace H] (M : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)) (phi : (H →L[ℂ] H) →ₗ[ℂ] ℂ) : Prop where\n   929\t  /-- normality, in the finite-vector sense -/\n   930\t  normal : IsFiniteVectorNormal phi\n   931\t  /-- normalization -/\n   932\t  unital : phi 1 = 1\n   933\t  /-- positivity -/\n   934\t  positive : ∀ T : H →L[ℂ] H, ∃ r : ℝ, 0 ≤ r ∧ phi (star T * T) = (r : ℂ)\n   935\t  /-- traciality on `M` -/\n   936\t  tracial : ∀ X ∈ M, ∀ Y ∈ M, phi (X * Y) = phi (Y * X)\n   937\t  /-- faithfulness on `M` -/\n   938\t  faithful : ∀ X ∈ M, phi (star X * X) = 0 → X = 0\n   939\t\n   940\tend ProductVectors\n   941\t\n   942\tsection FinitePure\n   943\t\n   944\tvariable {K₁ K₂ : Type u}\n   945\t  [NormedAddCommGroup K₁] [InnerProductSpace ℂ K₁] [CompleteSpace K₁]\n   946\t  [NormedAddCommGroup K₂] [InnerProductSpace ℂ K₂] [CompleteSpace K₂]\n   947\t  {ι : Type u} [Fintype ι] [Nonempty ι]\n   948\t\n   949\t/-- **The normalized finite-pure functional** `(dim K_pure)⁻¹ · tr ⊗ ⟪Ω, · Ω⟫`. -/\n   950\tnoncomputable def finitePureTrace (e : OrthonormalBasis ι ℂ K₁) (Ω : K₂) :\n   951\t    (Completion (K₁ ⊗[ℂ] K₂) →L[ℂ] Completion (K₁ ⊗[ℂ] K₂)) →ₗ[ℂ] ℂ where\n   952\t  toFun T := (Fintype.card ι : ℂ)⁻¹ * ∑ i, ⟪tvec (⇑e) Ω i, T (tvec (⇑e) Ω i)⟫_ℂ\n   953\t  map_add' T S := by\n   954\t    simp only [ContinuousLinearMap.add_apply, inner_add_right, Finset.sum_add_distrib]\n   955\t    ring\n   956\t  map_smul' c T := by\n   957\t    simp only [ContinuousLinearMap.smul_apply, inner_smul_right, ← Finset.mul_sum,\n   958\t      RingHom.id_apply, smul_eq_mul]\n   959\t    ring\n   960\t\n   961\tomit [Nonempty ι] in\n   962\tomit [CompleteSpace K₁] [CompleteSpace K₂] in\n   963\t@[simp] theorem finitePureTrace_apply (e : OrthonormalBasis ι ℂ K₁) (Ω : K₂)\n   964\t    (T : Completion (K₁ ⊗[ℂ] K₂) →L[ℂ] Completion (K₁ ⊗[ℂ] K₂)) :\n   965\t    finitePureTrace e Ω T\n   966\t      = (Fintype.card ι : ℂ)⁻¹ * ∑ i, ⟪tvec (⇑e) Ω i, T (tvec (⇑e) Ω i)⟫_ℂ := rfl\n   967\t\n   968\ttheorem card_ne_zero : ((Fintype.card ι : ℂ)) ≠ 0 :=\n   969\t  Nat.cast_ne_zero.mpr Fintype.card_ne_zero\n   970\t\n   971\tomit [CompleteSpace K₁] [CompleteSpace K₂] in\n   972\t/-- The finite-pure functional is normal in the finite-vector sense. -/\n   973\ttheorem finitePureTrace_isFiniteVectorNormal (e : OrthonormalBasis ι ℂ K₁) (Ω : K₂) :\n   974\t    IsFiniteVectorNormal (finitePureTrace e Ω) := by\n   975\t  classical\n   976\t  obtain ⟨f⟩ := Fintype.truncEquivFin ι\n   977\t  set c : ℂ := (((Real.sqrt (Fintype.card ι) : ℝ)) : ℂ)⁻¹ with hcdef\n   978\t  have hcard : (0:ℝ) < (Fintype.card ι : ℝ) := by exact_mod_cast Fintype.card_pos\n   979\t  have hc2 : (starRingEnd ℂ) c * c = ((Fintype.card ι : ℂ))⁻¹ := by\n   980\t    have h1 : (starRingEnd ℂ) c = c := by\n   981\t      rw [hcdef, map_inv₀, Complex.conj_ofReal]\n   982\t    rw [h1, hcdef, ← mul_inv, ← Complex.ofReal_mul, Real.mul_self_sqrt hcard.le]\n   983\t    norm_num\n   984\t  refine ⟨Fintype.card ι, fun j => c • tvec (⇑e) Ω (f.symm j), fun T => ?_⟩\n   985\t  have hscal : ∀ j : Fin (Fintype.card ι),\n   986\t      ⟪c • tvec (⇑e) Ω (f.symm j), T (c • tvec (⇑e) Ω (f.symm j))⟫_ℂ\n   987\t        = ((Fintype.card ι : ℂ))⁻¹ * ⟪tvec (⇑e) Ω (f.symm j), T (tvec (⇑e) Ω (f.symm j))⟫_ℂ := by\n   988\t    intro j\n   989\t    rw [map_smul, inner_smul_left, inner_smul_right, ← mul_assoc, hc2]\n   990\t  rw [finitePureTrace_apply, Finset.mul_sum]\n   991\t  rw [← Equiv.sum_comp f.symm\n   992\t    (fun i => ((Fintype.card ι : ℂ))⁻¹ * ⟪tvec (⇑e) Ω i, T (tvec (⇑e) Ω i)⟫_ℂ)]\n   993\t  exact (Finset.sum_congr rfl fun j _ => hscal j).symm\n   994\t\n   995\tomit [CompleteSpace K₁] [CompleteSpace K₂] in\n   996\t/-- **Unitality** of the finite-pure functional for a unit vector `Ω`. -/\n   997\ttheorem finitePureTrace_one (e : OrthonormalBasis ι ℂ K₁) {Ω : K₂} (hΩ : ‖Ω‖ = 1) :\n   998\t    finitePureTrace e Ω 1 = 1 := by\n   999\t  have hΩ2 : ⟪Ω, Ω⟫_ℂ = 1 := by\n  1000\t    rw [inner_self_eq_norm_sq_to_K, hΩ]; norm_num\n  1001\t  have hsum : ∑ _i : ι, ⟪Ω, Ω⟫_ℂ = (Fintype.card ι : ℂ) := by\n  1002\t    rw [Finset.sum_const, hΩ2, Finset.card_univ]\n  1003\t    simp\n  1004\t  rw [finitePureTrace_apply]\n  1005\t  have : ∀ i : ι, ⟪tvec (⇑e) Ω i, (1 : Completion (K₁ ⊗[ℂ] K₂) →L[ℂ] Completion (K₁ ⊗[ℂ] K₂))\n  1006\t      (tvec (⇑e) Ω i)⟫_ℂ = ⟪Ω, Ω⟫_ℂ := by\n  1007\t    intro i\n  1008\t    have he : ⟪e i, e i⟫_ℂ = 1 := by\n  1009\t      rw [inner_self_eq_norm_sq_to_K, e.orthonormal.1 i]; norm_num\n  1010\t    rw [ContinuousLinearMap.one_apply, inner_tvec_self, he, one_mul]\n  1011\t  rw [Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ => this i, hsum, inv_mul_cancel₀ card_ne_zero]\n  1012\t\n  1013\tomit [CompleteSpace K₁] [CompleteSpace K₂] in\n  1014\t/-- **Positivity** of the finite-pure functional. -/\n  1015\ttheorem finitePureTrace_positive (e : OrthonormalBasis ι ℂ K₁) (Ω : K₂)\n  1016\t    (T : Completion (K₁ ⊗[ℂ] K₂) →L[ℂ] Completion (K₁ ⊗[ℂ] K₂)) :\n  1017\t    ∃ r : ℝ, 0 ≤ r ∧ finitePureTrace e Ω (star T * T) = (r : ℂ) := by\n  1018\t  refine ⟨(Fintype.card ι : ℝ)⁻¹ * ∑ i, ‖T (tvec (⇑e) Ω i)‖ ^ 2, by positivity, ?_⟩\n  1019\t  rw [finitePureTrace_apply]\n  1020\t  have hterm : ∀ i : ι, ⟪tvec (⇑e) Ω i, (star T * T) (tvec (⇑e) Ω i)⟫_ℂ\n  1021\t      = ((‖T (tvec (⇑e) Ω i)‖ ^ 2 : ℝ) : ℂ) := by\n  1022\t    intro i\n  1023\t    rw [ContinuousLinearMap.mul_apply, ContinuousLinearMap.star_eq_adjoint,\n  1024\t      ContinuousLinearMap.adjoint_inner_right, inner_self_eq_norm_sq_to_K]\n  1025\t    push_cast\n  1026\t    norm_num\n  1027\t  rw [Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ => hterm i]\n  1028\t  push_cast\n  1029\t  ring\n  1030\t\n  1031\tomit [Nonempty ι] in\n  1032\t/-- **The elementary-product formula**: on `A ⊗ B` the functional is the normalized trace of `A`\n  1033\ttimes the mixed vector state of `B`. -/\n  1034\ttheorem finitePureTrace_lamp_ramp (e : OrthonormalBasis ι ℂ K₁) (Ω : K₂)\n  1035\t    (A : K₁ →L[ℂ] K₁) (B : K₂ →L[ℂ] K₂) :\n  1036\t    finitePureTrace e Ω (lamp A * ramp B)\n  1037\t      = (Fintype.card ι : ℂ)⁻¹ * (LinearMap.trace ℂ K₁ (A : K₁ →ₗ[ℂ] K₁)) * ⟪Ω, B Ω⟫_ℂ := by\n  1038\t  rw [finitePureTrace_apply, LinearMap.trace_eq_sum_inner _ e]\n  1039\t  simp only [inner_tvec_lamp_ramp]\n  1040\t  rw [← Finset.sum_mul, mul_assoc]\n  1041\t  rfl\n  1042\t\n  1043\tomit [Nonempty ι] in\n  1044\t/-- **Traciality on elementary products**, given traciality of the mixed vector state on the\n  1045\tpair `(B, B')`. -/\n  1046\ttheorem finitePureTrace_tracial_lamp_ramp [FiniteDimensional ℂ K₁]\n  1047\t    (e : OrthonormalBasis ι ℂ K₁) (Ω : K₂)\n  1048\t    (A A' : K₁ →L[ℂ] K₁) (B B' : K₂ →L[ℂ] K₂)\n  1049\t    (hmix : ⟪Ω, (B * B') Ω⟫_ℂ = ⟪Ω, (B' * B) Ω⟫_ℂ) :\n  1050\t    finitePureTrace e Ω ((lamp A * ramp B) * (lamp A' * ramp B'))\n  1051\t      = finitePureTrace e Ω ((lamp A' * ramp B') * (lamp A * ramp B)) := by\n  1052\t  have hprod : ∀ (X X' : K₁ →L[ℂ] K₁) (Y Y' : K₂ →L[ℂ] K₂),\n  1053\t      (lamp X * ramp Y) * (lamp X' * ramp Y') = lamp (X * X') * ramp (Y * Y') := by\n  1054\t    intro X X' Y Y'\n  1055\t    rw [lamp_mul, ramp_mul]\n  1056\t    have h := lamp_ramp_commute X' Y\n  1057\t    calc lamp X * ramp Y * (lamp X' * ramp Y')\n  1058\t        = lamp X * (ramp Y * lamp X') * ramp Y' := by\n  1059\t          simp only [mul_assoc]\n  1060\t      _ = lamp X * (lamp X' * ramp Y) * ramp Y' := by rw [← h]\n  1061\t      _ = lamp X * lamp X' * (ramp Y * ramp Y') := by simp only [mul_assoc]\n  1062\t  rw [hprod, hprod, finitePureTrace_lamp_ramp, finitePureTrace_lamp_ramp, hmix]\n  1063\t  congr 2\n  1064\t  have : ((A * A' : K₁ →L[ℂ] K₁) : K₁ →ₗ[ℂ] K₁)\n  1065\t      = (A : K₁ →ₗ[ℂ] K₁) * (A' : K₁ →ₗ[ℂ] K₁) := rfl\n  1066\t  rw [this]\n  1067\t  have : ((A' * A : K₁ →L[ℂ] K₁) : K₁ →ₗ[ℂ] K₁)\n  1068\t      = (A' : K₁ →ₗ[ℂ] K₁) * (A : K₁ →ₗ[ℂ] K₁) := rfl\n  1069\t  rw [this, LinearMap.trace_mul_comm]\n  1070\t\n  1071\tomit [CompleteSpace K₁] [CompleteSpace K₂] in\n  1072\t/-- **Faithfulness** of the finite-pure functional on a set of operators for which the product\n  1073\tvectors are separating. -/\n  1074\ttheorem finitePureTrace_faithful (e : OrthonormalBasis ι ℂ K₁) (Ω : K₂)\n  1075\t    {M : Set (Completion (K₁ ⊗[ℂ] K₂) →L[ℂ] Completion (K₁ ⊗[ℂ] K₂))}\n  1076\t    (hsep : ∀ T ∈ M, (∀ i, T (tvec (⇑e) Ω i) = 0) → T = 0)\n  1077\t    (T : Completion (K₁ ⊗[ℂ] K₂) →L[ℂ] Completion (K₁ ⊗[ℂ] K₂)) (hT : T ∈ M)\n  1078\t    (h0 : finitePureTrace e Ω (star T * T) = 0) : T = 0 := by\n  1079\t  refine hsep T hT fun i => ?_\n  1080\t  obtain ⟨r, hr0, hr⟩ := finitePureTrace_positive e Ω T\n  1081\t  have hterm : ∀ j : ι, ⟪tvec (⇑e) Ω j, (star T * T) (tvec (⇑e) Ω j)⟫_ℂ\n  1082\t      = ((‖T (tvec (⇑e) Ω j)‖ ^ 2 : ℝ) : ℂ) := by\n  1083\t    intro j\n  1084\t    rw [ContinuousLinearMap.mul_apply, ContinuousLinearMap.star_eq_adjoint,\n  1085\t      ContinuousLinearMap.adjoint_inner_right, inner_self_eq_norm_sq_to_K]\n  1086\t    push_cast\n  1087\t    norm_num\n  1088\t  have hsum : ((∑ j, ‖T (tvec (⇑e) Ω j)‖ ^ 2 : ℝ) : ℂ) = 0 := by\n  1089\t    have h1 : (Fintype.card ι : ℂ)⁻¹ * ∑ j, ⟪tvec (⇑e) Ω j, (star T * T) (tvec (⇑e) Ω j)⟫_ℂ = 0 := h0\n  1090\t    rw [Finset.sum_congr rfl fun j _ => hterm j] at h1\n  1091\t    have h2 : ∑ j : ι, ((‖T (tvec (⇑e) Ω j)‖ ^ 2 : ℝ) : ℂ) = 0 := by\n  1092\t      rcases mul_eq_zero.mp h1 with h | h\n  1093\t      · exact absurd (inv_eq_zero.mp h) card_ne_zero\n  1094\t      · exact h\n  1095\t    rw [← h2]\n  1096\t    push_cast\n  1097\t    ring\n  1098\t  have hsumR : (∑ j, ‖T (tvec (⇑e) Ω j)‖ ^ 2 : ℝ) = 0 := by\n  1099\t    exact_mod_cast hsum\n  1100\t  have hz : ‖T (tvec (⇑e) Ω i)‖ ^ 2 = 0 := by\n  1101\t    have := (Finset.sum_eq_zero_iff_of_nonneg (fun j _ => by positivity)).mp hsumR i\n  1102\t      (Finset.mem_univ i)\n  1103\t    exact this\n  1104\t  have : ‖T (tvec (⇑e) Ω i)‖ = 0 := by nlinarith [norm_nonneg (T (tvec (⇑e) Ω i))]\n  1105\t  exact norm_eq_zero.mp this\n  1106\t\n  1107\tend FinitePure\n  1108\t\n  1109\t\n  1110\t/-! ## 5. Transport of a normalized tracial state along a unitary\n  1111\t\n  1112\tConjugation by a unitary carries a normalized tracial state on a set of operators to a\n  1113\tnormalized tracial state on the image set.  Unconditional. -/\n  1114\t\n  1115\tsection Transport\n  1116\t\n  1117\tvariable {H H' : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℂ H] [CompleteSpace H]\n  1118\t  [NormedAddCommGroup H'] [InnerProductSpace ℂ H'] [CompleteSpace H']\n  1119\t\n  1120\t/-- The functional transported along conjugation by a unitary `U`. -/\n  1121\tnoncomputable def transportFunctional (U : H ≃ₗᵢ[ℂ] H') (phi : (H →L[ℂ] H) →ₗ[ℂ] ℂ) :\n  1122\t    (H' →L[ℂ] H') →ₗ[ℂ] ℂ where\n  1123\t  toFun T := phi (U.conjStarAlgEquiv.symm T)\n  1124\t  map_add' T S := by simp only [map_add]\n  1125\t  map_smul' c T := by simp only [map_smul, RingHom.id_apply]\n  1126\t\n  1127\t@[simp] theorem transportFunctional_apply (U : H ≃ₗᵢ[ℂ] H')\n  1128\t    (phi : (H →L[ℂ] H) →ₗ[ℂ] ℂ) (T : H' →L[ℂ] H') :\n  1129\t    transportFunctional U phi T = phi (U.conjStarAlgEquiv.symm T) := rfl\n  1130\t\n  1131\ttheorem IsFiniteVectorNormal.transport (U : H ≃ₗᵢ[ℂ] H')\n  1132\t    {phi : (H →L[ℂ] H) →ₗ[ℂ] ℂ} (h : IsFiniteVectorNormal phi) :\n  1133\t    IsFiniteVectorNormal (transportFunctional U phi) := by\n  1134\t  obtain ⟨n, w, hw⟩ := h\n  1135\t  refine ⟨n, fun i => U (w i), fun T => ?_⟩\n  1136\t  rw [transportFunctional_apply, hw]\n  1137\t  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ => ?_\n  1138\t  have hz : (U.conjStarAlgEquiv.symm T) (w i) = U.symm (T (U (w i))) := rfl\n  1139\t  rw [hz, ← U.inner_map_map (w i) (U.symm (T (U (w i)))), U.apply_symm_apply]\n  1140\t\n  1141\t/-- **Transport of the normalized tracial state.** -/\n  1142\ttheorem IsNormalizedTracialStateOn.transport (U : H ≃ₗᵢ[ℂ] H')\n  1143\t    {M : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)} {phi : (H →L[ℂ] H) →ₗ[ℂ] ℂ}\n  1144\t    (h : IsNormalizedTracialStateOn M phi) :\n  1145\t    IsNormalizedTracialStateOn (U.conjStarAlgEquiv '' M) (transportFunctional U phi) where\n  1146\t  normal := h.normal.transport U\n  1147\t  unital := by rw [transportFunctional_apply, map_one]; exact h.unital\n  1148\t  positive := by\n  1149\t    intro T\n  1150\t    obtain ⟨r, hr0, hr⟩ := h.positive (U.conjStarAlgEquiv.symm T)\n  1151\t    exact ⟨r, hr0, by rw [transportFunctional_apply, map_mul, map_star]; exact hr⟩\n  1152\t  tracial := by\n  1153\t    rintro _ ⟨X, hX, rfl⟩ _ ⟨Y, hY, rfl⟩\n  1154\t    simp only [transportFunctional_apply, ← map_mul, StarAlgEquiv.symm_apply_apply]\n  1155\t    exact h.tracial X hX Y hY\n  1156\t  faithful := by\n  1157\t    rintro _ ⟨X, hX, rfl⟩ h0\n  1158\t    have hstar : star (U.conjStarAlgEquiv X) = U.conjStarAlgEquiv (star X) :=\n  1159\t      (map_star U.conjStarAlgEquiv X).symm\n  1160\t    rw [transportFunctional_apply, hstar, ← map_mul, StarAlgEquiv.symm_apply_apply] at h0\n  1161\t    rw [h.faithful X hX h0, map_zero]\n  1162\t\n  1163\tend Transport\n  1164\t\n  1165\t\n  1166\t/-! ## 6. The finite-pure case: a normalized tracial state on the regional algebra\n  1167\t\n  1168\tAssembling Section 4 and Section 5.  The unconditional content is: normality (as a finite sum of\n  1169\tvector functionals), unitality, positivity, the elementary-product formula\n  1170\t`φ(A ⊗ B) = (dim K_pure)⁻¹ tr(A) ⟪Ω, B Ω⟫`, and traciality on elementary products.  Two analytic\n  1171\tinputs remain, and they are stated as explicit named premises (never as axioms):\n  1172\t\n  1173\t* `tracial`, that traciality — proved here on the elementary products generating the algebra —\n  1174\t  persists on the whole weak closure.  This is the exact analogue of P58's\n  1175\t  `MixedWeakClosurePremises.tracial`; deducing it from the generator case requires normality of\n  1176\t  `φ` in the σ-weak sense together with a Kaplansky density argument, neither of which is\n  1177\t  available in pinned Mathlib.\n  1178\t* `separating`, that the product vectors `eᵢ ⊗ Ω` are separating for the algebra; this is the\n  1179\t  standard consequence of `Ω` being separating for the mixed factor. -/\n  1180\t\n  1181\tsection FinitePureRegional\n  1182\t\n  1183\topen AristotleCandidates.ProductGNSTensor\n  1184\t\n  1185\tvariable (D : ProductGNSData.{u}) {ι : Type u} [Fintype ι] [Nonempty ι]\n  1186\t\n  1187\t/-- **The auxiliary premises for the finite-pure trace.**  See the section docstring. -/\n  1188\tstructure FinitePureTracePremises (e : OrthonormalBasis ι ℂ D.PureGNS) (Ω : D.MixedGNS) :\n  1189\t    Prop where\n  1190\t  /-- the mixed cyclic vector is a unit vector -/\n  1191\t  mixed_unit : ‖Ω‖ = 1\n  1192\t  /-- traciality persists from the elementary products to the whole spatial algebra -/\n  1193\t  tracial : ∀ X ∈ D.spatialTensorAlgebra, ∀ Y ∈ D.spatialTensorAlgebra,\n  1194\t    finitePureTrace e Ω (X * Y) = finitePureTrace e Ω (Y * X)\n  1195\t  /-- the product vectors are separating for the spatial algebra -/\n  1196\t  separating : ∀ T ∈ D.spatialTensorAlgebra, (∀ i, T (tvec (⇑e) Ω i) = 0) → T = 0\n  1197\t\n  1198\t/-- **Finite-pure case, spatial form.**  The normalized functional\n  1199\t`(dim K_pure)⁻¹ · tr ⊗ ⟪Ω, · Ω⟫` is a normal, unital, positive, tracial and faithful state on\n  1200\tthe spatial tensor product `B(K_pure) ⊗̄ R_mixed`. -/\n  1201\ttheorem spatialTensorAlgebra_isNormalizedTracialState\n  1202\t    (e : OrthonormalBasis ι ℂ D.PureGNS) (Ω : D.MixedGNS)\n  1203\t    (h : FinitePureTracePremises D e Ω) :\n  1204\t    IsNormalizedTracialStateOn D.spatialTensorAlgebra (finitePureTrace e Ω) where\n  1205\t  normal := finitePureTrace_isFiniteVectorNormal e Ω\n  1206\t  unital := finitePureTrace_one e h.mixed_unit\n  1207\t  positive := finitePureTrace_positive e Ω\n  1208\t  tracial := h.tracial\n  1209\t  faithful := fun X hX h0 => finitePureTrace_faithful e Ω h.separating X hX h0\n  1210\t\n  1211\t/-- **Finite-pure case, regional form.**  Transporting the previous theorem through the product\n  1212\tGNS unitary yields a normalized tracial state on the regional represented von Neumann algebra:\n  1213\tin the finite-pure case the local-hyperbolic algebra is a *finite* factor. -/\n  1214\ttheorem regionalAlgebra_isNormalizedTracialState\n  1215\t    (e : OrthonormalBasis ι ℂ D.PureGNS) (Ω : D.MixedGNS)\n  1216\t    (h : FinitePureTracePremises D e Ω) :\n  1217\t    IsNormalizedTracialStateOn (regionalAlgebra D)\n  1218\t      (transportFunctional D.productGNSUnitary (finitePureTrace e Ω)) := by\n  1219\t  have hmain := (spatialTensorAlgebra_isNormalizedTracialState D e Ω h).transport\n  1220\t    D.productGNSUnitary\n  1221\t  have himg : D.productGNSUnitary.conjStarAlgEquiv '' D.spatialTensorAlgebra\n  1222\t      = regionalAlgebra D := unitaryConj_image_spatial D\n  1223\t  rwa [himg] at hmain\n  1224\t\n  1225\tend FinitePureRegional\n  1226\t\n  1227\t\n  1228\t/-! ## 7. Weights defined by families of vectors\n  1229\t\n  1230\tFor the infinite-pure case the natural functional is an **unnormalizable weight**, taking values\n  1231\tin `ℝ≥0∞`.  We develop it for an arbitrary family of vectors: this is checked infrastructure,\n  1232\twith no premise. -/\n  1233\t\n  1234\tsection VectorWeight\n  1235\t\n  1236\tvariable {H H' : Type u}\n  1237\t  [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℂ H] [CompleteSpace H]\n  1238\t  [NormedAddCommGroup H'] [InnerProductSpace ℂ H'] [CompleteSpace H']\n  1239\t\n  1240\t/-- The `ℝ≥0∞`-valued weight `T ↦ ∑ⱼ ⟪vⱼ, T vⱼ⟫` attached to a family of vectors. -/\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"candidate='aristotle_responses/P59-local-hyperbolic-factor-trace-theorem-a12190c2-9efd5c22-quarantine/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p59-80nvzu02_aristotle/AristotleCandidates/LocalHyperbolicFactorTraceTheorem.lean'\nprintf '%s\\\\n' '--- infinite weight / terminal sections ---'\nnl -ba \\\"\"'$candidate\" | sed -n '\"'1230,1660p'\nprintf '%s\\\\n' '--- P58 terms actually used ---'\nrg -n 'MixedUHF|MixedWeak|mixedVonNeumann|Hyperfinite|qubit|IsHyperfinite|isMixed|Factor|FiniteFactor|HasTrivialOperatorCenter|uhf' \\\"\"'$candidate\" | sed -n '\"'1,420p'\nprintf '%s\\\\n' '--- P57 terms actually used ---'\nrg -n 'ProductGNS|ProductGNSData|spatialTensor|unitaryConj|pureFactorSet|mixedFactorSet|TensorGNS|TotalGNS|totalRep' \\\"\"'$candidate\" | sed -n '\"'1,500p'\"","aggregated_output":"--- infinite weight / terminal sections ---\n  1230\tFor the infinite-pure case the natural functional is an **unnormalizable weight**, taking values\n  1231\tin `ℝ≥0∞`.  We develop it for an arbitrary family of vectors: this is checked infrastructure,\n  1232\twith no premise. -/\n  1233\t\n  1234\tsection VectorWeight\n  1235\t\n  1236\tvariable {H H' : Type u}\n  1237\t  [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℂ H] [CompleteSpace H]\n  1238\t  [NormedAddCommGroup H'] [InnerProductSpace ℂ H'] [CompleteSpace H']\n  1239\t\n  1240\t/-- The `ℝ≥0∞`-valued weight `T ↦ ∑ⱼ ⟪vⱼ, T vⱼ⟫` attached to a family of vectors. -/\n  1241\tnoncomputable def vectorWeight {J : Type u} (v : J → H) (T : H →L[ℂ] H) : ENNReal :=\n  1242\t  ∑' j, ENNReal.ofReal ((⟪v j, T (v j)⟫_ℂ).re)\n  1243\t\n  1244\ttheorem re_inner_nonneg_of_isPositive {T : H →L[ℂ] H} (hT : T.IsPositive) (x : H) :\n  1245\t    0 ≤ (⟪x, T x⟫_ℂ).re := by\n  1246\t  have h := (ContinuousLinearMap.isPositive_iff' T).mp hT |>.2 x\n  1247\t  have hre : (0 : ℝ) ≤ (⟪T x, x⟫_ℂ).re := by\n  1248\t    simpa using (Complex.le_def.mp h).1\n  1249\t  have hconj : ⟪x, T x⟫_ℂ = (starRingEnd ℂ) ⟪T x, x⟫_ℂ := (inner_conj_symm _ _).symm\n  1250\t  rw [hconj, Complex.conj_re]\n  1251\t  exact hre\n  1252\t\n  1253\t/-- Additivity of the weight on positive operators. -/\n  1254\ttheorem vectorWeight_add {J : Type u} (v : J → H) {S T : H →L[ℂ] H}\n  1255\t    (hS : S.IsPositive) (hT : T.IsPositive) :\n  1256\t    vectorWeight v (S + T) = vectorWeight v S + vectorWeight v T := by\n  1257\t  unfold vectorWeight\n  1258\t  rw [← ENNReal.tsum_add]\n  1259\t  refine tsum_congr fun j => ?_\n  1260\t  rw [ContinuousLinearMap.add_apply, inner_add_right, Complex.add_re,\n  1261\t    ENNReal.ofReal_add (re_inner_nonneg_of_isPositive hS _) (re_inner_nonneg_of_isPositive hT _)]\n  1262\t\n  1263\tomit [CompleteSpace H] in\n  1264\t/-- Positive homogeneity of the weight. -/\n  1265\ttheorem vectorWeight_smul {J : Type u} (v : J → H) {c : ℝ} (hc : 0 ≤ c) (T : H →L[ℂ] H) :\n  1266\t    vectorWeight v ((c : ℂ) • T) = ENNReal.ofReal c * vectorWeight v T := by\n  1267\t  unfold vectorWeight\n  1268\t  rw [← ENNReal.tsum_mul_left]\n  1269\t  refine tsum_congr fun j => ?_\n  1270\t  rw [ContinuousLinearMap.smul_apply, inner_smul_right, Complex.mul_re, Complex.ofReal_re,\n  1271\t    Complex.ofReal_im, zero_mul, sub_zero, ENNReal.ofReal_mul hc]\n  1272\t\n  1273\t/-- The weight of `T* T` is the sum of the squared norms `‖T vⱼ‖²`. -/\n  1274\ttheorem vectorWeight_star_mul_self {J : Type u} (v : J → H) (T : H →L[ℂ] H) :\n  1275\t    vectorWeight v (star T * T) = ∑' j, ENNReal.ofReal (‖T (v j)‖ ^ 2) := by\n  1276\t  refine tsum_congr fun j => ?_\n  1277\t  congr 1\n  1278\t  rw [ContinuousLinearMap.mul_apply, ContinuousLinearMap.star_eq_adjoint,\n  1279\t    ContinuousLinearMap.adjoint_inner_right, inner_self_eq_norm_sq_to_K]\n  1280\t  norm_cast\n  1281\t\n  1282\t/-- If the weight of `T* T` vanishes then `T` kills every vector of the family. -/\n  1283\ttheorem vectorWeight_apply_eq_zero {J : Type u} (v : J → H) (T : H →L[ℂ] H)\n  1284\t    (h : vectorWeight v (star T * T) = 0) (j : J) : T (v j) = 0 := by\n  1285\t  rw [vectorWeight_star_mul_self] at h\n  1286\t  have hj : ENNReal.ofReal (‖T (v j)‖ ^ 2) = 0 := by\n  1287\t    have := ENNReal.tsum_eq_zero.mp h\n  1288\t    exact this j\n  1289\t  have h2 : ‖T (v j)‖ ^ 2 ≤ 0 := by\n  1290\t    simpa [ENNReal.ofReal_eq_zero] using hj\n  1291\t  have : ‖T (v j)‖ = 0 := by nlinarith [norm_nonneg (T (v j))]\n  1292\t  exact norm_eq_zero.mp this\n  1293\t\n  1294\tomit [CompleteSpace H] in\n  1295\t/-- The weight of the identity is the sum of the squared norms of the family. -/\n  1296\ttheorem vectorWeight_one {J : Type u} (v : J → H) :\n  1297\t    vectorWeight v 1 = ∑' j, ENNReal.ofReal (‖v j‖ ^ 2) := by\n  1298\t  refine tsum_congr fun j => ?_\n  1299\t  congr 1\n  1300\t  rw [ContinuousLinearMap.one_apply, inner_self_eq_norm_sq_to_K]\n  1301\t  norm_cast\n  1302\t\n  1303\tomit [CompleteSpace H] in\n  1304\t/-- **The infinite-pure weight is not a state**: for an infinite family of unit vectors the\n  1305\tweight of the identity is `∞`. -/\n  1306\ttheorem vectorWeight_one_eq_top {J : Type u} [Infinite J] (v : J → H)\n  1307\t    (hv : ∀ j, ‖v j‖ = 1) : vectorWeight v 1 = ⊤ := by\n  1308\t  rw [vectorWeight_one]\n  1309\t  have : ∀ j, ENNReal.ofReal (‖v j‖ ^ 2) = 1 := by\n  1310\t    intro j; rw [hv j]; norm_num\n  1311\t  rw [tsum_congr this]\n  1312\t  exact ENNReal.tsum_const_eq_top_of_ne_zero one_ne_zero\n  1313\t\n  1314\t/-- The weight transported along conjugation by a unitary. -/\n  1315\tnoncomputable def transportWeight (U : H ≃ₗᵢ[ℂ] H') (W : (H →L[ℂ] H) → ENNReal)\n  1316\t    (T : H' →L[ℂ] H') : ENNReal := W (U.conjStarAlgEquiv.symm T)\n  1317\t\n  1318\ttheorem transportWeight_vectorWeight {J : Type u} (U : H ≃ₗᵢ[ℂ] H') (v : J → H) :\n  1319\t    transportWeight U (vectorWeight v) = vectorWeight (fun j => U (v j)) := by\n  1320\t  funext T\n  1321\t  refine tsum_congr fun j => ?_\n  1322\t  congr 2\n  1323\t  have hz : (U.conjStarAlgEquiv.symm T) (v j) = U.symm (T (U (v j))) := rfl\n  1324\t  rw [hz, ← U.inner_map_map (v j) (U.symm (T (U (v j)))), U.apply_symm_apply]\n  1325\t\n  1326\tend VectorWeight\n  1327\t\n  1328\t\n  1329\t/-! ## 8. Faithful normal semifinite weights and their transport\n  1330\t\n  1331\t`IsFaithfulNormalSemifiniteWeightOn M W` is the project-local notion used in the infinite-pure\n  1332\tcase.  It is deliberately **not** a state: `W` takes values in `ℝ≥0∞`, is only additive and\n  1333\tpositively homogeneous on the positive cone, and its value on `1` is allowed to be `∞` (and in\n  1334\tthe intended infinite-pure model it *is* `∞`, see `vectorWeight_one_eq_top`). -/\n  1335\t\n  1336\tsection WeightStructure\n  1337\t\n  1338\tvariable {H H' : Type u}\n  1339\t  [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℂ H] [CompleteSpace H]\n  1340\t  [NormedAddCommGroup H'] [InnerProductSpace ℂ H'] [CompleteSpace H']\n  1341\t\n  1342\t/-- **Project-local definition (faithful normal semifinite trace-weight).** -/\n  1343\tstructure IsFaithfulNormalSemifiniteWeightOn (M : Set (H →L[ℂ] H))\n  1344\t    (W : (H →L[ℂ] H) → ENNReal) : Prop where\n  1345\t  /-- normality, in the concrete form: `W` is a (possibly infinite) sum of vector functionals -/\n  1346\t  normal : ∃ (J : Type u) (v : J → H), W = vectorWeight v\n  1347\t  /-- additivity on the positive cone -/\n  1348\t  additive : ∀ S T : H →L[ℂ] H, S.IsPositive → T.IsPositive → W (S + T) = W S + W T\n  1349\t  /-- positive homogeneity -/\n  1350\t  homogeneous : ∀ c : ℝ, 0 ≤ c → ∀ T : H →L[ℂ] H, W ((c : ℂ) • T) = ENNReal.ofReal c * W T\n  1351\t  /-- faithfulness on `M` -/\n  1352\t  faithful : ∀ T ∈ M, W (star T * T) = 0 → T = 0\n  1353\t  /-- semifiniteness: every nonzero positive element of `M` dominates a nonzero positive element\n  1354\t  of `M` of finite weight -/\n  1355\t  semifinite : ∀ T ∈ M, T.IsPositive → T ≠ 0 →\n  1356\t    ∃ S ∈ M, S.IsPositive ∧ S ≠ 0 ∧ S ≤ T ∧ W S ≠ ⊤\n  1357\t  /-- traciality on `M` -/\n  1358\t  tracial : ∀ T ∈ M, W (star T * T) = W (T * star T)\n  1359\t\n  1360\ttheorem isPositive_conjStarAlgEquiv_symm (U : H ≃ₗᵢ[ℂ] H') {T : H' →L[ℂ] H'}\n  1361\t    (hT : T.IsPositive) : (U.conjStarAlgEquiv.symm T).IsPositive := by\n  1362\t  rw [ContinuousLinearMap.isPositive_iff'] at hT ⊢\n  1363\t  refine ⟨?_, fun x => ?_⟩\n  1364\t  · have hstar : star (U.conjStarAlgEquiv.symm T) = U.conjStarAlgEquiv.symm (star T) :=\n  1365\t      (map_star U.conjStarAlgEquiv.symm T).symm\n  1366\t    show star (U.conjStarAlgEquiv.symm T) = _\n  1367\t    rw [hstar, hT.1]\n  1368\t  · have hx : (U.conjStarAlgEquiv.symm T) x = U.symm (T (U x)) := rfl\n  1369\t    rw [hx, ← U.inner_map_map (U.symm (T (U x))) x, U.apply_symm_apply]\n  1370\t    exact hT.2 (U x)\n  1371\t\n  1372\ttheorem isPositive_conjStarAlgEquiv (U : H ≃ₗᵢ[ℂ] H') {T : H →L[ℂ] H}\n  1373\t    (hT : T.IsPositive) : (U.conjStarAlgEquiv T).IsPositive :=\n  1374\t  isPositive_conjStarAlgEquiv_symm U.symm hT\n  1375\t\n  1376\ttheorem le_conjStarAlgEquiv (U : H ≃ₗᵢ[ℂ] H') {S T : H →L[ℂ] H} (h : S ≤ T) :\n  1377\t    U.conjStarAlgEquiv S ≤ U.conjStarAlgEquiv T := by\n  1378\t  rw [← sub_nonneg] at h ⊢\n  1379\t  rw [← map_sub, ContinuousLinearMap.nonneg_iff_isPositive]\n  1380\t  exact isPositive_conjStarAlgEquiv U (ContinuousLinearMap.nonneg_iff_isPositive _ |>.mp h)\n  1381\t\n  1382\ttheorem le_conjStarAlgEquiv_symm (U : H ≃ₗᵢ[ℂ] H') {S T : H' →L[ℂ] H'} (h : S ≤ T) :\n  1383\t    U.conjStarAlgEquiv.symm S ≤ U.conjStarAlgEquiv.symm T :=\n  1384\t  le_conjStarAlgEquiv U.symm h\n  1385\t\n  1386\t/-- **Transport of a faithful normal semifinite weight along a unitary.** -/\n  1387\ttheorem IsFaithfulNormalSemifiniteWeightOn.transport (U : H ≃ₗᵢ[ℂ] H')\n  1388\t    {M : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)} {W : (H →L[ℂ] H) → ENNReal}\n  1389\t    (h : IsFaithfulNormalSemifiniteWeightOn M W) :\n  1390\t    IsFaithfulNormalSemifiniteWeightOn (U.conjStarAlgEquiv '' M) (transportWeight U W) where\n  1391\t  normal := by\n  1392\t    obtain ⟨J, v, rfl⟩ := h.normal\n  1393\t    exact ⟨J, fun j => U (v j), transportWeight_vectorWeight U v⟩\n  1394\t  additive := by\n  1395\t    intro S T hS hT\n  1396\t    show W (U.conjStarAlgEquiv.symm (S + T)) = W _ + W _\n  1397\t    rw [map_add]\n  1398\t    exact h.additive _ _ (isPositive_conjStarAlgEquiv_symm U hS)\n  1399\t      (isPositive_conjStarAlgEquiv_symm U hT)\n  1400\t  homogeneous := by\n  1401\t    intro c hc T\n  1402\t    show W (U.conjStarAlgEquiv.symm ((c : ℂ) • T)) = _\n  1403\t    rw [map_smul]\n  1404\t    exact h.homogeneous c hc _\n  1405\t  faithful := by\n  1406\t    rintro _ ⟨X, hX, rfl⟩ h0\n  1407\t    have hstar : star (U.conjStarAlgEquiv X) = U.conjStarAlgEquiv (star X) :=\n  1408\t      (map_star U.conjStarAlgEquiv X).symm\n  1409\t    have h1 : W (star X * X) = 0 := by\n  1410\t      have : transportWeight U W (star (U.conjStarAlgEquiv X) * U.conjStarAlgEquiv X)\n  1411\t          = W (star X * X) := by\n  1412\t        show W (U.conjStarAlgEquiv.symm _) = _\n  1413\t        rw [hstar, ← map_mul, StarAlgEquiv.symm_apply_apply]\n  1414\t      rw [← this]; exact h0\n  1415\t    rw [h.faithful X hX h1, map_zero]\n  1416\t  semifinite := by\n  1417\t    rintro _ ⟨X, hX, rfl⟩ hpos hne\n  1418\t    have hXpos : X.IsPositive := by\n  1419\t      have := isPositive_conjStarAlgEquiv_symm U hpos\n  1420\t      rwa [StarAlgEquiv.symm_apply_apply] at this\n  1421\t    have hXne : X ≠ 0 := fun h => hne (by rw [h, map_zero])\n  1422\t    obtain ⟨S, hSM, hSpos, hSne, hSle, hSfin⟩ := h.semifinite X hX hXpos hXne\n  1423\t    refine ⟨U.conjStarAlgEquiv S, ⟨S, hSM, rfl⟩, isPositive_conjStarAlgEquiv U hSpos,\n  1424\t      fun hz => hSne ?_, le_conjStarAlgEquiv U hSle, ?_⟩\n  1425\t    · have := congrArg U.conjStarAlgEquiv.symm hz\n  1426\t      rwa [StarAlgEquiv.symm_apply_apply, map_zero] at this\n  1427\t    · show W (U.conjStarAlgEquiv.symm (U.conjStarAlgEquiv S)) ≠ ⊤\n  1428\t      rwa [StarAlgEquiv.symm_apply_apply]\n  1429\t  tracial := by\n  1430\t    rintro _ ⟨X, hX, rfl⟩\n  1431\t    have hstar : star (U.conjStarAlgEquiv X) = U.conjStarAlgEquiv (star X) :=\n  1432\t      (map_star U.conjStarAlgEquiv X).symm\n  1433\t    show W (U.conjStarAlgEquiv.symm _) = W (U.conjStarAlgEquiv.symm _)\n  1434\t    rw [hstar, ← map_mul, ← map_mul, StarAlgEquiv.symm_apply_apply,\n  1435\t      StarAlgEquiv.symm_apply_apply]\n  1436\t    exact h.tracial X hX\n  1437\t\n  1438\tend WeightStructure\n  1439\t\n  1440\t\n  1441\t/-! ## 9. The infinite-pure case: a faithful normal semifinite weight\n  1442\t\n  1443\tWhen the pure sector is infinite-dimensional the type I factor `B(K_pure)` is infinite and no\n  1444\ttracial *state* exists.  The canonical operator trace of `B(K_pure)`, tensored with the mixed\n  1445\tvector trace, is the `ℝ≥0∞`-valued weight `vectorWeight (tvec e Ω)`.  It is **not** a state:\n  1446\t`W 1 = ∞` (`regionalAlgebra_weight_one_eq_top`).\n  1447\t\n  1448\tUnconditional here: normality, additivity on the positive cone, positive homogeneity, the value\n  1449\t`∞` on the identity, faithfulness from a separating family, and the transport to the regional\n  1450\talgebra.  Two analytic inputs are named premises: semifiniteness and traciality of the weight on\n  1451\tthe whole weak closure. -/\n  1452\t\n  1453\tsection InfinitePureWeight\n  1454\t\n  1455\tvariable {K₁ K₂ : Type u}\n  1456\t  [NormedAddCommGroup K₁] [InnerProductSpace ℂ K₁] [CompleteSpace K₁]\n  1457\t  [NormedAddCommGroup K₂] [InnerProductSpace ℂ K₂] [CompleteSpace K₂]\n  1458\t  {ι : Type u}\n  1459\t\n  1460\tomit [CompleteSpace K₁] [CompleteSpace K₂] in\n  1461\ttheorem norm_tvec (v : ι → K₁) (Ω : K₂) (i : ι) : ‖tvec v Ω i‖ = ‖v i‖ * ‖Ω‖ := by\n  1462\t  rw [tvec, Completion.norm_coe, TensorProduct.norm_tmul]\n  1463\t\n  1464\t/-- **The infinite-pure weight**: the canonical operator trace of `B(K_pure)` tensored with the\n  1465\tmixed vector state, realized as the vector weight of the product vectors `eᵢ ⊗ Ω`. -/\n  1466\tnoncomputable def infinitePureWeight (v : ι → K₁) (Ω : K₂) :\n  1467\t    (Completion (K₁ ⊗[ℂ] K₂) →L[ℂ] Completion (K₁ ⊗[ℂ] K₂)) → ENNReal :=\n  1468\t  vectorWeight (tvec v Ω)\n  1469\t\n  1470\tomit [CompleteSpace K₁] [CompleteSpace K₂] in\n  1471\ttheorem infinitePureWeight_one_eq_top [Infinite ι] (e : HilbertBasis ι ℂ K₁) {Ω : K₂}\n  1472\t    (hΩ : ‖Ω‖ = 1) : infinitePureWeight (⇑e) Ω 1 = ⊤ :=\n  1473\t  vectorWeight_one_eq_top _ fun i => by\n  1474\t    rw [norm_tvec, hΩ, mul_one, e.orthonormal.1 i]\n  1475\t\n  1476\tend InfinitePureWeight\n  1477\t\n  1478\tsection InfinitePureRegional\n  1479\t\n  1480\topen AristotleCandidates.ProductGNSTensor\n  1481\t\n  1482\tvariable (D : ProductGNSData.{u}) {ι : Type u}\n  1483\t\n  1484\t/-- **The auxiliary premises for the infinite-pure weight.**  Semifiniteness and traciality on\n  1485\tthe weak closure are the two analytic inputs; they are stated as explicit named premises, never\n  1486\tas axioms. -/\n  1487\tstructure InfinitePureWeightPremises (e : HilbertBasis ι ℂ D.PureGNS) (Ω : D.MixedGNS) :\n  1488\t    Prop where\n  1489\t  /-- the mixed cyclic vector is a unit vector -/\n  1490\t  mixed_unit : ‖Ω‖ = 1\n  1491\t  /-- the product vectors are separating for the spatial algebra -/\n  1492\t  separating : ∀ T ∈ D.spatialTensorAlgebra, (∀ i, T (tvec (⇑e) Ω i) = 0) → T = 0\n  1493\t  /-- semifiniteness of the weight on the spatial algebra -/\n  1494\t  semifinite : ∀ T ∈ D.spatialTensorAlgebra, T.IsPositive → T ≠ 0 →\n  1495\t    ∃ S ∈ D.spatialTensorAlgebra, S.IsPositive ∧ S ≠ 0 ∧ S ≤ T ∧\n  1496\t      infinitePureWeight (⇑e) Ω S ≠ ⊤\n  1497\t  /-- traciality of the weight on the spatial algebra -/\n  1498\t  tracial : ∀ T ∈ D.spatialTensorAlgebra,\n  1499\t    infinitePureWeight (⇑e) Ω (star T * T) = infinitePureWeight (⇑e) Ω (T * star T)\n  1500\t\n  1501\t/-- **Infinite-pure case, spatial form.**  The weight `tr ⊗ ⟪Ω, · Ω⟫` is a faithful normal\n  1502\tsemifinite trace-weight on `B(K_pure) ⊗̄ R_mixed`. -/\n  1503\ttheorem spatialTensorAlgebra_isFaithfulNormalSemifiniteWeight\n  1504\t    (e : HilbertBasis ι ℂ D.PureGNS) (Ω : D.MixedGNS)\n  1505\t    (h : InfinitePureWeightPremises D e Ω) :\n  1506\t    IsFaithfulNormalSemifiniteWeightOn D.spatialTensorAlgebra\n  1507\t      (infinitePureWeight (⇑e) Ω) where\n  1508\t  normal := ⟨ι, tvec (⇑e) Ω, rfl⟩\n  1509\t  additive := fun _ _ hS hT => vectorWeight_add _ hS hT\n  1510\t  homogeneous := fun _ hc T => vectorWeight_smul _ hc T\n  1511\t  faithful := fun T hT h0 =>\n  1512\t    h.separating T hT fun i => vectorWeight_apply_eq_zero _ T h0 i\n  1513\t  semifinite := h.semifinite\n  1514\t  tracial := h.tracial\n  1515\t\n  1516\t/-- **Infinite-pure case, regional form.**  Transport through the product GNS unitary: the\n  1517\tregional represented von Neumann algebra carries a faithful normal semifinite trace-weight. -/\n  1518\ttheorem regionalAlgebra_isFaithfulNormalSemifiniteWeight\n  1519\t    (e : HilbertBasis ι ℂ D.PureGNS) (Ω : D.MixedGNS)\n  1520\t    (h : InfinitePureWeightPremises D e Ω) :\n  1521\t    IsFaithfulNormalSemifiniteWeightOn (regionalAlgebra D)\n  1522\t      (transportWeight D.productGNSUnitary (infinitePureWeight (⇑e) Ω)) := by\n  1523\t  have hmain := (spatialTensorAlgebra_isFaithfulNormalSemifiniteWeight D e Ω h).transport\n  1524\t    D.productGNSUnitary\n  1525\t  have himg : D.productGNSUnitary.conjStarAlgEquiv '' D.spatialTensorAlgebra\n  1526\t      = regionalAlgebra D := unitaryConj_image_spatial D\n  1527\t  rwa [himg] at hmain\n  1528\t\n  1529\t/-- **The infinite-pure weight is not a state.**  Its value on the identity operator is `∞`,\n  1530\tboth spatially and after transport to the regional algebra. -/\n  1531\ttheorem regionalAlgebra_weight_one_eq_top [Infinite ι]\n  1532\t    (e : HilbertBasis ι ℂ D.PureGNS) (Ω : D.MixedGNS)\n  1533\t    (hΩ : ‖Ω‖ = 1) :\n  1534\t    transportWeight D.productGNSUnitary (infinitePureWeight (⇑e) Ω) 1 = ⊤ := by\n  1535\t  show infinitePureWeight (⇑e) Ω (D.productGNSUnitary.conjStarAlgEquiv.symm 1) = ⊤\n  1536\t  rw [map_one]\n  1537\t  exact infinitePureWeight_one_eq_top e hΩ\n  1538\t\n  1539\tend InfinitePureRegional\n  1540\t\n  1541\t\n  1542\t/-! ## 10. The bundled spatial `⋆`-isomorphism\n  1543\t\n  1544\tSection 3 identified the regional algebra with the spatial tensor product as *sets* of operators.\n  1545\tHere the identification is packaged as a `⋆`-algebra isomorphism of `⋆`-subalgebras\n  1546\t\n  1547\t`B(K_pure) ⊗̄ R_mixed  ≃⋆ₐ[ℂ]  π_ω̃(A_Γ)''`,\n  1548\t\n  1549\timplemented by conjugation with the product GNS unitary.  Unconditional. -/\n  1550\t\n  1551\tsection SpatialIso\n  1552\t\n  1553\topen AristotleCandidates.ProductGNSTensor\n  1554\t\n  1555\tvariable (D : ProductGNSData.{u})\n  1556\t\n  1557\ttheorem star_generatorSet_subset :\n  1558\t    star (D.pureFactorSet ∪ D.mixedFactorSet) ⊆ D.pureFactorSet ∪ D.mixedFactorSet := by\n  1559\t  intro T hT\n  1560\t  have hT' : star T ∈ D.pureFactorSet ∪ D.mixedFactorSet := hT\n  1561\t  rcases hT' with h | h\n  1562\t  · rw [pureFactorSet_eq] at h\n  1563\t    obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := h\n  1564\t    refine Or.inl ?_\n  1565\t    rw [pureFactorSet_eq]\n  1566\t    refine ⟨star a, ?_⟩\n  1567\t    have hstar : pureAmp D (star a) = star (pureAmp D a) := by\n  1568\t      rw [pureAmp, pureAmp, map_star, ← lamp_star]\n  1569\t    rw [hstar, ha]\n  1570\t    exact star_star T\n  1571\t  · rw [mixedFactorSet_eq] at h\n  1572\t    obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ := h\n  1573\t    refine Or.inr ?_\n  1574\t    rw [mixedFactorSet_eq]\n  1575\t    refine ⟨star b, ?_⟩\n  1576\t    have hstar : mixedAmp D (star b) = star (mixedAmp D b) := by\n  1577\t      rw [mixedAmp, mixedAmp, map_star, ← ramp_star]\n  1578\t    rw [hstar, hb]\n  1579\t    exact star_star T\n  1580\t\n  1581\ttheorem star_range_totalRep_subset :\n  1582\t    star (Set.range D.totalRep) ⊆ Set.range D.totalRep := by\n  1583\t  intro T hT\n  1584\t  obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ : ∃ a, D.totalRep a = star T := hT\n  1585\t  exact ⟨star a, by rw [map_star, ha, star_star]⟩\n  1586\t\n  1587\t/-- The spatial tensor product `B(K_pure) ⊗̄ R_mixed`, packaged as a `⋆`-subalgebra. -/\n  1588\tnoncomputable def spatialSubalgebra : StarSubalgebra ℂ (D.TensorGNS →L[ℂ] D.TensorGNS) :=\n  1589\t  StarSubalgebra.centralizer ℂ\n  1590\t    ((StarSubalgebra.centralizer ℂ (D.pureFactorSet ∪ D.mixedFactorSet) :\n  1591\t      StarSubalgebra ℂ (D.TensorGNS →L[ℂ] D.TensorGNS)) : Set (D.TensorGNS →L[ℂ] D.TensorGNS))\n  1592\t\n  1593\t/-- The regional represented von Neumann algebra, packaged as a `⋆`-subalgebra. -/\n  1594\tnoncomputable def regionalSubalgebra : StarSubalgebra ℂ (D.TotalGNS →L[ℂ] D.TotalGNS) :=\n  1595\t  StarSubalgebra.centralizer ℂ\n  1596\t    ((StarSubalgebra.centralizer ℂ (Set.range D.totalRep) :\n  1597\t      StarSubalgebra ℂ (D.TotalGNS →L[ℂ] D.TotalGNS)) : Set (D.TotalGNS →L[ℂ] D.TotalGNS))\n  1598\t\n  1599\t@[simp] theorem coe_spatialSubalgebra :\n  1600\t    (spatialSubalgebra D : Set (D.TensorGNS →L[ℂ] D.TensorGNS)) = D.spatialTensorAlgebra := by\n  1601\t  rw [spatialSubalgebra, StarSubalgebra.coe_centralizer_centralizer,\n  1602\t    Set.union_eq_self_of_subset_right (star_generatorSet_subset D)]\n  1603\t  rfl\n  1604\t\n  1605\t@[simp] theorem coe_regionalSubalgebra :\n  1606\t    (regionalSubalgebra D : Set (D.TotalGNS →L[ℂ] D.TotalGNS)) = regionalAlgebra D := by\n  1607\t  rw [regionalSubalgebra, StarSubalgebra.coe_centralizer_centralizer,\n  1608\t    Set.union_eq_self_of_subset_right (star_range_totalRep_subset D)]\n  1609\t  rfl\n  1610\t\n  1611\ttheorem mem_spatialSubalgebra_iff (T : D.TensorGNS →L[ℂ] D.TensorGNS) :\n  1612\t    T ∈ spatialSubalgebra D ↔ D.unitaryConj T ∈ regionalSubalgebra D := by\n  1613\t  have himg : D.unitaryConj '' D.spatialTensorAlgebra = regionalAlgebra D :=\n  1614\t    unitaryConj_image_spatial D\n  1615\t  constructor\n  1616\t  · intro hT\n  1617\t    have h1 : T ∈ D.spatialTensorAlgebra := by rwa [← SetLike.mem_coe, coe_spatialSubalgebra] at hT\n  