∧\n825-    (∀ x ∈ (M : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)), phi (star x * x) = 0 → x = 0)\n826-  /-- an increasing chain of finite matrix subalgebras with dense union in a\n827-  C*-subalgebra generating `M` -/\n828-  hyperfinite : ∃ S : StarSubalgebra ℂ (H →L[ℂ] H),\n829-    Nonempty (IsMatricialChain S) ∧ StarSubalgebra.vonNeumannGenerated S = M\n830-  /-- matrix subalgebras of unbounded size sit inside `M`: `M` is not of finite\n831-  type I -/\n832-  infinite : ∀ N : ℕ, ∃ (k : ℕ) (S : StarSubalgebra ℂ (H →L[ℂ] H)),\n833-    N ≤ k ∧ (S : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)) ⊆ (M : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)) ∧\n834-      Nonempty ((S) ≃⋆ₐ[ℂ] Matrix (Fin k) (Fin k) ℂ)\n835-\n836-/-- **Conditional classification of the infinite mixed subsystem.**  Under the\n837-three explicitly named premises, the weak closure of the infinite mixed\n838-subsystem is a factor with a normal faithful tracial state, hyperfinite in the\n839-matricial-chain sense, and contains matrix subalgebras of unbounded size. -/\n840:theorem mixedVonNeumann_isHyperfiniteFiniteFactor (h : MixedWeakClosurePremises) :\n841-    IsHyperfiniteFiniteFactorModel mixedVonNeumann where\n842-  factor := h.factor\n843-  finite_trace :=\n844-    ⟨uhfVectorState, uhfVectorState_isVectorNormal, uhfVectorState_one,\n845-      uhfVectorState_positive, h.tracial, h.faithful⟩\n846-  hyperfinite := ⟨UHFConcreteCStar, ⟨uhfConcreteCStar_isMatricialChain⟩, rfl⟩\n847-  infinite N := by\n848-    refine ⟨2 ^ N, mixedStage N, Nat.le_of_lt Nat.lt_two_pow_self,\n849-      mixedStage_le_mixedVonNeumann N, ⟨mixedStage_matrixEquiv N⟩⟩\n850-\n851-end WeakClosure\n852-\n853-end StabilizerHyperfinite\n--- P57 spatial data declaration ---\n51-* `prodElt`, `prodElt_mul`, `prodElt_star_mul`, `totalState_prodElt_inner`, `preInner_prodElt`,\n52-  `norm_prodElt` — the algebra of elementary product elements and the factorization of the GNS\n53-  inner product on them.\n54-* `prodCLM`, `inner_prodCLM` — the bilinear product map `K_pure × K_mixed → H_ω̃`, with the\n55-  exact inner-product factorization `⟪x ⊗ y, x' ⊗ y'⟫ = ⟪x, x'⟫ ⟪y, y'⟫`.\n56-* `tensorLiftₗ`, `norm_tensorLiftₗ`, `tensorLiftIsometry`, `tensorUnitaryCLM` — the induced\n57-  isometry of the algebraic tensor product `TensorPre = K_pure ⊗[ℂ] K_mixed` and of its\n58-  completion `TensorGNS`.\n59-* `totalCoe`, `denseRange_tensorUnitaryCLM`, `surjective_tensorUnitaryCLM`.\n60-* `tensorMapₗ`, `norm_tensorMapₗ_le`, `tensorOp`, `tensorOpC` — the elementary tensor operators\n61-  `π₁(a) ⊗ π₂(b)`; their boundedness is *derived* from the intertwining identity and the\n62-  isometry property, since pinned Mathlib has no general bound `‖T ⊗ S‖ ≤ ‖T‖ ‖S‖` on an\n63-  algebraic tensor product of inner-product spaces.\n64-\n65-**(2) Theorems recovered in the manuscript's intended form (for `ProductGNSData`).**\n66-\n67:* `productGNSUnitary : TensorGNS ≃ₗᵢ[ℂ] TotalGNS` — the canonical GNS unitary\n68-  `K_pure ⊗ K_mixed ≅ H_ω̃`; this is the manuscript's `H_ω̃ = K ⊗ K'`.\n69-* `prodCLM_intertwine_coe` (intertwining on the dense subspace of classes of algebra elements,\n70-  i.e. on finite words) and `prodCLM_intertwine`, `tensorUnitaryCLM_tensorOpC` (intertwining\n71-  everywhere, by continuity).\n72-* `unitaryConj_tensorOpC` — conjugation by the unitary maps `π₁(a) ⊗ π₂(b)` to\n73-  `π_ω̃(ι₁ a · ι₂ b)`.\n74-* `centralizer_representedProductSet` — the elementary product operators and the whole\n75-  represented algebra have the same commutant.\n76-* `bicommutant_elementary_eq_spatial` — the bicommutant of the elementary tensor operators equals\n77-  `spatialTensorAlgebra`, the spatial von Neumann tensor product of the two represented factor\n78-  algebras, defined as usual as `({π₁(a) ⊗ 1} ∪ {1 ⊗ π₂(b)})''`.\n79:* `unitaryConj_image_spatialTensorAlgebra` — the manuscript's algebra identification:\n80-  `U (M_pure ⊗̄ M_mixed) U⋆ = π_ω̃(Total)''`.\n81-\n82-* `idPositive`, `trivialProductGNSData` and the resulting `Nonempty ProductGNSData` instance — a\n83-  non-vacuity witness showing that the fields of `