{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_42","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"printf '%s\\\\n' '--- P59 plan and packet exact lines ---'; nl -ba PLAN.md | sed -n '62,130p'; nl -ba aristotle_tasks/P59-local-hyperbolic-factor-trace-theorem.md | sed -n '1,220p'; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- predecessor decision lines ---'; nl -ba reviews/P57-product-gns-tensor-factorization-closeout.md | sed -n '102,182p'; nl -ba reviews/P58-mixed-uhf-hyperfinite-factor-closeout.md | sed -n '49,130p'; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- task log ---'; nl -ba history/logs/20260810T132354Z-a12190c2-tasks.log | sed -n '1,80p'\"","aggregated_output":"--- P59 plan and packet exact lines ---\n    62\t| P49C | `KaplanskyDensity.lean` | Prove bounded/unit-ball Kaplansky density for the represented C-star algebra in its bicommutant and derive the compressed-corner approximation used by the manuscript. No supplied density interface is accepted. |\n    63\t| P50 | `NormalFaithfulCornerTrace.lean` | Using P49 and P49C, prove traciality of `tau_q` on `q M_Gamma q` by bounded strong approximation, prove faithfulness, and establish the stronger concrete WOT-continuity certificate that P50U will translate into the standard ultraweak-normal interface. |\n    64\t| P50U | `UltraweakNormality.lean` | Define the concrete ultraweak topology from absolutely summable matrix-coefficient series, prove the ultraweak-to-WOT identity is continuous, and upgrade P50's WOT-continuity certificate to literal ultraweak normality. This is mandatory infrastructure and may not alias ultraweak topology to WOT/SOT/norm. |\n    65\t| P51 | `FullFiniteCornerCentralExclusion.lean` | Prove `q` finite, prove fullness, and derive `0 != z ->` a nonzero finite projection in `z M_Gamma`; define/use the project-local type-III obstruction. |\n    66\t\n    67\t### Explicit local-hyperbolic lane\n    68\t\n    69\t| Packet | Lean target | Purpose and acceptance gate |\n    70\t|---|---|---|\n    71\t| P52 | `CoherentLocalHyperbolicCoordinates.lean` | Build finite coordinate blocks and an exhaustion from local hyperbolic data. Audit whether finite support suffices; otherwise isolate the exact local-finiteness/coherence assumption. |\n    72\t| P53 | `LocalHyperbolicAlgebraicAlpha.lean` | Construct the finite stage maps, phase calibration, and coherent algebraic `alpha`; instantiate the existing direct-limit theorems without supplied stage equivalences. |\n    73\t| P54 | `UHFReferenceRepresentation.lean` | Construct a faithful compatible Hilbert/operator representation of the dyadic algebra from finite stages; do not assume an infinite tensor-product Hilbert space. |\n    74\t| P55A | `LocalHyperbolicFiniteStageUHFBridge.lean` | Construct, rather than assume, the finite-stage star equivalence from each P53 coordinate Pauli algebra to the corresponding finite dyadic matrix algebra, with explicit generator/phase formulas and norm control. |\n    75\t| P55B | `LocalHyperbolicSourceUHFBridge.lean` | Prove coherence of the P55A maps and identify the P53 source direct limit with the coordinate dyadic limit; prove the finite terminal-stage and infinite cofinal-UHF branches separately. |\n    76\t| P55C | `LocalHyperbolicConcreteRepresentations.lean` | Transport the P54 faithful representation through P55B and P53 alpha, and construct the source and regional closed operator-range C-star algebras with faithful dense embeddings. |\n    77\t| P55D | `RegionalConcreteCStarAlpha.lean` | Extend the P53 algebraic alpha uniquely between the P55C concrete C-star closures and prove the inverse and dense-range identities. |\n    78\t| P56 | `RegionalProductStateIdentity.lean` | Retired partial result: it proves the finite-word/algebraic state equality and conditional continuous-extension uniqueness, but does not prove C-star boundedness or positivity. |\n    79\t| P56R | `RegionalProductStateIdentity.lean` | Recovery after P55D: construct the pure/mixed product C-star state from finite-dimensional density-matrix estimates, prove positivity/unitality and transport it through `alpha`; no supplied norm bound. |\n    80\t| P57A | `VacuumRestrictedInfiniteTensorProduct.lean` | Shared infrastructure: port and audit the proved finite-support vacuum-restricted infinite-tensor pre-Hilbert core from `bound_beating`; do not import external projects or package a completion as an axiom. |\n    81\t| P57 | `ProductGNSTensorFactorization.lean` | After P54, P56R, and P57A, construct the pure/mixed product GNS Hilbert-space tensor splitting and the spatial represented-algebra identification. |\n    82\t| P58 | `MixedUHFHyperfiniteFactor.lean` | Construct/prove the finite mixed matrix and infinite mixed hyperfinite-II1 alternatives under project-local factor and normal-trace definitions. |\n    83\t| P59 | `LocalHyperbolicFactorTraceTheorem.lean` | Transport P57--P58 to the regional algebra, prove trivial center, and state the finite-pure trace versus infinite-pure faithful-normal-semifinite-weight dichotomy. |\n    84\t\n    85\t### Optional strengthening/reconnection\n    86\t\n    87\t| Packet | Lean target | Purpose |\n    88\t|---|---|---|\n    89\t| P60 | `FullCornerSemifiniteWeight.lean` | Retired partial attempt: it constructs a conditional extended-positive trace series and finite-compression certificate, but does not yet prove standard positive-cone semifiniteness. |\n    90\t| P60R | `FullCornerSemifiniteWeight.lean` | Recovery: define the weight on the positive cone and prove standard semifiniteness using positive square roots and the finite comparison projections. |\n    91\t| P61 | `HyperbolicImpliesCentralCriterion.lean` | Show the explicit Lane-H model supplies the finite-corner criterion used by Lane G. |\n    92\t\n    93\t## Initial parallel wave\n    94\t\n    95\tSubmit only the four independent foundation packets first: P47, P48, P52,\n    96\tand P54. Integrate and semantically audit them before submitting dependent\n    97\tpackets. Existing P42--P46 task drafts are preserved as historical drafts;\n    98\tthey are not evidence and must be re-scoped against this plan before reuse.\n    99\t\n   100\t## Non-negotiable gates\n   101\t\n   102\t1. No claim that `q M_Gamma q` has merely a semifinite weight when the\n   103\t   construction actually targets a finite faithful normal tracial state.\n   104\t2. No claim of a global trace/weight on `M_Gamma` from the finite-corner\n   105\t   theorem alone.\n   106\t3. No claim that a finite-dimensional subalgebra excludes type III; the proof\n   107\t   must produce a nonzero finite projection in every nonzero central summand.\n   108\t4. No claim that hyperbolic data imply a factor before the spatial tensor\n   109\t   factorization and factorhood of both factors are proved.\n   110\t5. Every manuscript-facing packet identifies an exact `main.tex` locator and\n   111\t   every extra analytic hypothesis appears as a named field, never an axiom.\n   112\t6. P49A--P49C are mandatory proved infrastructure. P50 may not replace the\n   113\t   bicommutant theorem or Kaplansky density by a supplied structure field; an\n   114\t   incomplete analytic package halts Lane G and triggers review.\n   115\t7. P50's WOT-continuity theorem is a mathematically stronger certificate but\n   116\t   is not itself the standard definition of normality. P50U must formalize the\n   117\t   actual ultraweak topology and checked comparison before the project reports\n   118\t   the corner state as ultraweak-normal in the formal interface. P51's\n   119\t   finiteness/fullness proof is logically independent because it uses only\n   120\t   traciality and faithfulness.\n   121\t8. The original P55 exhausted its remote budget without producing its\n   122\t   authorized Lean file. It is retired, not accepted. P55A--P55D replace it\n   123\t   and expose the previously missing bridge between P53's twisted-Pauli direct\n   124\t   limit and P54's dyadic UHF model. P56 may advance only after P55D is\n   125\t   integrated and audited.\n   126\t9. P56 is preserved as a partial artifact, not accepted evidence: its\n   127\t   `ProductStateBound` is an explicit missing C-star norm estimate and it has\n   128\t   no positivity theorem. P56R must derive the bound and positivity from the\n   129\t   finite-dimensional density-matrix data and P55D's concrete C-star model;\n   130\t   it may not use `ProductStateBound` in its final declarations or proofs.\n     1\t# P59 — local-hyperbolic factor and trace theorem\n     2\t\n     3\t## Context declaration\n     4\t\n     5\t- **Source basis:** `main.tex:1671-1679, 1970-2004`.\n     6\t\n     7\t## Plan alignment\n     8\t\n     9\t- **Package and lane:** `P59`; Lane `H`.\n    10\t- **Predecessors:** `P57`, `P58`, both integrated and locally audited before submission.\n    11\t- **Gate discharged:** transport the spatial product model to the regional\n    12\t  algebra, prove trivial center, and prove the finite/infinite pure trace dichotomy.\n    13\t- **Forbidden downstream claims:** no general-lattice central decomposition, no\n    14\t  assertion that Lane H proves Lane G, and no global tracial **state** in the\n    15\t  infinite-pure case.\n    16\t\n    17\t## Mathematical target\n    18\t\n    19\tCreate only `AristotleCandidates/LocalHyperbolicFactorTraceTheorem.lean`. Prove\n    20\tthe regional represented von Neumann algebra is spatially star-isomorphic to\n    21\t`B(K_pure) barTensor R_mixed` using the integrated P57--P58 declarations. Prove\n    22\tboth factors and their spatial tensor product have trivial center, then transport\n    23\tfactorhood. In the finite-pure case construct the normalized tracial state. In\n    24\tthe infinite-pure case construct or explicitly assume and transport a faithful\n    25\tnormal semifinite trace/weight; never call it a state.\n    26\t\n    27\t## Auxiliary assumptions\n    28\t\n    29\tList every spatial tensor-product, factor-center, normal transport, canonical\n    30\toperator trace, and semifinite-weight premise not constructed by predecessors.\n    31\t\n    32\t## Files and imports\n    33\t\n    34\tCreate only `AristotleCandidates/LocalHyperbolicFactorTraceTheorem.lean`; import\n    35\tP57 and P58.\n    36\t\n    37\t## Acceptance criteria\n    38\t\n    39\t`lake build AristotleCandidates.LocalHyperbolicFactorTraceTheorem` succeeds\n    40\twithout forbidden declarations. Report separately the spatial isomorphism,\n    41\tfactor conclusion, finite tracial state, and infinite semifinite weight.\n--- predecessor decision lines ---\n   102\t## Acceptance classification\n   103\t\n   104\t| Classification | Result |\n   105\t| --- | --- |\n   106\t| proved | The conditional product-data theorem constructs the GNS tensor-product unitary, proves the finite-word and continuous intertwining identities, and identifies the represented total bicommutant with the concrete bicommutant-defined spatial algebra. |\n   107\t| partial | The result remains generic over `ProductGNSData`; it does not itself instantiate that bundle from the manuscript's regional algebra and P55D/P56R data. Standard spatial von Neumann tensor-product theory and all later factor/type/trace conclusions remain open. |\n   108\t| blocked | Nothing blocks the packet's permitted strongest-local-form gate. The stronger standard spatial-von-Neumann API is unavailable in pinned Mathlib and is explicitly recorded rather than assumed. |\n   109\t| failed | None. No compilation, placeholder, archive-integrity, or scope failure was found. |\n   110\t\n   111\tThe packet's mathematical target is therefore met at its stated conditional\n   112\tscope.  It is not a proof of the complete manuscript claim\n   113\t`\\pi_{\\widetilde\\omega}(\\mathcal P_I)''=\\mathcal B(\\mathcal K)\\bar\\otimes\\mathcal R`:\n   114\tthe classification of the two factors and the source-specific regional\n   115\tidentification are downstream work.\n   116\t\n   117\t## Changed proof route\n   118\t\n   119\tThe candidate takes a constructive route through the algebraic tensor product\n   120\t`PureGNS ⊗[ℂ] MixedGNS`, then completes the norm-preserving tensor lift.  It\n   121\tderives boundedness of elementary tensor operators from the proved\n   122\tintertwining identity and the isometry, rather than assuming a general\n   123\toperator-tensor norm inequality unavailable in the pinned API.  It defines the\n   124\tstrongest available concrete spatial object as a bicommutant of the two\n   125\tcommuting factor families.  These are alternative proof choices within the\n   126\tpacket's scope, not silent weakenings; every added premise is a named field of\n   127\t`ProductGNSData` above.\n   128\t\n   129\t## Plan alignment\n   130\t\n   131\t- **Package and lane:** `P57`; Lane `H`, correct.\n   132\t- **Integrated predecessors:** `P54`, `P56R`, and `P57A`, each locally\n   133\t  integrated, compiled, and accepted in its closeout review.  The preserved\n   134\t  partial `P56` artifact is not used as a predecessor.  The additional GNS and\n   135\t  bicommutant imports are already-built local infrastructure.\n   136\t- **Permitted gate:** construct the pure/mixed product GNS Hilbert-space split,\n   137\t  prove the dense/continuous intertwining identity, and identify the generated\n   138\t  represented algebra with the strongest concrete spatial tensor object\n   139\t  supported by pinned Mathlib.  This gate is discharged conditionally on the\n   140\t  explicitly declared `ProductGNSData` fields.\n   141\t- **Forbidden downstream claims:** respected.  The candidate does not claim\n   142\t  mixed-factor classification, factorhood of either factor, regional\n   143\t  factorhood, `\\mathcal B(\\mathcal K)` identification, hyperfiniteness, or any\n   144\t  trace/weight dichotomy.\n   145\t\n   146\t## Verification\n   147\t\n   148\t- `lake build AristotleCandidates.ProductGNSTensorFactorization` — passed\n   149\t  (`8072/8072` jobs).\n   150\t- `lake build Aris